(window.LINGUA_BOOK=window.LINGUA_BOOK||{}).condense=Object.assign(window.LINGUA_BOOK.condense||{},{"part-005-chapter-5-morphology":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 5: Morphology","zh":"第 5 章：形态学"},"summary":{"en":"This chapter turns to words and to the meaningful pieces that combine to create them. Languages differ in how they build words, yet structure can be found inside words in every language. The linguistic study of word forms is called morphology. The chapter sets out four learning goals covering morphemes, inflection, derivation, compounding, lexical categories, and the analysis of complex words.","zh":"本章考察词以及构成词的有意义单位。各语言的构词方式不同，但在任何语言中都能发现词的内部结构。语言学中研究词形的分支称为形态学。本章提出的四项学习目标涉及语素、屈折、派生、复合、词类以及复杂词的分析，为后续各节奠定基础。"},"points":[{"en":"Languages vary in how they build words, but structure can be found inside words in all languages.","zh":"各语言构词方式不同，但在所有语言中都能在词的内部发现结构。"},{"en":"Morphology is the linguistic study of word forms.","zh":"形态学是语言学中研究词形的分支。"},{"en":"Readers should identify morphologically complex words and the morphemes within them.","zh":"读者应能识别形态复杂的词及其内部的语素。"},{"en":"Readers should distinguish inflectional morphology, derivational morphology, and compounds.","zh":"读者应能区分屈折形态、派生形态与复合词。"},{"en":"Readers should explain how morphology interacts with lexical category and analyse complex word structure.","zh":"读者应能解释形态与词类的互动，并分析复杂词的结构。"}],"terms":[{"en":"morphology","zh":"形态学","defEn":"The branch of linguistics that studies how words are formed and structured.","defZh":"语言学中研究词的构成与内部结构的分支。"},{"en":"morpheme","zh":"语素","defEn":"A minimal meaningful piece that combines with others to build words.","defZh":"构成词的最小意义单位，可与其他单位组合成词。"},{"en":"morphologically complex word","zh":"形态复杂的词","defEn":"A word that contains more than one morpheme inside it.","defZh":"内部包含一个以上语素的词。"},{"en":"inflectional morphology","zh":"屈折形态","defEn":"Morphology that adds grammatical information without creating a new word.","defZh":"只增添语法信息、不构成新词的形态变化。"},{"en":"derivational morphology","zh":"派生形态","defEn":"Morphology that builds new words, often changing the lexical category.","defZh":"构成新词的形态过程，常改变词的词类。"},{"en":"compounding","zh":"复合","defEn":"Word formation that joins two or more existing words into one.","defZh":"把两个或更多已有的词组合成一个新词的构词方式。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"This chapter turns to words and to the meaningful pieces that combine to create them. Languages vary widely in how they build words, but separate pieces and internal structure can be found inside words in every language. In linguistics, the study of word forms is known as morphology.","zh":"本章转向词以及构成词的有意义单位。各语言的构词方式差异很大，但在任何语言中都能在词的内部找到可分离的单位与结构。语言学中研究词形的分支称为形态学。"},{"en":"The chapter has four learning goals. Readers should be able to identify morphologically complex words and the morphemes within them; distinguish inflectional morphology, derivational morphology, and compounds; explain how a word's morphology interacts with its lexical category; and analyse the structure of complex words.","zh":"本章有四项目标：识别形态复杂的词及其中的语素；区分屈折形态、派生形态与复合词；解释词的形态与其词类如何互动；分析复杂词的结构。"}]},"chapter-040-slug-5-1-what-is-morphology":{"title":{"en":"5.1 What is morphology?","zh":"5.1 什么是形态学？"},"summary":{"en":"Morphology is the linguistic study of how words are put together out of smaller meaningful pieces. English words usually contain one or two such pieces, while other languages build much longer words, such as Inuktitut iglujjualiulauqtuq. Because writing with spaces is not a reliable guide, a word is defined as the smallest separable unit in language, and its internal pieces are called morphemes.","zh":"形态学研究词语如何由更小的有意义单位组合而成。英语单词通常只含一两个这样的单位，而其他语言能构成长得多的词，如 Inuktitut 语的 iglujjualiulauqtuq。由于以空格书写的正字法并不可靠，词被定义为语言中最小的可分离单位，词内的更小单位称为语素。"},"points":[{"en":"Morphology investigates how words are put together from smaller meaningful pieces.","zh":"形态学研究词语如何由更小的有意义单位组合而成。"},{"en":"A word is the smallest separable unit in language, a definition that does not rely on writing.","zh":"词是语言中最小的可分离单位，该定义不依赖书写。"},{"en":"Morphemes are the smallest systematic pairings of form with meaning or grammatical function.","zh":"语素是形式与意义或语法功能的最小的系统性配对。"},{"en":"Words containing more than one morpheme are morphologically complex; single-morpheme words are simple.","zh":"含一个以上语素的词是形态复杂的，只含一个语素的词是形态简单的。"},{"en":"Whether a word is complex depends on speakers' grammar, not on its etymology.","zh":"一个词是否形态复杂取决于使用者的语法，而不取决于词源。"}],"terms":[{"en":"morphology","zh":"形态学","defEn":"The study of how words are put together from smaller pieces.","defZh":"研究词语如何由更小单位组合而成的学科。"},{"en":"morpheme","zh":"语素","defEn":"The smallest systematic pairing of form with meaning or grammatical function.","defZh":"形式与意义或语法功能的最小系统性配对单位。"},{"en":"morphologically complex","zh":"形态复杂","defEn":"Describing a word that contains more than one morpheme.","defZh":"指一个词内部包含一个以上的语素。"},{"en":"morphologically simple","zh":"形态简单","defEn":"Describing a word that consists of only a single morpheme.","defZh":"指一个词只由一个语素构成。"},{"en":"orthographic","zh":"正字法的","defEn":"Relating to spelling or to a language's standard written conventions.","defZh":"与拼写或语言的标准书写规范有关的。"},{"en":"etymology","zh":"词源","defEn":"The history of a word and its earlier forms.","defZh":"指一个词的历史来源及其早期的形式。"}],"examples":[{"text":"cats","noteEn":"Built from two pieces: cat, the animal, and -s, meaning more than one.","noteZh":"由两个单位构成：cat 指这种动物，-s 表示不止一个。"},{"text":"non-renewability","noteEn":"A technical word containing at least five pieces: non-, re-, new, -abil, -ity.","noteZh":"一个技术性词，至少包含五个单位：non-、re-、new、-abil、-ity。"},{"text":"iglujjualiulauqtuq","noteEn":"An Inuktitut word of five pieces, translated as They (sg) made a big house.","noteZh":"Inuktitut 语中由五个单位构成的词，可译为 They (sg) made a big house。"},{"text":"scat","noteEn":"A word of English, but it does not mean more than one cat.","noteZh":"它是英语中的一个词，但意思并不是“不止一只猫”。"}],"body":[{"en":"Morphology is the branch of linguistics that studies how words are assembled from smaller meaningful pieces. English words typically contain only one or two such pieces, as in cats, made of cat plus -s; technical vocabulary can stack several, as in non-renewability, which has at least five. Some languages build far longer words, so that a single word expresses what English needs a whole sentence for.","zh":"形态学是语言学中研究词语如何由更小的有意义单位组合而成的分支。英语单词通常只含一两个这样的单位，如 cats 由 cat 加 -s 构成；专业词汇可以叠加多个单位，如 non-renewability 至少包含五个。有些语言能造出长得多的词，一个词就表达英语需用整句表达的意义。"},{"en":"In the Harvaqtuurmiutut variety of Inuktitut, iglujjualiulauqtuq consists of five pieces and is translated as They (sg) made a big house. The pieces are iglu house, -jjua big, -liu make, -lauq distant past, and -tuq declarative. Combinations are not free, however: reversing cat and -s does not give the meaning more than one cat, since scat is an entirely different word.","zh":"在 Inuktitut 的 Harvaqtuurmiutut 变体中，iglujjualiulauqtuq 由五个单位组成，可译为 They (sg) made a big house，五个单位分别是 iglu（house）、-jjua（big）、-liu（make）、-lauq（distant past）和 -tuq（declarative）。但组合并非任意：把 cat 与 -s 颠倒过来并不表示“不止一只猫”，scat 是一个完全不同的词。"},{"en":"Since spelling with spaces on either side is not a reliable guide, linguists define a word as the smallest separable unit in language, the smallest unit that can stand alone in an utterance and that is syntactically independent. Content words such as nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs can serve as one-word answers, as in cake, sleep, orange, and slowly.","zh":"由于左右以空格分隔的拼写方式并不可靠，语言学家把词定义为语言中最小的可分离单位，即能独立出现在话语中、且在句法上独立的单位。名词、动词、形容词、副词等实词可以单独充当答语，如 cake、sleep、orange、slowly。"},{"en":"Words are not the smallest units of language overall. The internal pieces that cannot stand on their own are morphemes, the smallest systematic pairing of form with meaning or grammatical function. Words with more than one morpheme are morphologically complex, while words with a single morpheme are morphologically simple. Whether a word counts as complex is a question about current speakers' grammar rather than etymology; historically, morphology itself comes from Greek morph- shape and -ology study of.","zh":"词并不是语言中最小的单位。词内不能独立存在的更小单位是语素，即形式与意义或语法功能的最小的系统性配对。含一个以上语素的词是形态复杂的词，只含一个语素的词是形态简单的词。一个词是否算形态复杂，取决于当代使用者心智中的语法，而非词源；从历史上看，morphology 由希腊语的 morph-（shape）与 -ology（study of）构成。"}]},"chapter-041-slug-5-2-types-of-morphology-affixes-and-beyond":{"title":{"en":"5.2 Roots, bases, and affixes","zh":"5.2 词根、词基与词缀"},"summary":{"en":"Morphemes fall into different types. Affixes cannot stand alone and must attach to a base, which may be simple or complex; a simple base is a root. Affixes are classified by position as prefixes, suffixes, circumfixes, infixes, and simultaneous affixes. The section also separates free from bound morphemes, since affixes are bound and only roots can be free.","zh":"语素可分为不同类型。词缀不能独立存在，必须依附于词基，而词基可以简单也可以复杂；简单的词基就是词根。词缀按位置分为前缀、后缀、环缀、中缀和同时词缀。本节还区分自由语素与黏着语素：词缀都是黏着的，只有词根才可能自由。"},"points":[{"en":"Affixes cannot stand on their own and must attach to a base, which may be simple or complex.","zh":"词缀不能独立存在，必须依附于词基，词基可简单也可复杂。"},{"en":"A root is the smallest possible base, the indivisible core of a word.","zh":"词根是最小的词基，是词不可再分的核心。"},{"en":"Prefixes and suffixes are very common; circumfixes, infixes, and simultaneous affixes are less common.","zh":"前缀和后缀十分常见，环缀、中缀和同时词缀则较少见。"},{"en":"A suffix that happens to fall mid-word, such as -y in unluckiness, is still not an infix.","zh":"恰好出现在词中间的 -y（如 unluckiness）仍然不是中缀。"},{"en":"Simultaneous affixes are common in signed languages and in languages with tone.","zh":"同时词缀在手语以及有声调的语言中很常见。"},{"en":"Since affixes must attach, only roots can be free; English has bound roots like -whelmed.","zh":"由于词缀必须依附，只有词根才可能自由；英语有 -whelmed 这样的黏着词根。"}],"terms":[{"en":"affix","zh":"词缀","defEn":"A morpheme that cannot stand alone and must attach to a base.","defZh":"不能独立存在、必须依附于词基的语素。"},{"en":"base","zh":"词基","defEn":"The element that an affix attaches to; it may be simple or complex.","defZh":"词缀所依附的成分，其本身可简单也可复杂。"},{"en":"root","zh":"词根","defEn":"The smallest possible base, which cannot be divided any further.","defZh":"最小的词基，不能再作进一步切分。"},{"en":"circumfix","zh":"环缀","defEn":"An affix that attaches around its base, partly before and partly after it.","defZh":"环绕词基附着的词缀，一部分在前、一部分在后。"},{"en":"infix","zh":"中缀","defEn":"An affix that attaches inside another morpheme, not merely inside a word.","defZh":"附着于另一个语素内部的词缀，而不只是位于词中间。"},{"en":"bound morpheme","zh":"黏着语素","defEn":"A morpheme that can occur only when accompanied by other morphemes.","defZh":"只能与其他语素共同出现的语素。"}],"examples":[{"text":"librarian","noteEn":"Formed by attaching the affix -ian to the base library; it can take -ship in librarianship.","noteZh":"由词缀 -ian 加到词基 library 上构成，还可再加 -ship 构成 librarianship。"},{"text":"ne-ta·nes-ena·n-aki","noteEn":"Meskwaki for our daughters, marked by the circumfix ne- ... -ena·n plus -aki.","noteZh":"Meskwaki 语中表示 our daughters，由环缀 ne- … -ena·n 再加 -aki 标记。"},{"text":"[tumakbuh]","noteEn":"Tagalog ran, formed from [takbuh] run with the infix -um- after the first consonant.","noteZh":"Tagalog 语的 ran，由 [takbuh]（run）在第一个辅音后插入中缀 -um- 构成。"},{"text":"récord / recórd","noteEn":"An English noun-verb pair sharing a root but differing in the position of stress.","noteZh":"一对同根的名词与动词，区别在于重音的位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"Affixes cannot stand alone and must attach to a base, which may be simple or complex: attaching -ian to library gives librarian, which can itself serve as the base for -ship in librarianship. A simple base is a root, the smallest possible, indivisible core of a word, such as cat, library, or nation. Though library and nation go back to Latin complex words (libr- book, nat- be born), most English speakers today probably treat them as simple roots.","zh":"词缀不能独立存在，必须依附于词基，而词基可以简单也可以复杂：把 -ian 加到 library 上得到 librarian，它又可作为 -ship 的词基构成 librarianship。简单的词基称为词根，即词的最小的、不可再分的核心，如 cat、library、nation。尽管 library 和 nation 可追溯到拉丁语的复杂词（libr- 意为 book，nat- 意为 be born），今天多数英语使用者大概仍视其为简单词根。"},{"en":"Affixes are named for where they attach: a prefix precedes its base, as inter- does in international; a suffix follows it, as -s does in cats; a circumfix attaches around it; an infix inside it; and a simultaneous affix at the same time as it. Prefixes and suffixes are very common, the others rarer. Meskwaki marks plural possessors with a circumfix: ne-ta·nes-aki my daughters uses only a prefix, while ne-ta·nes-ena·n-aki our daughters combines ne- with -ena·n. In Tagalog the infix -um- attaches inside a verb base after its first consonant.","zh":"词缀按附着位置命名：前缀在词基之前（如 international 中的 inter-），后缀在其后（如 cats 中的 -s），环缀环绕词基，中缀位于词基内部，同时词缀则与词基同时发生。Meskwaki 语用环缀标记复数领属者：ne-ta·nes-aki（my daughters）只用前缀，ne-ta·nes-ena·n-aki（our daughters）则由 ne- 与 -ena·n 共同构成。Tagalog 语的中缀 -um- 插在动词词基第一个辅音之后。"},{"en":"Simultaneous affixes are common in signed languages and in languages with tone. In ASL a morpheme adding circular motion to a verb's base sign expresses continuative aspect, occurring simultaneously with the verb. Some spoken languages have tonal morphemes, where tone alone carries grammatical information. English is not tonal, but pairs such as récord and recórd, pérmit and permíts, and áddress and addréssed share a root and differ in stress.","zh":"同时词缀在手语和有声调的语言中很常见。ASL 中有一个为动词词基添加圆周运动的语素，表示持续体，该运动与动词同时发生。有些口语语言拥有声调语素，仅靠声调变化表达语法信息。英语不是声调语言，但 récord 与 recórd、pérmit 与 permíts、áddress 与 addréssed 这类词对同根而重音位置不同。"},{"en":"Morphemes are also free or bound. A free morpheme occurs as a word on its own, such as cat; a bound morpheme occurs only with other morphemes. Since affixes must attach to a base, only roots can be free. English has a few bound roots, such as -whelmed in overwhelmed and underwhelmed, which cannot occur as whelmed. In French and the other Romance languages most verb roots are bound. Bound morphemes are written with hyphens on the attaching side.","zh":"语素还分为自由语素与黏着语素：自由语素能独立成词，如 cat；黏着语素只能与其他语素共同出现。由于词缀必须依附词基，只有词根才可能自由。英语有少数黏着词根，如 overwhelmed 和 underwhelmed 中的 -whelmed，它不能单独出现为 whelmed。在法语等罗曼语中，多数动词词根都是黏着的。黏着语素用连字符标在其附着的一侧。"}]},"chapter-042-slug-5-4-morphology-beyond-affixes":{"title":{"en":"5.3 Morphology beyond affixes","zh":"5.3 词缀之外的形态学"},"summary":{"en":"Not all morphology is affixation. This section examines internal change, suppletion, and reduplication, showing that some morphological patterns replace or repeat material rather than adding affixes. It then classifies languages typologically as isolating or analytic, synthetic, agglutinative, and fusional, with examples from English, Halq’eméylem, Japanese, and Spanish.","zh":"并非所有形态手段都是加词缀。本节讨论内部变化、异干互补和重叠，说明有些形态模式是替换或重复词内成分，而不是添加词缀。随后按形态类型把语言分为孤立语（分析语）、综合语、黏着语和屈折语，并以英语、哈勒克梅莱姆语（Halq’eméylem）、日语和西班牙语为例。"},"points":[{"en":"Internal change alters material inside a word, as in irregular plurals mouse ~ mice and past tenses sit ~ sat.","zh":"内部变化指改变词内成分，如不规则复数 mouse ~ mice、过去式 sit ~ sat。"},{"en":"Suppletion replaces an entire morpheme, as when the past tense of go is went, and is always irregular and memorized.","zh":"异干互补指整个语素被替换，如 go 的过去式是 went；它永远不规则，只能记忆。"},{"en":"Reduplication repeats part or all of a word; in Halq’eméylem it can turn a verb into a dispositional adjective.","zh":"重叠是重复词的一部分或全部；在哈勒克梅莱姆语中，动词重叠后可构成表示倾向的形容词。"},{"en":"Isolating or analytic languages use few affixes and express inflection with particles, as Mandarin and Cantonese largely do.","zh":"孤立语（分析语）很少使用词缀，屈折信息多由虚词表达，汉语的普通话和粤语即高度孤立。"},{"en":"Synthetic languages split into agglutinative types with separable affixes and fusional types combining several meanings in one affix.","zh":"综合语分为黏着语与屈折语：前者由可分离的词缀构成，后者把多种意义合并于同一词缀。"}],"terms":[{"en":"internal change","zh":"内部变化","defEn":"A morphological pattern that changes a sound inside a word rather than adding an affix.","defZh":"在词内部改变某个音以构成新形式的形态手段，属于非词缀形态。"},{"en":"suppletion","zh":"异干互补","defEn":"A morphological pattern in which one form of a morpheme is replaced entirely by another.","defZh":"以一个完全不同的形式替换某语素原有形式的形态手段，其结果无法预测，只能逐个记忆。"},{"en":"reduplication","zh":"重叠","defEn":"A morphological pattern that repeats part or all of a word.","defZh":"通过重复词的一部分或全部来构成新形式的形态手段，可表达多种意义和语法功能。"},{"en":"isolating (analytic) language","zh":"孤立语（分析语）","defEn":"A language whose words are morphologically simple, with inflection carried by particles.","defZh":"词形结构简单的语言，屈折信息通常由虚词（小词）而非词缀表达，但仍有大量复合词。"},{"en":"agglutinative language","zh":"黏着语","defEn":"A synthetic language type whose words are built from many easily separated affixes with consistent meanings.","defZh":"综合语的一种，词由许多易于切分、各承载固定意义的词缀串联而成，如日语。"},{"en":"fusional language","zh":"屈折语","defEn":"A synthetic language type that combines several inflectional meanings into a single affix.","defZh":"综合语的一种，把多个屈折意义合并到同一个词缀中，难以再切分，如罗曼语族语言。"}],"examples":[{"text":"kw’élh ‘to capsize’ [kʼʷə́ɬ] → [kʼʷə́ɬkʼʷəɬ] ‘likely to capsize’","noteEn":"Halq’eméylem reduplication of a verb yields an adjective describing a disposition to act.","noteZh":"哈勒克梅莱姆语中动词重叠后构成形容词，表示容易或倾向于做该动作。"},{"text":"qwà:l ‘to speak’ [qʷél] → [qʷélqʷel] ‘talkative’","noteEn":"The same reduplication pattern produces the adjective meaning talkative in Halq’eméylem.","noteZh":"同一重叠模式在哈勒克梅莱姆语中构成意为健谈的形容词。"},{"text":"Tuna salad is a salad, but it’s not a salad-salad.","noteEn":"English salad-salad reduplication marks a prototypical example of a category.","noteZh":"英语的 salad-salad 重叠用来标记某范畴的典型实例，意为地道的沙拉。"},{"text":"Watasi-wa natto-o tabe-sase-rare-ta","noteEn":"Japanese stacks separable suffixes for causative and passive before the past tense.","noteZh":"日语动词后依次连接使役、被动和过去时后缀，每个后缀承载一项固定意义。"}],"body":[{"en":"Most morphology in English is affixation, but some patterns do not involve affixes at all. Internal change covers cases such as the irregular noun plurals mouse ~ mice and goose ~ geese, or the verb past tenses sit ~ sat and write ~ wrote. These forms were once regular and phonologically predictable, but for present-day speakers they have to be memorized, which makes them irregular. Suppletion is even less predictable: a whole morpheme is replaced, as when the past tense of go is went, or in good ~ better ~ best and bad ~ worse ~ worst. Suppletion is always irregular and is a type of allomorphy.","zh":"英语形态学大多依靠加词缀，但有些模式完全不涉及词缀。内部变化指词内语音的改变，如不规则名词复数 mouse ~ mice、goose ~ geese，动词过去式 sit ~ sat、write ~ wrote。这些形式在历史上曾经规则且可由音系预测，但对今天的说话者只能逐个记忆，因而是不规则的。异干互补更不可预测，它用一个完全不同的形式替换整个语素，如 go 的过去式为 went，又如 good ~ better ~ best、bad ~ worse ~ worst。异干互补永远不规则，是语素变体现象的一种。"},{"en":"Reduplication repeats part or all of a word as part of a morphological pattern. In Halq’eméylem, a Salish language of British Columbia, one pattern of verb reduplication produces an adjective meaning that someone or something is likely or disposed to do the action, as when kw’élh ‘to capsize’ becomes [kʼʷə́ɬkʼʷəɬ] ‘likely to capsize’ and qwà:l ‘to speak’ becomes [qʷélqʷel] ‘talkative’. Salish languages have many such patterns with different meanings and functions. English has one reduplication pattern, sometimes called salad-salad reduplication, which marks a prototypical instance of a type and can apply to phrases as well as words.","zh":"重叠是重复词的一部分或全部以构成形态模式。在不列颠哥伦比亚省的萨利什语族语言哈勒克梅莱姆语中，动词的一种重叠模式构成形容词，表示某人或某物容易或倾向于做该动作：kw’élh 意为翻覆，重叠后为 [kʼʷə́ɬkʼʷəɬ]，意为容易翻覆；qwà:l 意为说话，重叠后为 [qʷélqʷel]，意为健谈。萨利什语族有多种重叠模式，各与不同的意义和语法功能相联系。英语也有一种重叠模式，语言学家常称为 salad-salad 重叠，表示某事物是某类型的典型实例，它既可以作用于词，也可以作用于短语。"},{"en":"Languages can also be classified typologically by their morphological structure. Isolating or analytic languages have morphologically simple words; no language is perfectly isolating, but Mandarin and Cantonese come close, since inflectional information is typically carried by particles rather than affixes, though these languages still have many compounds. English is analytic but less isolating than Mandarin or Cantonese. Synthetic languages show heavy morphological complexity within words and often have few or no free roots, and they divide into agglutinative and fusional types. Agglutinative languages such as Japanese string together easily separated affixes, each with one consistent piece of meaning, while fusional languages such as the Romance languages combine several inflectional meanings in a single affix.","zh":"语言还可以按其形态结构作类型学分类。孤立语（分析语）的词在形态上很简单；没有一种人类语言是纯粹孤立的，但汉语的普通话和粤语接近这一类型，因为其屈折信息通常由虚词而非词缀表达，不过这些语言仍有大量复合词。英语比普通话、粤语少一些孤立性，但仍高度分析化。综合语的词内形态高度复杂，往往没有或极少自由词根，又分为黏着语和屈折语两类。日语等黏着语的词由许多容易切分的词缀串联而成，每个词缀对应一项固定意义；而罗曼语族语言等屈折语则把多项屈折意义合并到同一个词缀之中。"}]},"chapter-043-allomorphy":{"title":{"en":"5.4 Allomorphy","zh":"5.4 语素变体"},"summary":{"en":"Morphemes sometimes keep a consistent meaning while appearing in different forms according to their environment. This section distinguishes phonologically conditioned allomorphy, as with the English indefinite article a ~ an and the plural sounds [s], [z], and [ɪz], from lexically conditioned allomorphy, as with -(r)en, internal change, and the zero affix.","zh":"语素的意义固定，却可能随所处环境而以不同形式出现。本节区分语音条件制约的语素变体与词汇条件制约的语素变体：前者如英语不定冠词 a ~ an 以及复数读音 [s]、[z]、[ɪz]，后者如 -(r)en、内部变化和零词缀。"},"points":[{"en":"Allomorphy occurs when one morpheme has several forms whose choice depends on the surrounding environment.","zh":"语素变体指同一语素具有多种形式，选用哪一种取决于它所处的环境。"},{"en":"Phonologically conditioned allomorphy is predictable from sounds: the article is a before consonants and an before vowels.","zh":"语音条件制约的语素变体可由语音预测：不定冠词在辅音前为 a，在元音前为 an。"},{"en":"The English plural is pronounced [s], [z], or [ɪz] depending on the final sound of the noun root.","zh":"英语复数依名词词根末尾音的不同读作 [s]、[z] 或 [ɪz]，属可预测的语音条件制约。"},{"en":"Lexically conditioned allomorphy is unpredictable and must be listed, as with children, oxen, mice, fish, sheep, and deer.","zh":"词汇条件制约的语素变体不可预测，必须逐个列出，如 children、oxen、mice、fish、sheep、deer。"},{"en":"A zero affix, written ∅, marks a morpheme with no overt form, as in plural fish, sheep, and deer.","zh":"零词缀写作 ∅，表示语素没有显性形式，如复数 fish、sheep、deer。"}],"terms":[{"en":"allomorphy","zh":"语素变体（现象）","defEn":"The phenomenon in which one morpheme appears in different forms depending on its environment.","defZh":"同一语素因所处环境不同而呈现不同形式的现象，其各种形式称为语素变体。"},{"en":"allomorph","zh":"语素变体","defEn":"One of the alternative forms in which a single morpheme can be realized.","defZh":"同一语素在具体环境中实现出来的不同形式，如复数语素的 -s、-z、-ɪz 等。"},{"en":"phonologically conditioned allomorphy","zh":"语音条件制约的语素变体","defEn":"Allomorphy whose choice of form is predictable from the sounds in the environment.","defZh":"由语素前后语音环境决定的语素变体，其形式可以预测，如 a ~ an 和复数读音。"},{"en":"lexically conditioned allomorphy","zh":"词汇条件制约的语素变体","defEn":"Allomorphy determined by the particular root, which must therefore be memorized.","defZh":"由特定词根决定的语素变体，无法预测，只能作为词表逐项记忆。"},{"en":"zero affix","zh":"零词缀","defEn":"An affix with no overt form, indicated by the symbol ∅, as in plural sheep.","defZh":"没有显性语音形式的词缀，用数学空集符号 ∅ 表示，如复数 sheep。"}],"examples":[{"text":"a book, an apple","noteEn":"The English indefinite article has two allomorphs conditioned by the following sound.","noteZh":"英语不定冠词有两个语素变体，其选择由后接音是辅音还是元音决定。"},{"text":"[s]: books, cats, naps","noteEn":"This allomorph of the plural appears after the final sounds of these noun roots.","noteZh":"复数的这一变体出现在这些名词词根末尾音之后，读作 [s]。"},{"text":"[z]: papers, dogs, miles","noteEn":"A second predictable allomorph of the English plural is the sound [z].","noteZh":"英语复数的第二个可预测变体读作 [z]，出现在另一类词根末尾音之后。"},{"text":"children, oxen; mice, geese, women; fish, sheep, deer","noteEn":"These plurals are lexically conditioned allomorphs: the form must be memorized for each root.","noteZh":"这些复数属词汇条件制约的语素变体，其形式必须随词根逐个记忆。"}],"body":[{"en":"A morpheme may keep a consistent meaning while appearing in different forms according to the environment in which it occurs; this is allomorphy. The English indefinite article illustrates the point: it shows up as a before a consonant, as in a book, but as an before a vowel, as in an apple. Because the choice depends on the sounds that surround the morpheme, this is phonologically conditioned allomorphy.","zh":"同一语素可以意义固定，却因所处环境不同而呈现不同形式，这就是语素变体现象。英语不定冠词可以说明这一点：它在辅音前写作并读作 a，如 a book；在元音前则为 an，如 an apple。由于形式的选择取决于语素前后的语音环境，而非词的拼写，这属于语音条件制约的语素变体。"},{"en":"The English plural shows the same kind of predictability. Although it is spelled s or es, it is pronounced [s] after the final sounds of book, cat, and nap, [z] after those of paper, dog, and mile, and [ɪz] or [əz] after those of niece, horse, and eyelash. A generalization about the last sound of the noun root determines which allomorph appears.","zh":"英语复数表现出同类的可预测性。它虽然一律拼写为 s 或 es，读音却随词根末尾音而变化：在 book、cat、nap 的末尾音之后读 [s]，在 paper、dog、mile 的末尾音之后读 [z]，在 niece、horse、eyelash 的末尾音之后读 [ɪz] 或 [əz]。只要对名词词根的最后一个音作出概括，就能判断出现的是哪一个变体，这正是语音条件制约的语素变体的特点。"},{"en":"Other plurals are not predictable at all and have to be memorized as a list, which makes them lexically conditioned allomorphy. These include -(r)en in children and oxen, internal change in mice, geese, and women, and no change in fish, sheep, and deer. Nouns with no change are described as taking an empty or zero affix, written with the symbol ∅. The allomorphs of the English plural seen here are therefore -s, -z, -ɪz, -(r)en, internal change, and -∅.","zh":"另一些复数形式完全不可预测，只能作为词表逐项记忆，因而属于词汇条件制约的语素变体。这包括 children、oxen 中的 -(r)en，mice、geese、women 中的内部变化，以及 fish、sheep、deer 的无变化形式。复数无变化的名词可说是接了一个空词缀或称零词缀，用符号 ∅ 表示，即该语素没有显性形式。英语复数的语素变体不止本节所列，仅这里出现的就有 -s、-z、-ɪz、-(r)en、内部变化和 -∅ 六种。"},{"en":"When a single morpheme can be realized in more than one way, its different forms are called allomorphs of that morpheme. Listing the allomorphs of the English plural seen in this section gives -s, -z, -ɪz, -(r)en, internal change, and -∅. The section closes by noting that English has more plural allomorphs than these and by asking whether other affixes, in English or in other languages, also show allomorphy.","zh":"当一个语素可以有不止一种实现方式时，它的各种形式就称为该语素的语素变体。把本节所见英语复数的语素变体列出来，即 -s、-z、-ɪz、-(r)en、内部变化和 -∅。本节最后指出，英语复数的语素变体还不止这些，并请读者思考英语或其他语言中是否还有其他词缀也表现出语素变体现象，以及自己熟悉的语言里复数的语素变体又有哪些。"}]},"chapter-044-slug-5-4-lexical-categories-and-the-split-between-derivation-and-inflection":{"title":{"en":"5.5 Lexical categories","zh":"5.5 词类"},"summary":{"en":"Morphology divides into derivation, which changes meaning or category, and inflection, which expresses grammatical information for a word’s category; compounds contain multiple roots in one word. This section defines lexical categories by distribution rather than by meaning and reviews syntactic and morphological tests for nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs in English.","zh":"形态学分为派生与屈折：派生改变词基的意义或词类，屈折表达与词类相适应的语法信息；复合词则由多个词根构成。本节主张按分布而非按意义界定词类，并逐一给出英语名词、动词、形容词和副词的句法测试与形态测试。"},"points":[{"en":"Derivational morphology changes the meaning or category of a base, while inflectional morphology expresses grammatical information suited to its category.","zh":"派生形态学改变词基的意义或词类，屈折形态学则表达与词类相适应的语法信息。"},{"en":"Categories are defined by distribution, the grammatical contexts where words occur, rather than by semantic definitions like person, place or thing.","zh":"词类应按分布即词语出现的语法环境来界定，而不能依赖人、地、物这类语义定义。"},{"en":"Nouns follow determiners, are modified by adjectives, serve as subjects or objects, and have plural forms such as books and governments.","zh":"名词可接限定词、受形容词修饰、充当主语或宾语，并有复数形式，如 books、governments。"},{"en":"Verbs combine with auxiliaries, follow the infinitive marker to, take objects, and show -s, past, perfect, and progressive forms.","zh":"动词可与助动词组合、接不定式标记 to、带宾语，并有 -s、过去、完成和进行等形式。"},{"en":"Adjectives modify nouns, can be modified by very, and may take -ish, comparative, or superlative forms.","zh":"形容词修饰名词，可受 very 修饰，并可加 -ish 或构成比较级、最高级。"},{"en":"Adverbs modify verbs, adjectives, and other adverbs, cannot stand alone between a determiner and a noun, and often end in -ly.","zh":"副词修饰动词、形容词和其他副词，不能单独出现在限定词与名词之间，且多以后缀 -ly 结尾。"}],"terms":[{"en":"derivational morphology","zh":"派生形态学","defEn":"Morphology that changes the meaning or the lexical category of its base.","defZh":"改变词基意义或词类的形态过程，其词缀还可选择所附词基的词类。"},{"en":"inflectional morphology","zh":"屈折形态学","defEn":"Morphology that expresses grammatical information appropriate to a word’s category.","defZh":"表达与该词词类相适应的语法信息的形态过程，如动词的时和名词的复数。"},{"en":"lexical category","zh":"词类","defEn":"A group of words that behave alike grammatically, such as nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs.","defZh":"在语法上表现相同的一类词或语素，通常指名词、动词、形容词和副词。"},{"en":"distribution","zh":"分布","defEn":"The set of grammatical contexts in which a word or morpheme can occur.","defZh":"某一词或语素可以出现的语法环境的总和，是划分词类的依据。"},{"en":"selection","zh":"选择（限制）","defEn":"The property of derivational affixes creating particular categories and attaching only to specific categories.","defZh":"派生词缀既造成特定词类、又只黏附于特定词类的特性，如 -ment 只附于动词。"},{"en":"compound","zh":"复合词","defEn":"A word that contains more than one root within a single word.","defZh":"由两个或更多词根构成的一个词，与加词缀的构词方式相区别。"}],"examples":[{"text":"an event, the proposal","noteEn":"Nouns can follow a determiner and be modified by adjectives such as happy or new.","noteZh":"名词前可有限定词，并可受 happy、new 等形容词修饰。"},{"text":"Events occurred. → They occurred.","noteEn":"Nouns can be subjects of a verb and can be replaced by a pronoun.","noteZh":"名词可以充当动词的主语，并且可以用代词替换。"},{"text":"she/he/it kicks, goes, remains","noteEn":"Verbs have a third person singular present tense form built with -s.","noteZh":"动词有第三人称单数现在时形式，通常以后缀 -s 构成。"},{"text":"happier, happiest","noteEn":"Adjectives may have comparative and superlative forms, in addition to taking the suffix -ish.","noteZh":"形容词除可加后缀 -ish 外，还可能有比较级和最高级形式。"}],"body":[{"en":"Morphology is commonly divided into two types. Derivational morphology changes the meaning or the category of its base, while inflectional morphology expresses grammatical information appropriate to a word’s category. A third pattern, compounding, builds a single word out of multiple roots. Because both definitions refer to the category of the base, that notion matters. Traditional grammar calls the category of a word its part of speech; in morphology the lexical categories of interest are nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs.","zh":"形态学通常分为两类：派生形态学改变词基的意义或词类，屈折形态学表达与词类相适应的语法信息。第三种构词方式是复合，即用多个词根构成一个词。由于上述两个定义都涉及词基的词类，词类这一概念十分重要。传统语法把词的类别称作词性；在形态学中，我们关注的词类是名词、动词、形容词和副词。"},{"en":"A category is a group of words or morphemes that behave the same way as one another for grammatical purposes. Traditional semantic definitions, such as calling a noun a person, place, or thing or a verb an action word, do not reliably identify the categories relevant to linguistic analysis; they are hard to apply in borderline cases and can yield inconsistent results, since action and event look like action words but are in fact nouns. Linguists therefore define categories by distribution, the grammatical contexts in which words or morphemes occur, and distribution varies from language to language.","zh":"一个词类就是在语法上表现相同的一组词或语素。传统上依据意义给词性下定义，例如说名词表示人、地或物，动词表示动作，但这类语义测试并不能可靠地识别语言分析所需的词类：它们在临界情形下难以操作，结果也不一致，因为 action 和 event 看起来像动作词，实际上却是名词。因此语言学家按分布来界定词类，即词或语素出现的语法环境，而不同语言的分布并不相同。"},{"en":"Distributional tests for English lexical categories are then reviewed. Nouns can follow a determiner, be modified by adjectives, act as subject or object, be replaced by a pronoun, and take singular and plural forms. Verbs combine with auxiliaries, follow the infinitive marker to, take objects, and have third person -s, past, perfect or passive, and progressive forms. Adjectives modify nouns, can be modified by very, and may take -ish or comparative and superlative forms. Adverbs modify verbs, adjectives, and other adverbs, cannot stand alone between a determiner and a noun, and many end in -ly.","zh":"本节随后回顾英语各词类的分布测试。名词可以接限定词、受形容词修饰、充当主语或宾语、用代词替换，并有单复数形式。动词可与助动词组合、接不定式标记 to、带宾语，并有第三人称 -s、过去、完成或被动以及进行等形式。形容词修饰名词，可受 very 修饰，并可加 -ish 或构成比较级、最高级。副词修饰动词、形容词和其他副词，不能单独出现在限定词与名词之间，其中许多以 -ly 结尾。"},{"en":"Derivational affixes also help identify category. Suffixes such as -ment and -ness always create nouns, while -ify and -ize always create verbs, and their bases are typically of a specific category. This property of creating particular categories while attaching only to specific ones is called selection.","zh":"派生词缀也有助于判断词类。像 -ment 和 -ness 这样的后缀总是构成名词，而 -ify 和 -ize 总是构成动词，并且它们的词基通常属于特定词类。这种既产生特定词类、又只黏附于特定词类的特性称为选择（限制）。"}]},"chapter-045-slug-5-5-derivational-morphology":{"title":{"en":"5.6 Derivational morphology","zh":"5.6 派生形态学"},"summary":{"en":"Derivational morphemes build new words and are typically selective about the category of the base they attach to. English suffixes such as -able may change category, while prefixes such as un- and re- keep it and add meaning. Because each affix has selectional restrictions, the order in which affixes attach is often uniquely determined, as in foolishly and unkindness.","zh":"派生语素用于构造新词，并且往往对词基的类别有所选择，这种特性称为选择性。英语后缀如 -able 会改变词类，通常只接在动词上；而 un-、re- 等前缀不改变词类，只增添否定、重复等意义。借自法语和拉丁语的词缀能产性较低，-ish、-ness、-able、-ing 则最为能产。由于每个词缀都有选择限制，词缀接合的顺序常被唯一确定，foolishly 与 unkindness 即是典型例证。"},"points":[{"en":"Derivational affixes select the category of their base: -able attaches only to verbs and always creates adjectives.","zh":"派生词缀会选择词基的类别：-able 只能接在动词上，并且一律构成形容词。"},{"en":"English prefixes never change the category of their base, but express meanings such as negation, repetition, and ordering.","zh":"英语前缀从不改变词基的词类，只表达否定、重复、顺序等意义。"},{"en":"Latinate affixes borrowed from French and Latin prefer to combine with each other, making them less productive than other affixes.","zh":"借自法语和拉丁语的拉丁语系词缀倾向于彼此结合，因此比其他词缀的能产性更低。"},{"en":"-ish, -ness, -able, and -ing are among the most productive suffixes; -ing attaches to every English verb.","zh":"-ish、-ness、-able 和 -ing 是英语中最能产的后缀，其中 -ing 尤其能产，可以接于全部动词。"},{"en":"Affixes attach to the outer edge of the base, so selectional properties often determine the only possible order of attachment.","zh":"词缀总是接在词基外缘，因此选择限制往往决定唯一可行的接合顺序。"}],"terms":[{"en":"derivational morphology","zh":"派生形态学","defEn":"Morphology that builds new words and often changes the lexical category of the base.","defZh":"构造新词、并常改变词基词类的形态学过程，与屈折形态学相对。"},{"en":"select","zh":"选择","defEn":"Of an affix, to restrict the category or identity of the bases it attaches to.","defZh":"指词缀对接合词基的类别或具体词根加以限制的特性，限制越强则能产性越低。"},{"en":"productive","zh":"能产的","defEn":"Describing an affix that combines freely with many bases in a language.","defZh":"形容某一词缀能与语言中大量词基自由组合，造出可接受的新词。"},{"en":"root","zh":"词根","defEn":"The smallest meaningful lexical unit, to which affixes may attach.","defZh":"最小的有意义词汇单位，词缀可以接于其上构成新词，如 fool 之于 foolish。"},{"en":"circumfix","zh":"环缀","defEn":"An affix with two parts that surround the base, attaching at both edges.","defZh":"由两部分构成、分别接在词基两端的词缀，两个部分共同表达一个意义。"}],"examples":[{"text":"readable, writeable, playable, employable, and googleable","noteEn":"Adjectives produced by the suffix -able attaching only to English verbs.","noteZh":"后缀 -able 只接在英语动词后，由此构成的形容词表示「能够被……的」。"},{"text":"non-issue, non-distinct, undo, unhappy, redo","noteEn":"Derivational prefixes that keep the category of their base while adding meaning.","noteZh":"这些派生前缀不改变词基的词类，只在原有意义上增添否定、重复等含义。"},{"text":"foolishly","noteEn":"The noun root fool takes -ish to form an adjective, then -ly to form an adverb.","noteZh":"名词词根 fool 先接 -ish 构成形容词 foolish，再接 -ly 构成副词，这是唯一可能的顺序。"},{"text":"unkindness","noteEn":"Only un- before -ness is possible, because un- cannot attach to the noun kindness.","noteZh":"只能先接 un- 再接 -ness，因为 un- 不能接在名词 kindness 上，否则选择限制无法满足。"}],"body":[{"en":"Derivational morphology builds new words. A derivational affix is selective: it cares about the category of the base it attaches to, and it may change that category in the resulting word. The English suffix -able, for instance, attaches only to verbs and always produces adjectives meaning \"able to be verb-ed\", which is why even so recent a verb as google yields the adjective googleable. A representative sample of English derivational suffixes includes -tion, -able, -en, -ed, -ing, -ment, -ness, -ity, -ous, -hood, -ize, -ly, and -ish, each described by the category it selects and the category it creates.","zh":"派生形态学负责构造新词。派生词缀具有选择性：它关注词基的类别，并可能使整个词的类别发生改变。以英语后缀 -able 为例，它只能接在动词后，并且一律构成表示「能够被……的」的形容词，因此即便像 google 这样较新的动词，也能造出形容词 googleable。英语派生后缀的一个代表性样本包括 -tion、-able、-en、-ed、-ing、-ment、-ness、-ity、-ous、-hood、-ize、-ly 和 -ish，每个后缀都可以按其所选择的类别和所构成的类别加以描述。这说明构词能力来自词缀的组合规则，而不取决于词典是否已经收录某个词。"},{"en":"English prefixes behave differently: they never change the category of their base, though they carry clear meanings such as negation, repetition, and ordering, as in pre- and post-. The prefixes non-, un-, and re- illustrate this, attaching to nouns, adjectives, or verbs without altering the category. Some derivational affixes are even more restrictive and demand particular roots. Many English derivational patterns were borrowed from French and Latin, and these latinate affixes tend to combine with one another, or only with latinate roots, which makes them less productive than affixes that combine freely with most bases.","zh":"英语前缀的表现不同：它们从不改变词基的类别，却带有明确的意义，如否定、重复和顺序（如 pre- 与 post-）。前缀 non-、un- 和 re- 即为例证，它们可以接在名词、形容词或动词上而不改变词类。有些派生词缀限制更强，要求与特定的词根结合。英语中许多派生模式借自法语和拉丁语，这些拉丁语系词缀往往彼此结合，或只与拉丁语词根结合，因而比能与大多数词基自由组合的词缀更能产性更低。"},{"en":"The order in which affixes attach matters, because affixes attach to the outer edge of their base. In foolishly, -ish must attach first to the noun root fool, producing the adjective foolish, before -ly turns it into an adverb. When a word contains both prefixes and suffixes, selectional properties often rule out all but one order. In unkindness, attaching -ness first would create the noun kindness, to which un- cannot attach at all; only the order in which un- attaches to the adjective kind before -ness matches the selectional properties of the affixes involved.","zh":"词缀接合的顺序之所以重要，是因为词缀总是接在词基的外缘。在 foolishly 中，-ish 必须先接在名词词根 fool 上构成形容词 foolish，然后 -ly 才把它变成副词。当一个词同时包含前缀和后缀时，选择限制往往排除掉除一种之外的所有顺序。在 unkindness 中，若先接 -ness 就会得到名词 kindness，而 un- 根本无法接在其上；只有先让 un- 接在形容词 kind 上、再接 -ness 的顺序，才符合相关词缀的选择限制。因此表面上存在两种可能的构造顺序，实际上却只有一种符合语言事实。"}]},"chapter-046-slug-5-6":{"title":{"en":"5.7 Inflectional morphology","zh":"5.7 屈折形态学"},"summary":{"en":"Inflectional morphology never changes the category of its base; it adds grammatical information that a language requires. English marks number, case on pronouns, verb agreement, tense, participles, and the progressive, plus adjective comparison. Other languages add dual, trial, paucal, inclusive and exclusive person, richer case and agreement systems, aspect, negation, and categories such as evidentiality, modality, and gender.","zh":"屈折形态学不改变词基的词类，只添加该语言所要求的语法信息。英语的屈折包括名词的数、代词的格、动词一致、时、分词与进行体，以及形容词的比较等级。其他语言还区分双数、三数、少量数，第一人称的包括式与排除式，更丰富的格与一致系统、体、否定，以及示证、情态、性别等更多范畴。"},"points":[{"en":"Inflectional morphology never changes the lexical category of its base and expresses grammatical information the language requires.","zh":"屈折形态学从不改变词基的词类，只表达该语言所要求的语法信息。"},{"en":"English inflection covers number, pronominal case, verb agreement, tense, participles, progressive -ing, and adjective comparison.","zh":"英语屈折包括数、代词格、动词一致、时、分词、进行体 -ing 和形容词比较等级。"},{"en":"Inflection can also be expressed syntactically with particles, a separate word rather than an affix on the verb.","zh":"屈折信息也可通过句法手段表达，如用时态助词而非动词上的词缀。"},{"en":"Number systems may contrast singular, plural, dual, trial, or paucal, as Inuktitut does on nouns and agreeing verbs.","zh":"数系统可区分单数、复数、双数、三数或少量数，因纽特语的名词和一致动词即如此。"},{"en":"Person may distinguish inclusive from exclusive first person plural, as in Anishinaabemowin giinawind and niinawind.","zh":"人称可区分第一人称复数的包括式与排除式，如阿尼希纳贝语的 giinawind 与 niinawind。"},{"en":"Languages may mark obviation, causative, evidentiality, modality, gender, or noun class through morphology rather than syntax.","zh":"一些语言用形态而非句法标记近指与远指、使役、示证、情态、性别或名词类别。"}],"terms":[{"en":"inflectional morphology","zh":"屈折形态学","defEn":"Morphology that marks grammatical information without changing the category of the base.","defZh":"不改变词基词类、只标记语法信息（如数、时、格、一致）的形态学过程。"},{"en":"number","zh":"数","defEn":"The grammatical distinction between singular, plural, and possibly dual, trial, or paucal.","defZh":"单数、复数以及可能的双数、三数或少量数之间的语法区分，属于名词的屈折范畴。"},{"en":"case","zh":"格","defEn":"Marking on nouns that reflects their grammatical role in the sentence.","defZh":"名词上反映其在句中语法角色（如主语、宾语、领属）的标记，英语只保留在代词上。"},{"en":"agreement","zh":"一致","defEn":"Inflectional morphology that reflects properties of another word in the sentence.","defZh":"反映句中另一词语（通常是主语名词）属性的屈折形态，如动词与主语在人称、数上的一致。"},{"en":"aspect","zh":"体","defEn":"The perspective taken on an event, described either as complete or as ongoing.","defZh":"对事件所采取的视角，即把事件描述为已经完成还是仍在进行，如完成体与进行体。"},{"en":"evidentiality","zh":"示证","defEn":"Morphology indicating the source of a speaker's evidence or degree of certainty.","defZh":"标示说话人证据来源或确信程度的形态标记，如土耳其语的直接过去与间接过去。"}],"examples":[{"text":"titiraut, titirautiik, titirautit","noteEn":"Inuktitut singular, dual, and plural forms of the noun meaning \"pen\".","noteZh":"因纽特语中意为「笔」的名词的单数、双数与复数形式。"},{"text":"giinawind","noteEn":"The Anishinaabemowin pronoun for inclusive we, meaning \"we including the person addressed\".","noteZh":"阿尼希纳贝语表示包括式的第一人称复数代词，意为「包括听话人在内的我们」。"},{"text":"gel-di, gel-miş","noteEn":"Turkish direct past versus indirect past, for witnessed versus reported evidence.","noteZh":"土耳其语的直接过去与间接过去，分别表示亲见证据与转述证据。"},{"text":"le (了), zài (在)","noteEn":"Mandarin particles expressing perfective and progressive aspect, separate from the verb.","noteZh":"汉语普通话中表示完成体与进行体的助词，与动词分离而非充当词缀。"}],"body":[{"en":"Inflectional morphology differs from derivation in one crucial respect: it never changes the category of its base, suiting instead the grammatical information that a particular language requires. English has a very limited inflectional system. Nouns inflect for number, and pronouns for nominative, accusative, and possessive case. Verbs agree with third person singular subjects in the present, contrast past with present tense, take participial -ed or -en, and add progressive -ing after auxiliary be. Adjectives take comparative -er and superlative -est, though some analyse these as derivational.","zh":"屈折形态学与派生形态学有一个关键区别：它从不改变词基的词类，只满足特定语言所要求的语法信息。英语的屈折系统十分有限：名词有数的屈折；代词有主格、宾格和属格的区分；动词在现在时中与第三人称单数主语一致，并区分过去时与现在时，还有分词 -ed 或 -en，以及助动词 be 后的进行体 -ing；形容词有比较级 -er 和最高级 -est，不过也有人把它们分析为派生。"},{"en":"Inflectional information can also be expressed syntactically rather than morphologically. Some languages have tense but mark it with a particle, a separate word, instead of an affix on the verb; this is still tense, yet it is not part of inflectional morphology. The survey below covers inflectional distinctions commonly made in the world's languages, but many types of inflection are not mentioned.","zh":"屈折信息也可以用句法而非形态手段表达。有些语言拥有时范畴，却用助词这一独立的词来标记，而不是在动词上附加词缀；这仍然是时，但不属于屈折形态学。以下概述介绍世界语言中常见的屈折区分类型，但仍有许多屈折类型未予提及。"},{"en":"Number is the most familiar category. Many languages contrast only singular with plural, but others add dual for exactly two things, as Inuktitut does for nouns and agreeing verbs; a few languages have a trial for groups of three, usually only on pronouns, and some have a paucal for small groups. Person distinguishes first, second, and third, and some languages split the first person plural into inclusive, meaning me plus you, and exclusive, meaning me plus others but not you. Anishinaabemowin marks this contrast with giinawind and niinawind.","zh":"数是最常见的范畴。许多语言只区分单数与复数，另一些语言还有表示恰好两个事物的双数，因纽特语的名词以及与主语一致的动词即如此；少数语言还有通常只用于代词、表示三个一组的三数，有些语言则有表示少量小组的少量数。人称区分第一、第二和第三人称，部分语言把第一人称复数分为包括式（我加你）与排除式（我加其他人但不包括你），阿尼希纳贝语用 giinawind 和 niinawind 表达这一对立。"},{"en":"Case marks the grammatical role of nouns and survives in English only on pronouns, while French distinguishes dative from accusative on third person pronouns. Agreement reflects properties of another word, most commonly a subject noun. Tense contrasts present with past, and aspect presents an event as complete or ongoing; Mandarin le (了) and zài (在) express perfective and progressive aspect as particles. Negation, obviation, causatives, evidentiality, modality, and gender or noun class are marked morphologically in various languages, though English uses other means.","zh":"格标记名词的语法角色，在现代英语中只保留于代词，而法语在第三人称代词上区分与格和宾格。一致反映句中另一词语（通常是主语名词）的属性。时区分现在与过去，体则把事件呈现为完成或正在进行；汉语普通话用助词 了 和 在 分别表达完成体与进行体。此外，否定、近指与远指、使役、示证、情态以及性别或名词类别在许多语言中由形态标记，而英语大多通过其他手段表达。"}]},"chapter-047-slug-5-7-compounding":{"title":{"en":"5.8 Compounding","zh":"5.8 复合"},"summary":{"en":"Compounds are words built from more than one root, combining roots with roots rather than roots with affixes. English forms compounds freely across categories such as Noun-Noun and Adjective-Noun, and spelling is inconsistent, but compounds take stress on their first member and are interpreted as single words. Their head normally lies on the right, while exocentric and dvandva compounds differ.","zh":"复合词由两个或更多词根构成，是词根与词根的结合，而非词根与词缀的结合。英语可以自由构成名词-名词、形容词-名词等各种类型的复合词；其拼写并不统一，但重音落在第一个成分上，并被理解为单一的词。复合词的中心语通常位于右侧，外部中心复合词与并列复合词则属例外。"},"points":[{"en":"Compounds contain more than one root and combine roots with roots rather than roots with affixes.","zh":"复合词包含一个以上词根，是词根与词根的组合，而不是词根与词缀的组合。"},{"en":"English builds compounds freely across categories, including Noun-Noun, Adjective-Noun, Verb-Noun, and Noun-Verb combinations.","zh":"英语可跨词类自由构词，包括名词-名词、形容词-名词、动词-名词和名词-动词等组合。"},{"en":"Compounds take stress on their first member, while phrases take stress on their last member.","zh":"复合词的重音落在第一个成分上，而短语的重音落在最后一个成分上。"},{"en":"The head of an English compound is on the right, so endocentric compounds are a type of what their head denotes.","zh":"英语复合词的中心语位于右侧，因此向心复合词表示其中心语所指事物的一种。"},{"en":"Exocentric compounds lack such a head, and dvandva compounds are co-headed and can be paraphrased with and.","zh":"外部中心复合词没有这种中心语，并列复合词则属共同中心，可用「和」来改写。"}],"terms":[{"en":"compounding","zh":"复合","defEn":"Word formation that combines two or more roots into a single word.","defZh":"把两个或更多词根组合成一个词的构词方式，不同于派生和屈折。"},{"en":"endocentric","zh":"向心","defEn":"Describing a compound whose head determines its category and interpretation.","defZh":"中心语位于复合词内部并决定整词词类与释义的复合词，如 sunflower 与 bluebird。"},{"en":"exocentric","zh":"外部中心","defEn":"Describing a compound with no head inside it, denoting neither member.","defZh":"内部没有中心语的复合词，其指称不等于其中任何一个成分。"},{"en":"dvandva","zh":"并列复合词","defEn":"A co-headed compound paraphrasable with and between its two members.","defZh":"共同中心的复合词，指称两个成分之和，可在两者之间用「和」来改写。"},{"en":"head","zh":"中心语","defEn":"The member of a compound that determines its category and interpretation.","defZh":"复合词中决定整词词类和释义的那个成分，英语复合词的中心语位于右侧。"}],"examples":[{"text":"doghouse, website, basketball, sunflower, moonlight","noteEn":"English Noun-Noun compounds listed among the categories in the section.","noteZh":"该节按词类列举的英语名词-名词复合词，其中心语均位于右侧。"},{"text":"bláckboard, gréenhouse, blúebird","noteEn":"Compounds carry stress on the first member, unlike the phrases black bóard and green hóuse.","noteZh":"复合词重音落在第一个成分上，与短语 black bóard、green hóuse 的重音位置不同。"},{"text":"Donaudampfschiffahrtsgesellschaftskapitän","noteEn":"German compound meaning Danube steam shipping company captain, spelled without spaces.","noteZh":"德语复合词，意为「多瑙河蒸汽航运公司船长」，书写时不留空格。"},{"text":"zigzag, helter skelter, flip flop, riff raff, hocus pocus","noteEn":"Reduplicative dvandva compounds whose two roots mirror each other's sounds.","noteZh":"叠音式并列复合词，两个词根在语音上彼此呼应。"}],"body":[{"en":"Compounding is the last main type of morphology. A compound is a word built from more than one root, though it may also contain derived words; any word containing two roots is certainly a compound. What sets compounding apart from derivation and inflection is that it combines roots with roots instead of roots with affixes. English builds compounds very freely, much like other Germanic languages such as German and Dutch, and examples exist for almost every pair of categories: Noun-Noun (doghouse, website, basketball), Adjective-Noun (greenhouse, bluebird), Verb-Noun (breakwater), Noun-Adjective (trustworthy, watertight), Adjective-Adjective (purebred, kind-hearted), Noun-Verb (browbeat, sidestep), and Adjective-Verb (blacklist).","zh":"复合是最后一类主要构词方式。复合词是由一个以上词根构成的词，其中也可以包含派生词；只要一个词里出现两个词根，它就一定是复合词。复合与派生、屈折的区别在于，它把词根与词根组合起来，而不是把词根与词缀组合起来。英语构词十分自由，与德语、荷兰语等日耳曼语言相似，几乎任何两个词类的组合都能找到实例：名词-名词（doghouse、website、basketball）、形容词-名词（greenhouse、bluebird）、动词-名词（breakwater）、名词-形容词（trustworthy、watertight）、形容词-形容词（purebred、kind-hearted）、名词-动词（browbeat、sidestep）以及形容词-动词（blacklist）。"},{"en":"English spells compounds inconsistently: older ones are written solid, others are hyphenated, and many new ones are written with a space. Pronunciation nevertheless reveals their status, because compounds carry stress on their first member while phrases carry it on their last: bláckboard and gréenhouse differ from black bóard and green hóuse. Interpretation also differs, since a blackboard need not be black and a greenhouse usually is not green. Syntactically, English cannot string bare nouns together, so any such sequence of noun-like words must be a compound.","zh":"英语复合词的拼写并不统一：较古老的写法连写，另一些用连字符，许多新复合词则分开书写。但读音仍能显示其性质，因为复合词的重音落在第一个成分上，而短语的重音落在最后一个成分上：bláckboard、gréenhouse 与 black bóard、green hóuse 读音不同。释义也不同，因为 blackboard 未必是黑色的，greenhouse 通常也不是绿色的。从句法上看，英语无法把光杆名词直接连缀起来，因此凡是这样的名词性序列，必然是复合词。"},{"en":"Most compounds have a head, which determines both their interpretation and their category: a sunflower is a type of flower and is a noun, while a bluebird is a type of bird and also a noun. English is thus a right-headed language. Compounds with a head are endocentric, and those without one are exocentric: redhead and sabretooth describe a person or animal rather than a type of head or tooth, and outcome and tell-all have no head matching their category at all. Dvandva compounds are co-headed and can be paraphrased with and; many are reduplicatives such as zigzag and flip flop, with bittersweet and parent-child as further examples. Dvandva compounds are relatively uncommon in English.","zh":"大多数复合词都有一个中心语，它同时决定整词的释义和词类：sunflower 是花的一种，也是名词；bluebird 是鸟的一种，也是名词。因此英语是中心语在右的语言。有中心语的复合词是向心复合词，没有中心语的则是外部中心复合词：redhead 和 sabretooth 指人或动物，而不表示某类头或牙；outcome 和 tell-all 更没有任何成分与其词类相配。并列复合词属共同中心，可用「和」改写；其中许多是叠音词，如 zigzag 和 flip flop，bittersweet 与 parent-child 也是例子。并列复合词在英语中相对少见。"}]},"chapter-048-ambiguity-in-ordering":{"title":{"en":"5.9 Structural ambiguity in morphology","zh":"5.9 形态学中的结构歧义"},"summary":{"en":"Affixes do not always attach in a fixed order, and when a string of morphemes permits more than one structural representation it is structurally ambiguous. Such ambiguity arises in derivational morphology when an affix can attach to bases of more than one category, and it is even more common with compounds. Different trees usually correspond to different meanings.","zh":"词缀的附着顺序并非总是固定不变；当一个语素串可以与不止一种结构表征相容时，它就具有结构歧义。在派生形态中，只要至少有一个词缀能够附着于不止一个词类的词基，就可能出现这种歧义；在复合词中结构歧义更为常见。不同的树形结构通常对应不同的意义。"},"points":[{"en":"A string is structurally ambiguous when it fits more than one structural representation, and each tree usually carries a different meaning.","zh":"当一个语素串可以与不止一种结构表征相容时，它便具有结构歧义，而每种树形结构通常对应不同的意义。"},{"en":"Derivational ambiguity requires at least one affix to attach to bases of more than one lexical category.","zh":"派生歧义的出现要求至少有一个词缀能够附着于不止一个词类的词基。"},{"en":"Untieable is ambiguous: able to be untied, or not able to be tied, depending on whether un- or -able attaches first.","zh":"untieable 有两种解读：可以解开的，或无法系上的，取决于 un- 与 -able 谁先附着。"},{"en":"Compounds like river boat race are ambiguous because any string of noun roots may combine in multiple orders.","zh":"像 river boat race 这样的复合词具有歧义，因为任何一串名词词根都可能以多种顺序组合。"},{"en":"Structural ambiguity differs from homophony: bank has two different roots that sound the same, with nothing structural involved.","zh":"结构歧义不同于同音异义：bank 是两个同音的不同词根，其中不涉及任何结构因素。"},{"en":"Phonology can reduce ambiguity, since some speakers stress ríver for one reading of river boat race and bóat for the other.","zh":"语音可降低歧义：有人读 river boat race 时，一种意思重音在 ríver，另一种在 bóat。"}],"terms":[{"en":"structural ambiguity","zh":"结构歧义","defEn":"A situation in which one string of morphemes has more than one possible structural representation.","defZh":"指同一个语素串可以对应不止一种结构表征，从而产生多种意义的现象。"},{"en":"paraphrase","zh":"释义（改述）","defEn":"A different way of saying the same thing, used to bring out a word's interpretations.","defZh":"用另一种说法表达相同的意思，用以显示某个词的不同解读。"},{"en":"homophone","zh":"同音词","defEn":"A word that sounds the same as another word but has a different meaning.","defZh":"与另一个词读音相同而意义不同、词源也不同的词，如 bank 的两个含义。"},{"en":"compound","zh":"复合词","defEn":"A word built by combining two or more roots, such as river boat race.","defZh":"由两个或更多词根组合而成的词，例如 river boat race。"},{"en":"root","zh":"词根","defEn":"The core morpheme of a word that carries its basic meaning.","defZh":"词的核心语素，承载基本词汇意义，是构词所依据的最小单位。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the knot most people use for their shoelaces is chosen because it’s easily untieable","noteEn":"One reading of untieable: able to be untied, with un- attaching to tie first.","noteZh":"untieable 的一种解读：可以解开的，由 un- 先附着于 tie 得到。"},{"text":"if you haven’t learned to tie knots, some complex knots might seem untieable","noteEn":"The other reading: not able to be tied, with -able attaching to tie first.","noteZh":"另一种解读：无法系上的，由 -able 先附着于 tie 得到。"},{"text":"river boat race","noteEn":"A three-root compound: a race between river boats, or a boat race on a river.","noteZh":"由三个词根构成的复合词：河船之间的比赛，或在河上举行的划船比赛。"},{"text":"the kind of bank that’s a financial institution or the kind of bank that’s the edge of a river","noteEn":"Homophony, not structural ambiguity: two roots that simply sound the same.","noteZh":"这属于同音异义而非结构歧义：两个只是读音相同的不同词根。"}],"body":[{"en":"Affixes are not restricted to a single attachment order. When both orders, or all orders if there are more than two affixes, satisfy the selectional requirements of every affix involved, one string of morphemes becomes compatible with more than one tree. Such a string is structurally ambiguous, and the competing structures are typically paired with distinct meanings. The word untieable illustrates this: it can mean able to be untied, if the prefix un- first attaches to the verb tie and the suffix -able is added afterwards, or not able to be tied, if -able attaches to tie first and un- then attaches to the resulting adjective.","zh":"词缀并不限于某一种固定的附着顺序。当两种顺序（若词缀多于两个，则是所有顺序）都满足相关词缀的选择要求时，同一个语素串就会与不止一种树形结构相容。这样的语素串具有结构歧义，而相互竞争的结构通常对应着不同的意义。untieable 一词便是如此：若前缀 un- 先附着于动词 tie，再附加后缀 -able，得到“可以解开的”这一解读；若 -able 先附着于 tie，再让 un- 附着于由此得到的形容词，则得到“无法系上的”这一解读。"},{"en":"This kind of ambiguity in derivational morphology depends on at least one affix being able to attach to bases of more than one lexical category. Compounds display the same phenomenon even more readily, since any string of noun roots may in principle combine in several ways. The compound river boat race contains the roots river, boat and race. Combining river and boat first yields [river boat] race, a race between river boats wherever it is held; combining boat and race first yields river [boat race], a race of any boats that takes place on a river.","zh":"派生形态中的这类歧义要求至少有一个词缀能够附着于不止一个词类的词基。复合词中这种现象更为常见，因为任何一串名词词根原则上都可以以多种方式组合。复合词 river boat race 包含 river、boat、race 三个词根：先把 river 与 boat 组合，得到 [river boat] race，指河船之间的比赛，无论比赛在何处举行；先把 boat 与 race 组合，则得到 river [boat race]，指任何船只在河上进行的比赛。"},{"en":"Structural ambiguity is not the same as homophony. In a sentence about going to the bank, the uncertainty between a financial institution and a river's edge is not structural at all: there are simply two different roots that sound alike. Phonology can also make a written compound less ambiguous than it looks, as when some speakers put primary stress on ríver for one reading of river boat race and on bóat for the other.","zh":"结构歧义不同于同音异义。说去 the bank 时，听话人无法确定是金融机构还是河岸，这种歧义并非来自结构：只是两个读音相同而意义不同的词根而已。语音有时也会让书面形式看似歧义的复合词变得不那么歧义，例如有些说话人读 river boat race 的一种解读时把主重音放在 ríver，读另一种解读时放在 bóat。"}]},"chapter-049-slug-5-8-how-to-draw-morphological-trees":{"title":{"en":"5.10 How to draw morphological trees","zh":"5.10 如何绘制形态树"},"summary":{"en":"The order in which derivational affixes attach, or in which the roots of a compound combine, sometimes matters: governmental is not a flat string of govern, -ment and -al, but the result of attaching -ment to govern and then -al to that base. Tree diagrams represent this constituency, the subgroupings of pieces inside a word or phrase. Drawing a tree involves identifying roots, affixes, categories and attachment order.","zh":"派生词缀的附着顺序、或复合词词根的组合顺序有时至关重要：governmental 并非 govern、-ment、-al 的简单线性排列，而是先在 govern 上附加 -ment、再在该词基上附加 -al 的结果。树形图用来表示这种直接成分关系，即词或短语内部各组成部分的分组方式。绘制形态树需要识别词根、词缀、词类以及词缀的附着顺序。"},"points":[{"en":"A word like governmental results from attaching -ment to govern first and then -al to that base.","zh":"governmental 一词是先在 govern 上附加 -ment，再在该词基上附加 -al 的结果。"},{"en":"Tree diagrams represent constituency, the subgroupings of pieces within a larger word or phrase.","zh":"树形图表示直接成分关系，即较大词或短语内部各组成部分之间的分组。"},{"en":"Constituency is always relevant when pieces combine, whether morphemes in a word or words in a sentence.","zh":"只要各组成部分相互结合，成分关系就始终相关，无论是一个词内的语素还是句子中的词。"},{"en":"Steps: identify the root and affixes, determine the root's category and attachment order, then the categories of bases and the whole word.","zh":"步骤是：识别词根与词缀，确定词根的词类与词缀附着顺序，再确定各中间词基及整词的词类。"},{"en":"Reading along the bottom of the tree recovers the order of morphemes, so prefixes stay left and suffixes right.","zh":"沿树形图底端读取即可得到语素的顺序，因此前缀在左、后缀在右。"}],"terms":[{"en":"tree diagram","zh":"树形图","defEn":"A representation of the hierarchical constituency of a word or phrase.","defZh":"用来表示词或短语内部层级性直接成分关系的图式，分支显示各成分如何结合。"},{"en":"constituency","zh":"直接成分关系（组成关系）","defEn":"The subgroupings of pieces within a larger word or phrase.","defZh":"指较大词或短语内部的各组成部分如何分组、哪些成分先结合的关系。"},{"en":"root","zh":"词根","defEn":"The core morpheme of a word, which carries the basic meaning.","defZh":"作为构词核心、承载基本意义的语素，词缀即附着于其上。"},{"en":"affix","zh":"词缀","defEn":"A morpheme that attaches to a base but does not carry the main meaning.","defZh":"附着于词基、本身不承载主要词汇意义的语素，包括前缀和后缀等。"},{"en":"prefix","zh":"前缀","defEn":"An affix that attaches to the left of the base it combines with.","defZh":"附着于所结合词基左侧的词缀；在树形图中位于所附成分的左边。"},{"en":"suffix","zh":"后缀","defEn":"An affix that attaches to the right of the base it combines with.","defZh":"附着于所结合词基右侧的词缀；在树形图中位于所附成分的右边。"}],"examples":[{"text":"governmental","noteEn":"Not a flat string: govern plus -ment, then that base plus -al.","noteZh":"并非简单线性排列：先由 govern 加 -ment，再由该词基加 -al。"},{"text":"govern + the suffix –ment + the suffix –al","noteEn":"The pieces of governmental, listed linearly, though they do not attach all at once.","noteZh":"governmental 的各个组成部分，这里只是线性列出，但它们并不同时附着。"}],"body":[{"en":"In section 5.9 we saw that the order in which derivational affixes attach, or in which the roots of a compound combine, sometimes matters. A word such as governmental is therefore not merely a flat string of the root govern plus the suffix -ment plus the suffix -al. It comes from combining govern with -ment first, and then combining the result of that step with the further suffix -al.","zh":"我们在 5.9 节看到，派生词缀的附着顺序、或复合词词根的组合顺序有时至关重要。因此，像 governmental 这样的词并不只是词根 govern、后缀 -ment 和后缀 -al 的线性排列；它是先把 govern 与 -ment 组合，再把这一步得到的结果与后缀 -al 组合而成的。"},{"en":"Linguists typically represent this kind of structure with a tree diagram. Trees show the constituency of language, that is, the subgroupings of pieces inside a larger word or phrase. A central insight of linguistics is that constituency is always relevant when we describe how pieces combine, whether the pieces are morphemes inside a word or words inside a sentence, though different theories in linguistics often take different views of which hierarchical structures natural languages allow.","zh":"语言学家通常用树形图来表示这类结构。树形图展示语言中的直接成分关系，即较大词或短语内部各组成部分的分组方式。语言学的一个重要洞见是：在描述各成分如何结合时，成分关系始终是相关的，无论这些成分是一个词内部的语素还是句子内部的词；不过，语言学中的不同理论对于自然语言允许哪些层级结构往往持不同看法。"},{"en":"To draw a morphological tree, begin by identifying the root and any affixes: one root means a non-compound word, while two roots mean a compound word. Then determine the category of the root, the order in which the affixes attach, and the category of every intervening base as well as of the whole word. You may find it sensible to work in different orders, and in different orders for different words; practice is the best way to discover what suits you. Trees also encode linear order: reading along the bottom should yield the order of morphemes, so prefixes are always placed to the left of the constituent they attach to and suffixes to the right.","zh":"绘制形态树时，可以先识别词根与词缀：只有一个词根的是非复合词，有两个词根的是复合词。接着确定词根的词类、词缀的附着顺序，以及每个中间词基和整词的词类。你可能会发现，按不同顺序操作更顺手，不同的词也适合不同的顺序；最好的办法是通过练习找到适合自己的方式。树形图还表示各元素的线性顺序：沿树形图底端读下去，应能得到词中语素的顺序；因此前缀总是位于所附成分的左边，后缀总是位于右边。"}]},"chapter-050-how-to-solve-morphology-problems":{"title":{"en":"5.11 How to solve morphology problems","zh":"5.11 如何解决形态学问题"},"summary":{"en":"A key morphological skill is segmenting words of an unfamiliar language into their individual morphemes, that is, identifying roots and affixes in complex words. Because a morpheme is a consistent pairing of form with meaning or function, the method is to compare words whose meanings are known and look for shared parts of form matching shared parts of meaning. Inuktut nouns illustrate the procedure.","zh":"形态学的一项重要技能，是把不熟悉语言中的词切分为一个个语素，也就是识别复杂词中的词根与词缀。由于语素是形式（语音或手势）与意义或功能之间的一致配对，方法就是比较已知意义的词，看意义的共同部分是否对应形式的共同部分。因纽特语（Inuktut）的名词可以说明这一做法。"},"points":[{"en":"Finding morphemes means comparing words whose meanings are known, matching shared meaning with shared form.","zh":"寻找语素就是比较已知意义的词，把意义的共同部分与形式的共同部分对应起来。"},{"en":"In Inuktut, matuit and nuvujait are both plural and share final -it, so -it is the plural suffix.","zh":"在因纽特语中，matuit 与 nuvujait 都是复数，共有词尾 -it，因此 -it 是复数后缀。"},{"en":"Comparing matuit with matu identifies matu as the root meaning door, with no singular suffix required.","zh":"比较 matuit 与 matu 可确定 matu 是意为“门”的词根，单数并不需要后缀。"},{"en":"The dual suffixes -uk and -ak are allomorphs, and their distribution may be phonologically determined.","zh":"双数后缀 -uk 与 -ak 是语素变体，其分布可能由语音条件决定。"},{"en":"Compare words differing in one aspect of meaning, match meaning differences to form differences, and revise earlier hypotheses when stuck.","zh":"比较仅在一个意义方面有差别的词，把意义差别与形式差别对应起来；若卡住，就回头修改先前的假设。"}],"terms":[{"en":"morpheme","zh":"语素","defEn":"A consistent pairing of form, whether sound or sign, with meaning or function.","defZh":"形式（语音或手势）与意义或功能之间的一致配对，是最小的语法单位。"},{"en":"root","zh":"词根","defEn":"The morpheme in a complex word that carries the basic meaning.","defZh":"复杂词中承载基本词汇意义、其余词缀附着于其上的语素。"},{"en":"suffix","zh":"后缀","defEn":"An affix that follows the base it attaches to, such as -it for plural.","defZh":"位于所附词基之后的词缀，例如因纽特语中表示复数的 -it。"},{"en":"allomorph","zh":"语素变体","defEn":"One of the variant forms of a single morpheme, such as -uk and -ak.","defZh":"同一语素的不同形式变体，例如双数后缀 -uk 与 -ak。"},{"en":"dual","zh":"双数","defEn":"A grammatical number referring to exactly two entities, as in matuuk.","defZh":"表示正好两个实体的语法数范畴，区别于单数和复数，如 matuuk。"}],"examples":[{"text":"matuit : nuvujait","noteEn":"Both words are plural and share the final -it, the hypothesized plural suffix.","noteZh":"两个词都是复数，共有词尾 -it，由此推测 -it 为复数后缀。"},{"text":"matuit : matu","noteEn":"Both contain matu and share the meaning door, so matu is the root.","noteZh":"两个词都含 matu、都含“门”的意义，因此 matu 是词根。"},{"text":"matuuk","noteEn":"A dual form made of matu plus the suffix -uk, meaning door (two).","noteZh":"双数形式：matu 加 -uk，意为“两扇门”。"},{"text":"nuvujaak","noteEn":"The other dual form, made of nuvuja plus the suffix -ak, meaning clouds (two).","noteZh":"另一双数形式：nuvuja 加 -ak，意为“两朵云”。"}],"body":[{"en":"An important skill in morphology is the ability to segment words from another language into their individual morphemes, that is, to identify the roots and affixes of complex words. Since a morpheme is a consistent pairing of form (sound or sign) with meaning or function, the search for morphemes requires comparing words whose meanings are known, in order to see whether shared parts of meaning correspond to shared parts of form.","zh":"形态学的一项重要技能，是能把另一种语言的词切分为一个个语素，也就是识别复杂词中的词根与词缀。由于语素是形式（语音或手势）与意义或功能之间的一致配对，寻找语素就必须比较已知意义的词，看意义的共同部分是否与形式的共同部分相对应。"},{"en":"Inuktut nouns for door and cloud, given in singular, dual and plural forms, illustrate the procedure. Starting from a single plural word such as matuit, doors (three or more), there is no way to know how it should be divided. But matuit and nuvujait are both plural, and although their sounds overlap very little they share the final -it; because this is a consistent pairing of form and meaning, we hypothesize that -it is a suffix meaning plural. Comparing matuit with matu, where both contain matu and both include door in their meaning, identifies matu as the root meaning door; singular nouns are commonly suffixless across languages, though one could also posit a -∅ singular suffix.","zh":"因纽特语中表示“门”和“云”的名词有单数、双数、复数三种形式，可以说明这一操作过程。如果只看一个复数词，如 matuit（门，三个或更多），根本无法判断该怎样切分。但 matuit 与 nuvujait 都是复数，它们的语音重合很少，却共有词尾 -it；由于这是形式与意义的一致配对，我们可以假设 -it 是表示复数的后缀。再把 matuit 与 matu 比较：两者都含 matu，也都含“门”的意义，由此可以确定 matu 是意为“门”的词根；单数名词在许多语言中通常不带后缀，不过我们也可以设定一个 -∅ 单数后缀。"},{"en":"Once -it is identified, nuvujait leaves the string nuvuja, which appears in the data with the meaning cloud and can therefore be taken as a root. The two dual forms matuuk door (two) and nuvujaak clouds (two) separate into matu-uk and nuvuja-ak, leaving the slightly different suffixes -uk and -ak; since the roots are already known, these are confidently analysed as allomorphs expressing dual. With more data, the next step would be to test whether the choice between -uk and -ak is predictable in Inuktitut; from these two words one might hypothesize that -uk occurs after [u] and -ak after [a], an instance of phonologically determined allomorphy, but more words are needed to check that prediction.","zh":"一旦确定了 -it，nuvujait 剩下的部分就是 nuvuja，而 nuvuja 确实在数据中以“云”的意义出现，因此可视为词根。两个双数形式 matuuk（两扇门）和 nuvujaak（两朵云）可切分为 matu-uk 与 nuvuja-ak，剩下略有差别的后缀 -uk 与 -ak；由于词根已经确定，可以有把握地把它们分析为表示双数的语素变体。若数据更多，下一步就是检验因纽特语中 -uk 与 -ak 的选择是否可以预测；仅凭这两个词，可以假设 -uk 出现在 [u] 之后、-ak 出现在 [a] 之后，这是由语音条件决定的语素变体现象，但需要更多词来验证这一预测。"}]},"chapter-051-practice-time":{"title":{"en":"5.12 Exercise your linguistics skills","zh":"5.12 练习你的语言学技能"},"summary":{"en":"This closing section gathers an exercise set that practices the chapter's core tools, graded from basic through intermediate to advanced, with each item pointing to the relevant earlier section. Learners segment Turkish and Kreyòl data into morphemes, classify English affixes as derivational or inflectional, determine the lexical categories of words, and identify compounds in English sentences and in Hebrew data, including compounds spelled solid, spaced, or hyphenated.","zh":"本节是一组由基础到进阶的练习，用于操练本章的核心工具。学习者要切分土耳其语与克里奥尔语（Kreyòl）材料中的语素，判断英语词缀属派生还是屈折，确定词类，并辨认英语和希伯来语中的复合词。"},"points":[{"en":"Exercise 1 segments Turkish words into roots and suffixes and builds the phrase meaning 'in our little hands'.","zh":"练习一要求切分土耳其语词中的词根与后缀，并构造出表示“在我们的小手里”的说法。"},{"en":"Exercise 2 asks learners to describe the environments in which the Kreyòl definite article appears as a, la, or ã.","zh":"练习二要求描述克里奥尔语定冠词以 a、la、ã 三种形式出现的环境，并判断制约条件。"},{"en":"Exercises 3 to 5 classify English affixes, test lexical categories, and debate whether conceive and deceive are complex.","zh":"练习三至五判断英语词缀类型、测试词类，并讨论 conceive、deceive 等词是否为复合形式。"},{"en":"Exercises 6 and 7 examine English compound spelling and Hebrew compounds built from nominal roots.","zh":"练习六、七考察英语复合词的拼写差异，以及由名词性词根构成的希伯来语复合词。"},{"en":"The difficulty labels Basic, Intermediate, and Advanced, together with section references, point to the relevant part of the chapter.","zh":"每个练习标注基础、中级或进阶，并给出对应小节编号，指向本章的相关内容。"}],"terms":[{"en":"morpheme","zh":"语素","defEn":"The smallest meaningful unit of language, identified here by comparing recurring forms across words.","defZh":"语言中最小的音义结合单位，在练习中通过比较各个词里反复出现的形式来切分并确定。"},{"en":"allomorph","zh":"语素变体","defEn":"One of the forms in which a morpheme appears, such as the Kreyòl article a, la, or ã.","defZh":"同一语素在具体环境中实现出的形式，如克里奥尔语定冠词的 a、la、ã。"},{"en":"derivational affix","zh":"派生词缀","defEn":"An affix that changes the meaning or category of its base, as in purity or Canadian.","defZh":"改变词基意义或词类的词缀，如 purity、Canadian 中的词缀，能构成新词。"},{"en":"inflectional affix","zh":"屈折词缀","defEn":"An affix that adds grammatical information without changing the category of its base.","defZh":"只添加语法信息而不改变词基词类的词缀，如 newest 的 -est、nieces 的 -s。"},{"en":"lexical category","zh":"词类","defEn":"The class of a word, such as noun, verb, or adjective, established by distributional criteria.","defZh":"词所属的类别，如名词、动词、形容词，依据分布而非意义来判定。"},{"en":"compound","zh":"复合词","defEn":"A word formed from two or more roots, spelled solid, spaced, or hyphenated in English.","defZh":"由两个或更多词根构成的词，英语中可连写、分写或用连字符连接。"}],"examples":[{"text":"evdʒıklerimizde ‘in our little houses’","noteEn":"The Turkish form stacks diminutive, plural, first person plural possessive, and locative suffixes on the root ev.","noteZh":"该土耳其语形式在词根 ev 上依次叠加指小、复数、第一人称复数领属和处所后缀。"},{"text":"panie ‘basket’ ~ paniea ‘the basket’; pitit ‘child’ ~ pititla ‘the child’","noteEn":"The Kreyòl definite article appears as a after a vowel and as la after a consonant.","noteZh":"克里奥尔语定冠词在元音后作 a，在辅音后作 la，属可预测的语音条件制约。"},{"text":"chẽ ‘dog’ ~ chẽã ‘the dog’","noteEn":"After a nasalized vowel the Kreyòl article is ã rather than a.","noteZh":"在鼻化元音之后，克里奥尔语定冠词取 ã 而非 a，说明其选择依据后接语音环境。"},{"text":"yom huledet ‘birthday’","noteEn":"A Hebrew compound of the nouns day and birth, illustrating the nominal roots involved.","noteZh":"由“日”和“出生”两个名词构成的希伯来语复合词，说明参与复合的是名词性词根。"}],"body":[{"en":"Exercise 1 presents sixteen Turkish words transcribed in the International Phonetic Alphabet and asks learners to list every morpheme with its gloss, to say whether each is a root, a prefix, or a suffix, and finally to build a phrase meaning 'in our little hands'. The roots are deniz 'sea', el 'hand', ev 'house', and diʃ 'tooth', and the remaining material is a set of suffixes, since no prefix occurs in the data. Exercise 2 shifts to Kreyòl, where each noun is paired with its definite form, and asks for a generalization about the allomorphs of the article and a decision about whether the allomorphy is lexically or phonologically conditioned.","zh":"练习一给出十六个用国际音标转写的土耳其语词，要求列出每个语素并写出其释义词或语法功能，说明它是词根、前缀还是后缀，最后据此构造表示“在我们的小手里”的说法。该组数据的词根有 deniz（海）、el（手）、ev（房）、diʃ（牙），其余材料都是后缀，数据中未出现任何前缀。练习二转向克里奥尔语，每个名词都配以带定冠词的形式，要求就冠词各语素变体出现的环境作出概括，并判断这种语素变体是词汇条件制约还是语音条件制约。"},{"en":"Exercise 3 gives eight English words and asks which affixes each contains, whether each affix is derivational or inflectional, and, for the inflectional ones, what grammatical information they carry. Exercise 4 looks at a highlighted word in each of ten sentences, asking learners to identify its category and to state the criteria used. For every morphologically complex word they must also identify the root, list the affixes, and work out each affix's selectional requirement together with the change it makes to the category or meaning of its base. Exercise 5, marked Advanced, asks whether conceive, receive, perceive, and deceive are morphologically simple or complex, and to justify the answer and weigh any opposing evidence.","zh":"练习三给出八个英语词，要求指出其中包含哪些词缀、每个词缀属派生还是屈折，并对屈折词缀说明其表达的语法信息。练习四给出十个句子，要求判断句中加粗词的词类并说明所用判定标准；对其中形态复杂的词，还要找出词根、列出全部词缀，并说明每个词缀的选择限制以及它给词基的词类或意义带来的变化。练习五标为进阶，要求讨论 conceive、receive、perceive、deceive 是形态简单词还是形态复杂词，并给出理由、权衡可能存在的反证。"},{"en":"Exercise 6 turns to compounding: English compounds may be written solid, as in redhead and greenhouse, spaced, as in ice cream and ski boots, or hyphenated, as in gluten-free and long-term, and learners must pick the compounds out of four sentences quoted from a novel. Exercise 7 presents Hebrew compounds, among them beyt xolim 'hospital', batey sefer 'schools', and yom huledet 'birthday', and asks which categories of roots can compound and whether Hebrew compounds are left-headed or right-headed. Both exercises close with footnotes giving the source of the sentence data and of the Hebrew examples.","zh":"练习六讨论复合：英语复合词有的连写，如 redhead、greenhouse；有的分写，如 ice cream、ski boots；有的用连字符，如 gluten-free、long-term。学习者须从引自一部小说的四个句子中挑出全部复合词。练习七给出希伯来语复合词，如 beyt xolim（医院）、batey sefer（学校）、yom huledet（生日），要求判断哪些类别的词根可以参与复合，以及希伯来语复合词是左中心还是右中心。两个练习都以脚注收尾，分别注明小说语句与希伯来语例证的出处。"}]},"part-006-chapter-6-syntax":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 6: Syntax","zh":"第 6 章：句法"},"summary":{"en":"This chapter moves from the internal structure of words to the way words are organized into phrases and sentences, the area of linguistics known as syntax. It states the chapter's learning goals: using constituency tests to identify phrases, classifying words by distribution, relating grammatically connected sentences, and drawing tree diagrams. An alternative reading path interleaves core concepts with tree diagrams and X-bar theory.","zh":"本章从词的内部结构转向词如何组织成短语和句子，这一领域在语言学中称为句法。开篇列出本章的学习目标：运用成分测试识别短语、依据分布给词分类、辨认语法上相互关联的句子，以及绘制树形图。章首还提供了一条把核心概念与树形图、X 杠理论交叉安排的替代阅读路径。"},"points":[{"en":"Syntax studies how words are organized into phrases and sentences, which have hierarchical structure rather than being mere sequences.","zh":"句法研究词如何组织成短语和句子，这些单位具有层级结构，而不只是单纯的线性序列。"},{"en":"Just as a word contains a head morpheme, every phrase can be shown to have a syntactic head.","zh":"正如词含有中心语素，每个短语也都可以证明拥有一个句法上的中心语。"},{"en":"Constituency tests provide the evidence used to identify which phrases are present within a sentence.","zh":"成分测试提供证据，用来判定一个句子内部包含哪些短语。"},{"en":"Words are sorted into lexical and functional categories on the basis of their distribution.","zh":"词依据其在句中的分布，被划分为词汇类与功能类两大类。"},{"en":"Core concepts and argumentation come in 6.1 to 6.12, while tree diagrams and X-bar theory come in 6.13 to 6.21.","zh":"核心概念与论证安排在 6.1 至 6.12，树形图与 X 杠理论则安排在 6.13 至 6.21。"}],"terms":[{"en":"syntax","zh":"句法","defEn":"The study of how words are organized into phrases and sentences.","defZh":"研究词如何组织成短语和句子、并揭示其层级结构的语言学分支。"},{"en":"constituency test","zh":"成分测试","defEn":"A diagnostic that provides evidence for identifying the phrases making up a sentence.","defZh":"通过换位、替换、省略等手段，为判定句子由哪些短语构成提供证据的测试方法。"},{"en":"tree diagram","zh":"树形图","defEn":"A visual representation of the structural analysis of a sentence.","defZh":"用分层的节点与连线呈现句子结构分析结果的图形表示。"},{"en":"X-bar theory","zh":"X 杠理论","defEn":"A formalization of phrase structure presented in the second half of the chapter.","defZh":"本章后半部分用以刻画短语结构、区分指示语与附加语等形式化理论。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"Chapter 5 examined the internal structure of words. This chapter turns to a larger unit of organization: how words are arranged into phrases and sentences, which linguists call syntax. The guiding idea is that a sentence is not merely a string of words in sequence but has a hierarchical structure, much as a word is built from organized morphemes. Just as every word has a head morpheme, every phrase can be shown to have a syntactic head.","zh":"第 5 章考察了词的内部结构，本章则转向更大的组织单位：词如何组合成短语和句子，语言学家称之为句法。核心观点是，句子并不只是一串按顺序排列的词，而是具有层级结构，正如词由有组织的语素构成一样。正像每个词都有中心语素，每个短语也都可以证明有一个句法上的中心语。"},{"en":"The stated learning goals are to use constituency tests as evidence for identifying the phrases inside a sentence, to sort words into lexical and functional categories according to their distribution, to recognize relationships among grammatically related sentences such as active and passive or statements and questions, and to draw tree diagrams for English sentences. The chapter is organized so that core concepts and argumentation come first, in 6.1 to 6.12, and tree diagrams with X-bar theory come second, in 6.13 to 6.21; an interleaved reading order is offered for courses that prefer to combine the two from the start. Appendix 1 offers an alternative formalization that uses phrase structure rules instead of X-bar theory.","zh":"本章列出的学习目标包括：运用成分测试所提供的证据识别句子中的短语；依据分布把词归入词汇类与功能类；辨认语法上相互关联的句子之间的关系，如主动与被动、陈述与疑问；为英语句子绘制树形图。全章在编排上把核心概念与论证放在前半部分，即 6.1 至 6.12，把树形图与 X 杠理论放在后半部分，即 6.13 至 6.21；对于希望一开始就把两者结合起来的课程，书中还给出了一种交叉式的阅读顺序。附录 1 还提供了另一种形式化方式，即用短语结构规则代替 X 杠理论。"}]},"chapter-052-what-we-know-when-we-know-the-syntax-of-a-language":{"title":{"en":"6.1 Syntactic knowledge and grammaticality judgements","zh":"6.1 句法知识与合乎语法性判断"},"summary":{"en":"Syntax studies how words are organized into phrases and sentences, which have hierarchical structure rather than being mere strings of words. Speakers can judge whether novel sentences such as All grypnos are tichek. fit the patterns of their internal grammar, and these grammaticality judgements reveal the limits on sentence building. The goals of syntactic theory are to predict which sentences are grammatical and to explain the properties of grammatical sentences, since a language is not a finite list.","zh":"句法研究词如何组织成短语和句子，而句子具有层级结构，并非单纯的词串。说话人能够判断像 All grypnos are tichek. 这样的新句子是否符合其内在语法的模式，这类合乎语法性判断揭示了造句所受的限制。句法理论的目标是预测哪些句子合乎语法，并解释合乎语法的句子所具有的性质，因为语言并不是一份有限的句子清单。"},"points":[{"en":"Syntax is the study of how words are organized into phrases and sentences, which have hierarchical structure.","zh":"句法研究词如何组织成短语和句子，而句子具有层级结构。"},{"en":"Just as a word has a head morpheme, every phrase has an element that is its syntactic head.","zh":"正如词有中心语素，每个短语也都有一个充当句法中心语的成分。"},{"en":"Grammaticality judgements come from individual language users, never from a language as a whole.","zh":"合乎语法性判断来自个别的语言使用者，而不可能来自作为整体的某种语言。"},{"en":"Ungrammatical examples are marked with an asterisk, and semantically odd but grammatical ones with a hashmark.","zh":"不合乎语法的例子用星号标示，合乎语法但语义怪异的例子则用井号标示。"},{"en":"Syntactic theory aims to predict which sentences are grammatical and to explain the properties of grammatical sentences.","zh":"句法理论旨在预测哪些句子合乎语法，并解释合乎语法的句子所具有的性质。"},{"en":"Knowledge of syntax cannot be a mere list, because speakers generate and understand sentences they have never encountered.","zh":"句法知识不可能只是一份清单，因为说话人能生成并理解从未遇到过的句子。"}],"terms":[{"en":"syntax","zh":"句法","defEn":"The study of how words are organized into phrases and sentences.","defZh":"研究词如何组织成短语和句子、并揭示其层级结构的语言学分支。"},{"en":"grammaticality judgement","zh":"合乎语法性判断","defEn":"A language user's evaluation of whether a sentence is grammatical.","defZh":"语言使用者对某个句子是否符合其内在语法所作的评价，只能来自个人。"},{"en":"grammatical","zh":"合乎语法的","defEn":"Describes a sentence that matches the patterns of a user's internal grammar.","defZh":"指符合某一语言使用者内在语法模式的句子，通常不加任何标记。"},{"en":"ungrammatical","zh":"不合乎语法的","defEn":"Describes a sentence inconsistent with the grammatical system of a language user.","defZh":"指与某一语言使用者的语法系统不一致的句子，语言学中用星号标示。"},{"en":"generativity","zh":"生成性","defEn":"The property by which a grammar generalizes to produce and understand novel sentences.","defZh":"语法能够推广到新情形，从而生成并理解前所未见的句子的特性。"}],"examples":[{"text":"All grypnos are tichek.","noteEn":"Made-up words arranged in an order that still fits the patterns of English.","noteZh":"由生造词构成，但排列顺序仍符合英语模式的句子。"},{"text":"*Grypnos tichek all are.","noteEn":"The same invented words in an order that does not fit English; the star marks ungrammaticality.","noteZh":"同样的生造词以不符合英语的顺序排列；星号标示其不合乎语法。"},{"text":"#The book pedalled the ladder harmoniously.","noteEn":"Well formed for English but semantically odd, which the hashmark indicates.","noteZh":"结构上合乎英语，但语义怪异，井号正表示这一点。"}],"body":[{"en":"Syntax is the branch of linguistics that asks how words are organized into phrases and sentences. Like the morphemes inside a word, the words in a sentence are best thought of as having a hierarchical structure rather than forming a simple string, and each phrase, like each word, contains a syntactic head. Example (1), All grypnos are tichek., is built from invented words, yet it has the right shape for English, whereas *Grypnos tichek all are. does not. Since speakers have never heard either sentence, their internal grammar must generalize to new cases; this is the generativity of language.","zh":"句法是语言学中研究词如何组织成短语和句子的分支。如同词内部的语素，句子中的词最好也被看作具有层级结构，而不是构成一个简单的词串；并且和词一样，每个短语都含有句法上的中心语。例（1）All grypnos are tichek. 由生造词构成，却仍然具备英语应有的形式，而 *Grypnos tichek all are. 则不然。既然说话人从未听到过这两个句子，其内在语法就必然能够推广到新的情形，这就是语言的生成性。"},{"en":"A language user's evaluation of a sentence is a grammaticality judgement. Sentences that match the patterns of that user's internal grammar are grammatical; those that do not are ungrammatical. Calling something ungrammatical does not mean it breaks a schoolroom rule, only that it is inconsistent with a speaker's grammatical system. Judgements belong to individual speakers rather than to a language as a whole, though saying something is ungrammatical in English is usually shorthand for general agreement among its users. Ungrammatical examples take an asterisk, and sentences that are grammatical but semantically odd take a hashmark.","zh":"语言使用者对句子所作的评价就是合乎语法性判断。符合该使用者内在语法模式的句子是合乎语法的，不符合的则是不合乎语法的。说不合乎语法，并不是指它违反了课堂上教的规则，而只是指它与说话人的语法系统不一致。判断属于个别的说话人，而不属于作为整体的某种语言；不过说某句在英语中不合乎语法，通常只是表示英语使用者对此大体有一致看法。不合乎语法的例子前加星号，合乎语法但语义怪异的句子前加井号。"},{"en":"Syntactic theory has two goals: to predict which sentences are grammatical and which are not, and to explain the observed properties of grammatical sentences. Much of the chapter uses varieties of English, but other languages reveal the scope of syntactic variation, and the eventual aim is a theory of all human languages. A mere list of grammatical sentences would not suffice, since speakers can produce and understand sentences that no one has encountered before.","zh":"句法理论有两个目标：预测哪些句子合乎语法、哪些不合乎语法，并解释合乎语法的句子所呈现的性质。本章大部分内容讨论英语的各种变体，但其他语言展示了句法变异的范围，最终目标则是建立一种适用于所有人类语言的理论。仅仅列出合乎语法的句子是不够的，因为说话人能够生成并理解任何人都未曾遇到过的句子。"}]},"chapter-053-a-starting-point-word-order":{"title":{"en":"6.2 Word order","zh":"6.2 词序"},"summary":{"en":"Word order is one of the most obvious properties of a sentence and is central to English. The grammatical All grypnos are tichek. and the ungrammatical *Grypnos tichek all are. differ only in the order of their words. English statements require the verb to follow at least one noun, giving the pattern N V (N), and English is Subject-Verb-Object, an order reported in about 35.5% of the world's languages, while Subject-Object-Verb is the most common at 41%.","zh":"词序是句子最明显的特征之一，在英语中尤为重要。合乎语法的 All grypnos are tichek. 与不合乎语法的 *Grypnos tichek all are. 之间只有词序之别。英语陈述句要求动词位于至少一个名词之后，形成 N V（N）的模式；英语属于主—动—宾（SVO）语言，约 35.5% 的世界语言采用该词序，而主—宾—动（SOV）以 41% 最为常见。"},"points":[{"en":"English has relatively fixed word order, so rearranging words usually changes the meaning or yields an ungrammatical sentence.","zh":"英语词序相对固定，因此调换词序通常会改变意义或造成不合乎语法的句子。"},{"en":"In an English statement the verb must follow at least one noun and may be followed by a second: N V (N).","zh":"在英语陈述句中，动词必须位于至少一个名词之后，其后可以再跟一个名词，即 N V（N）。"},{"en":"Subjects almost always precede the predicate and control agreement on the verb, while direct objects usually follow it.","zh":"主语几乎总是位于谓语之前并决定动词的一致形式，直接宾语则通常位于动词之后。"},{"en":"Predicates are classified by transitivity: intransitive takes one argument, transitive two, and ditransitive three.","zh":"谓语按及物性分类：不及物谓语带一个论元，及物谓语带两个，双及物谓语带三个。"},{"en":"English is Subject-Verb-Object, and Subject-Object-Verb, at 41%, is the most common basic order in the world.","zh":"英语是主—动—宾语言；主—宾—动以 41% 成为世界上最常见的基本词序。"},{"en":"Languages with flexible order often use a strict topic-comment arrangement, where style, topic and focus determine placement.","zh":"词序灵活的语言常采用严格的话题—述题安排，由语体、话题与焦点决定成分位置。"}],"terms":[{"en":"basic word order","zh":"基本词序","defEn":"The order found in simple declarative clauses, without special emphasis or topic.","defZh":"在没有任何特殊强调或话题化的简单陈述小句中呈现的、作为默认值的词序。"},{"en":"subject","zh":"主语","defEn":"The argument that usually precedes the predicate and controls agreement on the verb.","defZh":"通常位于谓语之前、决定动词一致形式，且代词形式使用主格的论元。"},{"en":"direct object","zh":"直接宾语","defEn":"An argument that usually appears after the verb; pronominal objects take accusative case.","defZh":"通常出现在动词之后的论元；其代词形式使用宾格，如 me、us、him。"},{"en":"argument","zh":"论元","defEn":"A phrase corresponding to a participant or actor involved in the sentence's predicate.","defZh":"与句子谓语所涉及的参与者或行为者相对应的短语，多为名词短语。"},{"en":"transitivity","zh":"及物性（配价）","defEn":"The number of arguments that a predicate takes, also called its valency.","defZh":"谓语所带论元的数目，也称配价；据此分为不及物、及物与双及物。"},{"en":"topic and focus","zh":"话题与焦点","defEn":"The topic is what a sentence is about; the focus is what the speaker emphasizes.","defZh":"话题是句子所谈论的对象，焦点则是说话人想要强调或突出的内容。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Amal ate chocolate.","noteEn":"A grammatical English statement in which the verb follows the subject and precedes the object.","noteZh":"合乎语法的英语陈述句，动词位于主语之后、宾语之前。"},{"text":"*Amal chocolate ate.","noteEn":"The same words in a disallowed order, showing that the verb cannot come last here.","noteZh":"同样几个词以不被允许的顺序排列，说明此处动词不能位于句末。"},{"text":"Chocolate ate Amal.","noteEn":"Grammatical English with an implausible meaning; it cannot mean the same as Amal ate chocolate.","noteZh":"合乎语法但意义不合常理；它无法表达与 Amal ate chocolate. 相同的意思。"},{"text":"[ Danai laughed ] and [ Seo-yeon cried ]","noteEn":"A compound sentence in which two clauses are linked by the conjunction and.","noteZh":"由并列连词 and 连接两个小句而成的复合句。"}],"body":[{"en":"Word order is one of the most obvious properties of a sentence, and for English it carries great weight: the grammatical All grypnos are tichek. and the ungrammatical *Grypnos tichek all are. differ only in word order. English has relatively fixed order, and changing it usually alters the meaning or makes a sentence ungrammatical. French, Chatino and Choktaw are also relatively fixed, while Latin, Anishinaabemowin, Kanien'kéha and ASL permit much more flexible order, where style, topic and focus shape the arrangement.","zh":"词序是句子最明显的特征之一，在英语中尤其重要：合乎语法的 All grypnos are tichek. 与不合乎语法的 *Grypnos tichek all are. 之间只有词序之别。英语的词序相对固定，改动词序通常会改变意义或使句子不合乎语法。法语、查蒂诺语与乔克托语的词序也相对固定，而拉丁语、阿尼什纳贝语、卡尼恩凯哈语与美国手语则容许灵活得多的词序，其排列方式由语体、话题与焦点决定。"},{"en":"Grammatical examples like Amal ate chocolate. and ungrammatical ones like *Amal chocolate ate. show that the verb cannot be first in an English statement. Since the verb does come last in Daffodils bloom. and Eagles fly., the most accurate generalization is that the verb must follow at least one noun and may be followed by a second: N V (N). Word order is also sensitive to grammatical function, since it is the subject that precedes the verb and the object that follows it; Chocolate ate Amal. therefore cannot mean the same as Amal ate chocolate.","zh":"像 Amal ate chocolate. 这样的合乎语法例句和 *Amal chocolate ate. 这样的不合乎语法例句表明，英语陈述句中的动词不能位于句首。由于动词在 Daffodils bloom. 和 Eagles fly. 中确实位于句末，最准确的概括应是：动词必须跟在至少一个名词之后，其后可以再跟一个名词，即 N V（N）。词序还与语法功能相关，位于动词之前的是主语，位于其后的是宾语；因此 Chocolate ate Amal. 不能表达与 Amal ate chocolate. 相同的意思。"},{"en":"Predicates are classified by transitivity, the number of arguments they take: intransitive predicates take one argument, transitive two, and ditransitive three. Arguments, the phrases naming participants in the event, are usually noun phrases but may also be prepositional phrases or whole clauses. Subjects almost always precede the predicate and control agreement, direct objects usually follow the verb, and with a ditransitive the indirect object is often the recipient. English is Subject-Verb-Object, an order Dryer (2013) reports in about 35.5% of languages; Subject-Object-Verb is the most common at 41%, and every logically possible order is attested somewhere.","zh":"谓语按及物性分类，即按其所能带论元的数目分类：不及物谓语带一个论元，及物谓语带两个，双及物谓语带三个。论元是指称事件参与者的短语，通常是名词短语，也可以是介词短语或整个小句。主语几乎总是位于谓语之前并决定一致形式，直接宾语通常位于动词之后，在双及物结构中间接宾语往往是接受者。英语是主—动—宾语言，据 Dryer（2013）报告，约 35.5% 的语言采用这一词序；主—宾—动以 41% 最为常见，而所有逻辑上可能的词序在世界语言中都确有实例。"}]},"chapter-054-phrases-structure-within-the-sentence":{"title":{"en":"6.3 Structure within the sentence: Phrases, heads, and selection","zh":"6.3 句子内部的结构：短语、中心语与选择"},"summary":{"en":"Human languages group words into constituents, and a phrase is a set of words that acts together as a unit. Within a phrase, the head determines the phrase's category and meaning, and it selects its complements. English places heads before complements while Japanese places them after, a property called head directionality. Phrases may also contain phrases of the same type, which is recursion.","zh":"所有人类语言都把词组合成句法成分，短语就是共同充当一个整体的一组词。短语中决定类别与意义的核心成分是中心语，中心语选择自己的补足语。英语的中心语位于补足语之前，日语则位于其后，这一属性称为中心语方向性。短语内部还可以包含同类型的短语，这种现象称为递归。"},"points":[{"en":"A phrase is a set of words that act together as a single unit.","zh":"短语是指在句子中共同起作用、充当一个整体单位的一组词。"},{"en":"The head is the most important word: it determines the phrase's category and core meaning.","zh":"中心语是短语中最重要的词，它决定整个短语的类别和核心意义。"},{"en":"Heads select their complements, deciding whether a complement is required and what category it must be.","zh":"中心语会对其补足语进行选择，决定补足语是否必需以及必须属于什么类别。"},{"en":"English heads precede their complements, whereas Japanese heads follow them; this is head directionality.","zh":"英语的中心语位于补足语之前，日语的中心语则位于其后，这就是中心语方向性。"},{"en":"Recursion allows a phrase to contain another phrase of the same type, as in these videos of a baby panda.","zh":"递归使短语能够包含另一个同类型短语，如 these videos of a baby panda 所示。"},{"en":"Headedness and phrasing rather than single words are what syntactic generalizations are really about.","zh":"句法概括针对的是短语而非孤立的单词，中心语性质对所有语言都至关重要。"}],"terms":[{"en":"head","zh":"中心语","defEn":"The most important word in a phrase, which determines the phrase's category.","defZh":"短语中最重要的词，决定整个短语的类别和意义，并决定该短语在句中的位置。"},{"en":"complement","zh":"补足语","defEn":"An element selected by a head, such as the object of a verb.","defZh":"由中心语选择的成分，如动词的宾语；中心语决定它是否必需以及类别。"},{"en":"selection","zh":"选择","defEn":"The property of heads that determines which complements they allow.","defZh":"中心语的性质，决定它允许哪些补足语，以及补足语是否必需、属于何种类别。"},{"en":"recursion","zh":"递归","defEn":"The ability of a structure to contain another structure of the same type.","defZh":"某一结构可以在自身内部包含另一个同类型结构的能力，是自然语言语法的关键属性。"},{"en":"head directionality","zh":"中心语方向性","defEn":"Whether a language places heads before or after their complements.","defZh":"一种语言把中心语放在补足语之前还是之后的属性，分为中心语前置和中心语后置。"},{"en":"noun phrase","zh":"名词短语","defEn":"A group of words whose head is a noun and which acts as a unit.","defZh":"以名词为中心语、在句中作为一个整体起作用的一组词，如 all kittens。"}],"examples":[{"text":"All kittens are very cute.","noteEn":"The group all kittens can be replaced by other plural noun phrases.","noteZh":"all kittens 这一组词可以被其他含复数名词的名词短语替换。"},{"text":"The ducklings that I saw earlier are very cute.","noteEn":"A longer group of words can occupy the same subject position.","noteZh":"更长的词组同样可以出现在句首主语的位置上。"},{"text":"*That I saw earlier is very cute.","noteEn":"It contains a pronoun but is not a noun phrase, so it cannot be subject.","noteZh":"虽含有代词 I，但不是名词短语，因此不能充当主语。"},{"text":"Watasi-wa ringo-o tabe-ta.","noteEn":"Japanese example meaning 'I ate (an) apple', with the verb final.","noteZh":"日语例，意为“我吃了一个苹果”，动词位于句末，体现中心语后置。"}],"body":[{"en":"Human languages group words into constituents, and grammaticality judgements refer to phrases in structural positions, not to notions like the fourth word of a sentence. A phrase is a set of words that act together as a unit. In All kittens are very cute, the string all kittens can be replaced by Puppies, the ducklings that I saw earlier, or these videos of a baby panda. What the replacements share is a plural noun; with the puppy, are becomes ungrammatical, though is is good.","zh":"人类语言在词序之外还会把词组合成句法成分，语法性判断针对的是处于特定结构位置的短语，而不是“句中第四个词”这类纯线性的属性。短语是一组共同充当一个单位的词。在 All kittens are very cute 中，all kittens 这一串词可以被 Puppies、the ducklings that I saw earlier 或 these videos of a baby panda 替换。这些替换形式都含有复数名词；若换成单数名词 the puppy，句子与 are 连用就不合语法，但改用 is 又恢复合法。"},{"en":"Merely containing a noun is not enough: strings like that I saw earlier and of a baby panda cannot be subjects, even though they contain a pronoun or a compound noun. A noun phrase is a group of words in which the noun is the most important element, determining part of the meaning and the category of the whole phrase, which fixes where the phrase can go. That noun is the head, the same headedness seen in compounds, applied to words in a phrase.","zh":"仅仅含有名词还不够：that I saw earlier 和 of a baby panda 虽然含有代词或复合名词，却不能充当主语。名词短语是这样一组词，其中名词是最重要的成分，它既决定意义的重要部分，也决定整个短语的类别，从而决定该短语在句中能出现的位置。这个名词就是中心语，其性质与复合词中的中心语相同，只是应用于短语中的词而非词中的语素。"},{"en":"Heads also determine what else may appear in the phrase, in particular whether it contains an object. Verbs differ in transitivity; each verb has an opinion about how many objects it allows, whereas no verb cares whether it is modified by an adverb. The term is selection: heads select their objects, and for non-verbal heads the more general term complement is used. Phrases may contain phrases of the same type, as these videos of a baby panda contains a baby panda; this is recursion.","zh":"中心语还决定短语中还能出现什么成分，特别是决定短语是否包含宾语。动词的及物性各不相同，每个动词都“在意”自己能带几个宾语，而没有任何动词在意是否被副词修饰。这一属性称为选择：中心语选择自己的宾语；对非动词中心语，通常用更一般的术语“补足语”。英语名词从不要求补足语，但一旦带补足语，几乎总是小句或介词短语。短语可以包含同类型的短语，如 these videos of a baby panda 中含有 a baby panda，这就是递归。"},{"en":"Languages vary in whether heads precede or follow their complements. English is head-initial: verbs precede objects, prepositions precede noun phrase complements, and nouns precede prepositional phrase complements. Japanese is an SOV, head-final language, as in Watasi-wa ringo-o tabe-ta, Tokyo e, and robotto no shasin. Japanese e is a postposition, and adposition is the general term covering both types.","zh":"语言在中心语位于补足语之前还是之后这一点上存在差异。英语是中心语前置语言：动词在宾语前，介词在名词短语补足语前，名词在介词短语补足语前。日语是 SOV 的中心语后置语言，如 Watasi-wa ringo-o tabe-ta、Tokyo e 和 robotto no shasin。日语的 e 是后置词，介词与后置词合称 adposition。这一属性称为中心语方向性。"}]},"chapter-055-identifying-phrases-constituency-tests":{"title":{"en":"6.4 Identifying phrases: Constituency tests","zh":"6.4 识别短语：成分测试"},"summary":{"en":"A constituent is any group of words that acts together as a unit inside a sentence. Since the mental grammar cannot be observed directly, linguists rely on grammaticality judgements and constituency tests as evidence. This section presents four types of test — replacement, movement, it-clefts, and answers to questions — and explains why the coordination test is unreliable, because constructions such as Right Node Raising join non-constituents.","zh":"句法成分是在句子内部共同充当一个单位的任何一组词。由于无法直接观察心理语法，语言学家只能借助合乎语法性判断和成分测试来寻找证据。本节介绍四类测试：替换测试、移位测试、it 分裂句以及问句回答；并说明并列测试并不可靠，因为像右节点提升这样的结构会把并非成分的词组并列起来。"},"points":[{"en":"A constituent is any group of words that acts together as a unit within a sentence.","zh":"句法成分是指在句子内部共同起作用、充当一个单位的任何一组词。"},{"en":"Replacement tests substitute a pronoun, do (too), then or there for the string, and are category-specific.","zh":"替换测试用代词、do (too)、then 或 there 替换待测词组，且替换词与类别对应。"},{"en":"If a string can be moved elsewhere and the sentence stays grammatical, it is a constituent.","zh":"若一串词移到句中别处后句子仍然合乎语法，那么它就是句法成分。"},{"en":"Clefts place a string in the frame It was X that Y, where non-constituents give ungrammatical results.","zh":"分裂句把待测词组放进 It was X that Y 框架，非成分会使句子不合语法。"},{"en":"Constituents can often stand alone as answers, and passing two tests is usually enough.","zh":"成分通常可以单独充当问句的回答；一般通过两项测试即可确认。"},{"en":"The coordination test is unreliable because Right Node Raising coordinates strings that are not constituents.","zh":"并列测试并不可靠，因为右节点提升会把并非成分的词组并列起来。"}],"terms":[{"en":"constituent","zh":"句法成分","defEn":"Any group of words that acts together as a unit in a sentence.","defZh":"在句子内部共同起作用、充当一个单位的任何一组词，是句法的核心概念之一。"},{"en":"constituency test","zh":"成分测试","defEn":"A diagnostic, such as replacement or movement, that shows whether a string is a constituent.","defZh":"用来检验一串词是否为句法成分的诊断方法，如替换测试、移位测试等。"},{"en":"replacement test","zh":"替换测试","defEn":"Replacing a string with a pronoun, do, then or there to test constituency.","defZh":"用代词、do (too)、then 或 there 替换待测词组，以检验其是否为成分的测试。"},{"en":"cleft construction","zh":"分裂结构","defEn":"A sentence of the form It is or It was X that Y, used to test constituency.","defZh":"形式为 It is/was X that Y 的句式，把待测词组置于 X 位置以检验成分。"},{"en":"coordination","zh":"并列","defEn":"Joining two elements with a coordinator such as and or but.","defZh":"用 and、but 等并列连词把两个成分连接起来，被连接的成分称为并列项。"},{"en":"Right Node Raising","zh":"右节点提升","defEn":"A construction in which coordinated clauses seem to share a following object.","defZh":"两个并列的小句或动词短语似乎共同拥有其后一个宾语的结构，会使并列项并非成分。"}],"examples":[{"text":"The students saw it after class.","noteEn":"Replacing a movie with it is grammatical, so a movie is a noun phrase here.","noteZh":"用 it 替换 a movie 后句子合法，说明此处 a movie 是名词短语。"},{"text":"At that strange little shop Nimra bought a scarf.","noteEn":"Moving the prepositional phrase to the front still yields a grammatical sentence.","noteZh":"把介词短语移到句首后句子依然合乎语法，说明它是句法成分。"},{"text":"It was a movie about dinosaurs that the students saw.","noteEn":"A cleft showing that the whole noun phrase is a constituent.","noteZh":"分裂句测试表明整个名词短语 a movie about dinosaurs 是一个成分。"},{"text":"Rathna's brother baked these delicious cookies.","noteEn":"Used for cleft and question-answer tests, as in Who baked these delicious cookies?","noteZh":"用于分裂句与问句回答测试，可回答 Who baked... 这样的问句。"}],"body":[{"en":"Constituency, along with headedness, is one of the central concepts of syntax. Calling a string of words a phrase amounts to claiming that language users represent it as a unit in their mental grammar. The technical term for such a unit is constituent: any group of words that acts together within a sentence. Since the mental grammar cannot be observed directly, we need evidence from grammaticality judgements and a few simple tests: replacement, movement, it-clefts, and answers to questions. A coordination test is often introduced too, but it is not always reliable.","zh":"成分性与中心语性质一样，是句法的核心概念之一。把一串词称为短语，就等于主张语言使用者在心理语法中把它表征为一个单位。这样的单位在术语上称为句法成分，即在句子内部共同起作用的任何一组词。由于无法直接观察心理语法，我们需要证据，而证据来自合乎语法性判断和几项简单测试：替换、移位、it 分裂句以及问句回答。许多教材还引入并列测试，但它并不总是可靠。"},{"en":"Replacement tests substitute a single word for the string under investigation. A noun phrase can be replaced by a pronoun such as it or they, a verb phrase by do or do too, some prepositional phrases by then or there, and adjective phrases by a known adjective such as happy. Replacement is category-specific, so the result both identifies a constituent and reveals its category. Both grammaticality and meaning must be checked: The students saw it about dinosaurs is unacceptable on the intended meaning, even though it is fine elsewhere.","zh":"替换测试用一个词替换待考察的词组。名词短语可以用 it、they 等代词替换，动词短语可以用 do 或 do too 替换；部分介词短语可以用 then 或 there 替换，形容词短语可以用 happy 这类已知形容词替换。替换与类别相关，因此测试结果既能确认成分，也能揭示其类别。关键在于同时考察合乎语法性和意义：The students saw it about dinosaurs 在别的情境中可以用，但在想表达的原意上不可接受。"},{"en":"Movement tests relocate a string, usually to the front of the sentence, and ask whether the result is grammatical and keeps the same meaning. Clefts place the string after It was and the rest of the sentence after that, as in It was a movie about dinosaurs that the students saw, while non-constituents fail these tests. To cleft a verb phrase, English requires a tense form of do in the original verb position.","zh":"移位测试把待测词组移到句中别处，通常是句首，然后判断新句子是否合乎语法且意义不变，如 At that strange little shop Nimra bought a scarf。分裂句把待测词组放在 It was 之后，把句子其余部分放在 that 之后，如 It was a movie about dinosaurs that the students saw。非成分无法通过这两类测试，例如 It was a movie that the students saw about dinosaurs。若要对动词短语作分裂，英语需要在原动词位置放一个带时的 do。"},{"en":"Constituents also tend to be grammatical as answers to questions: What did Rathna's brother bake? These delicious cookies. A result of a constituency test applies only to the specific sentence being tested, so a string that fails in one sentence may still be a constituent elsewhere. Passing two of the four tests is normally enough to be confident that a string is a constituent.","zh":"成分通常也能合法地充当问句的回答：What did Rathna's brother bake? These delicious cookies. 成分测试的结果只适用于所测试的那个具体句子，因此在某句中通不过测试的词组在别的句子里可能仍是成分。并非每个成分都能通过所有测试，但一般只要通过四项测试中的两项，就可以确信该词组是句法成分。"}]},"chapter-056-functional-categories":{"title":{"en":"6.5 Functional categories","zh":"6.5 功能语类"},"summary":{"en":"Not every word in a sentence belongs to a lexical category. Words such as the, will, in and very are functional categories, the grammatical glue that holds syntax together, and they typically carry purely grammatical meaning. This section describes determiners, pronouns, auxiliaries, prepositions and other functional categories, and explains why functional categories are closed classes, since new members are hard to add.","zh":"句子中并非每个词都属于词汇语类。the、will、in、very 这类词属于功能语类，是把句法黏合起来的语法黏合剂，通常只表达纯语法的意义。本节介绍限定词、代词、助动词、介词等功能语类，并说明功能语类是封闭类，因为很难为其增添新成员。"},"points":[{"en":"Functional categories are the grammatical glue of syntax and carry purely grammatical meaning.","zh":"功能语类是把句法黏合起来的语法黏合剂，通常表达纯语法的意义。"},{"en":"Determiners come first in noun phrases, only one is allowed, and they include articles, demonstratives and quantifiers.","zh":"限定词位于名词短语最前，只能出现一个，包括冠词、指示词和部分量词。"},{"en":"Auxiliaries accompany a main verb, show tense and agreement, and precede not and the subject in questions.","zh":"助动词与主要动词同现，携带时与一致，并出现在否定词和疑问句主语之前。"},{"en":"Modals occur only as auxiliaries, do not agree with the subject, and include will, can and must.","zh":"情态助动词只能作助动词，不与主语一致，包括 will、can、must 等。"},{"en":"Prepositions express locations or grammatical relations and almost always select a noun phrase complement.","zh":"介词表达处所或语法关系，几乎总是选择一个名词短语作补足语。"},{"en":"Functional categories are closed classes, though new pronouns such as neopronouns can still be added.","zh":"功能语类属于封闭类，但人们仍可以提出并使用新的代词，如新代词。"}],"terms":[{"en":"functional category","zh":"功能语类","defEn":"A category of words with mostly grammatical meaning, such as determiners and auxiliaries.","defZh":"主要表达语法意义的一类词，如限定词、助动词等，可看作把句法黏合起来的语法黏合剂。"},{"en":"determiner","zh":"限定词","defEn":"A functional category that occurs first in a noun phrase, only one per phrase.","defZh":"出现在名词短语最前位置的功能语类，每个短语只能有一个，包括冠词、指示词和部分量词。"},{"en":"auxiliary","zh":"助动词","defEn":"A verb-like element that shows tense or agreement and accompanies a main verb.","defZh":"与主要动词同现、可携带时与一致的功能语类，否定和疑问句中位置特殊。"},{"en":"modal auxiliary","zh":"情态助动词","defEn":"An auxiliary such as will or must that never agrees with the subject.","defZh":"will、can、must 等只能作助动词、且不与主语一致的一类助动词。"},{"en":"preposition","zh":"介词","defEn":"A functional element expressing location or grammatical relation, usually with a noun phrase complement.","defZh":"表达处所或语法关系、几乎总是带名词短语补足语的功能成分，可由程度词修饰。"},{"en":"closed class","zh":"封闭类","defEn":"A category that is hard to add new words to, unlike open lexical classes.","defZh":"很难增添新成员的语类，功能语类多属此类，与开放的词汇语类相对。"}],"examples":[{"text":"The spaceship will arrive in orbit very soon.","noteEn":"Contains the functional words the, will, in and very alongside lexical words.","noteZh":"句中除实词外，还含有 the、will、in、very 等功能词。"},{"text":"the three red books","noteEn":"An article precedes numbers and adjectives in the noun phrase.","noteZh":"冠词位于数词和形容词之前，出现在名词短语的最前位置。"},{"text":"The bears are dancing.","noteEn":"The auxiliary are appears after the subject and before the main verb.","noteZh":"助动词 are 位于主语之后、主要动词之前。"},{"text":"the cat of my friend from school","noteEn":"Possession can also be marked by a prepositional phrase after the noun.","noteZh":"所有关系也可由位于名词之后的介词短语表达。"}],"body":[{"en":"Although nouns, verbs, adjectives and adverbs are lexical categories, not all words in a sentence belong to them. In The spaceship will arrive in orbit very soon, spaceship is the head noun of the noun phrase the spaceship, arrive is a verb, orbit a noun and soon an adverb, but the, will, in and very are not lexical words at all: they belong to functional categories, the grammatical glue that holds syntax together. Lexical categories mostly describe things, states or events, while functional categories often have purely grammatical meaning or use.","zh":"名词、动词、形容词和副词属于词汇语类，但句子中并非所有词都属于这些类别。在 The spaceship will arrive in orbit very soon 中，spaceship 是名词短语 the spaceship 的中心名词，arrive 是动词，orbit 是名词，soon 是副词，而 the、will、in、very 都不是实词，它们属于功能语类，可以看作把句法黏合起来的语法黏合剂。词汇语类大多描写事物、状态或事件，功能语类则常常只有纯语法的意义或用途。"},{"en":"Determiners form one of the most important functional categories of this chapter. Articles, demonstratives such as this and those, and quantifiers such as every and most all occupy the same initial position in a noun phrase, occur only one at a time, and are in complementary distribution; possessors such as my and the possessive phrase a friend from school's behave the same way. The possessive marker 's attaches to a whole phrase rather than to the head noun, which makes it a clitic rather than an affix. Pronouns are a special functional category that can replace a whole noun phrase, though this textbook still treats them as nouns.","zh":"限定词是本章最重要的功能语类之一。冠词、this 和 those 等指示词、every 和 most 等量词都出现在名词短语的同一初始位置，且一次只能出现一个，彼此处于互补分布；my 以及 a friend from school's 这样的领属成分也遵循同样的分布。领属标记 's 附着在整个短语而非中心名词上，因此是附缀而不是词缀。代词是一类特殊的功能语类，可以替换整个名词短语，但本教材仍把它们归入名词。"},{"en":"Auxiliaries resemble verbs in showing tense and agreement, but they always occur with a lexical main verb. In English they follow the subject and precede the main verb, appear to the left of not in negatives, and are fronted in yes-no questions. Be, have and do can also be main verbs, while the modals will, can and must occur only as auxiliaries and never agree with the subject. Prepositions express locations or grammatical relations and almost always select a noun phrase complement. Functional categories are closed classes: coining a new noun is easy, but adding a new determiner is hard, though new pronouns can still be proposed.","zh":"助动词与动词相似，可以携带时和一致，但总是与实义主要动词同现。在英语中，助动词位于主语之后、主要动词之前，在否定句中出现在 not 左侧，在是非问句中移到句首。be、have、do 也可以用作主要动词；情态助动词 will、can、must 等则只能作助动词，且不与主语一致。介词表达处所或语法关系，几乎总是选择名词短语作补足语。功能语类属于封闭类：创造新名词很容易，增加新的限定词则很难，但人们仍会提出新的代词。"}]},"chapter-057-sentences-inside-sentences-embedded-clauses":{"title":{"en":"6.6 Clausal embedding","zh":"6.6 小句嵌入"},"summary":{"en":"Clauses can occur inside other clauses as embedded clauses, introduced by complementizers such as that, whether, if, and for, which head complementizer phrases. Because verbs select both the number and the category of their complements, they differ in which clause types they allow. Embedded clauses may be statements ([–Q]), questions ([+Q]), or nonfinite clauses such as I want ghosts to exist.","zh":"小句可以嵌入另一小句之中，构成嵌入小句，由 that、whether、if、for 等标句词引导，这些标句词投射出标句词短语。由于动词既要选择补足语的数量，也要选择补足语的范畴，不同动词允许的从句类型并不相同。嵌入小句可以是陈述（[–Q]）、疑问（[+Q]）或非限定小句，如 I want ghosts to exist。"},"points":[{"en":"A verb's complement may be a whole clause, and such a clause inside another clause is an embedded clause.","zh":"动词的补足语可以是一个完整小句，这种位于另一小句内部的小句称为嵌入小句。"},{"en":"Complementizers like that introduce embedded clauses and head complementizer phrases, identified by constituency tests.","zh":"that 一类标句词引导嵌入小句，并投射出标句词短语，其成分地位可由成分测试确认。"},{"en":"Verbs select the category as well as the number of complements: eat takes only NPs, talk rejects complementizer phrases.","zh":"动词既选择补足语的数量，也选择其范畴：eat 只接名词短语，talk 不接受标句词短语。"},{"en":"that and the silent complementizer introduce embedded statements and are [–Q]; whether and if introduce embedded questions and are [+Q].","zh":"that 与零形式标句词引导嵌入陈述句，属于 [–Q]；whether 和 if 引导嵌入疑问句，属于 [+Q]。"},{"en":"Other verbs embed complementizerless nonfinite clauses, and for may introduce them, yielding for to infinitives.","zh":"另一些动词嵌入无标句词的非限定小句，for 可以引导这类小句，形成 for to 不定式结构。"}],"terms":[{"en":"embedded clause","zh":"嵌入小句","defEn":"A clause that occurs inside another clause, typically as the complement of a verb.","defZh":"出现在另一个小句内部的小句，通常充当动词的补足语。"},{"en":"complementizer","zh":"标句词","defEn":"A functional category whose members introduce embedded clauses and turn them into complements of verbs.","defZh":"一种功能范畴，其成员引导嵌入小句，把小句变成动词的补足语。"},{"en":"complementizer phrase (CP)","zh":"标句词短语（CP）","defEn":"A phrase headed by a complementizer, such as that Samnang might leave.","defZh":"以标句词为中心语的短语，例如 that Samnang might leave。"},{"en":"recursion","zh":"递归","defEn":"The property that lets a clause contain another clause of the same general type.","defZh":"使一个小句能够包含另一同类小句的属性，是语言结构可无限扩展的基础。"},{"en":"nonfinite clause","zh":"非限定小句","defEn":"A clause whose verb lacks tense, appearing in English with the infinitive marker to.","defZh":"动词不携带时的小句，在英语中伴随不定式标记 to 出现。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Deniz said that [Samnang might leave].","noteEn":"The clause Samnang might leave occupies the object position, showing that a complement can be a clause.","noteZh":"小句 Samnang might leave 占据宾语位置，说明补足语本身可以是一个小句。"},{"text":"I know whether ghosts exist.","noteEn":"The verb know selects a CP headed by the question complementizer whether.","noteZh":"动词 know 选择由疑问标句词 whether 引导的标句词短语。"},{"text":"I prefer for my coffee to have milk in it.","noteEn":"Here for introduces a nonfinite clause containing an overt subject, my coffee.","noteZh":"此处 for 引导一个非限定小句，小句中含有显性主语 my coffee。"},{"text":"The newspaper reported that there was a demonstration yesterday.","noteEn":"This verb strongly prefers an overt that and is ungrammatical if that is omitted.","noteZh":"该动词强烈要求出现显性 that，若省略 that 则句子不合语法。"}],"body":[{"en":"Words group into constituents within a single clause, but the object of a verb can itself be a whole clause. In Deniz said that [Samnang might leave], the clause Samnang might leave appears exactly where the object something appears in Deniz said something. Replacement confirms that [said that Samnang might leave] is a verb phrase: Keiko said that Samnang might leave, and Deniz did too. A clause inside another clause is an embedded clause.","zh":"词语在单个小句内组合成句法成分，但动词的宾语本身可以是一个完整小句。在 Deniz said that Samnang might leave 中，嵌入小句占据的正是 Deniz said something 中宾语 something 的位置。替代测试也确认了这一点：did too 可以替代整个动词短语。这种位于另一小句内部的小句即嵌入小句。"},{"en":"The word that introduces the embedded clause; such words form a functional category, the complementizers, so named because they turn clauses into complements of verbs. They head complementizer phrases (CPs). Verbs select the category as well as the number of their complements: know takes this fact (noun phrase), about birds (prepositional phrase), or that birds can fly (CP), while eat permits only noun phrase complements and talk permits noun phrases and prepositional phrases but not CPs.","zh":"that 的作用是引导嵌入小句；具有这一功能的词构成功能范畴，即标句词，此名正源于它们把小句变为动词的补足语。标句词像其他中心语一样投射出标句词短语（CP）。动词既选择补足语的数量，也选择其范畴：know 可接 this fact（名词短语）、about birds（介词短语）或 that birds can fly（CP），而 eat 只允许名词短语补足语，talk 允许名词短语和介词短语，却不允许 CP。"},{"en":"Embedded clauses are not only statements. Besides that and the silent ∅, which mark embedded statements and are [–Q], English has the question complementizers whether and if, which are [+Q]. So know allows I know whether ghosts exist, believe allows only that or ∅, and wonder only whether or if. Quotation shows the contrast: They asked if ghosts exist reports the quoted question Do ghosts exist?","zh":"嵌入小句并不限于陈述句。除属于 [–Q]、引导嵌入陈述句的 that 与零形式 ∅ 之外，英语还有属于 [+Q] 的疑问标句词 whether 和 if。因此 know 允许 I know whether ghosts exist，believe 只允许 that 或 ∅，wonder 只允许 whether 或 if。引用测试显出差别：They asked if ghosts exist 转述的是引语中的疑问句 Do ghosts exist?"},{"en":"Other verbs embed clauses with no complementizer and a nonfinite verb: I want [ghosts to exist] is grammatical, but that or whether clauses are not. For many speakers for introduces nonfinite clauses (I prefer [for my coffee to have milk in it]), and some varieties yield for to infinitives like I was happy for to leave. Because prefer also allows I prefer [that cookies have chocolate chips], a verb may select a finite or a nonfinite clause.","zh":"另一些动词嵌入的是无标句词、动词为非限定形式的小句：I want ghosts to exist 合语法，带 that 或 whether 的小句则不合语法。对许多说话人而言，for 可引导非限定小句，如 I prefer for my coffee to have milk in it；某些变体还产生 for to 不定式，如 I was happy for to leave。由于 prefer 也允许 I prefer that cookies have chocolate chips，一个动词既可选定限定小句，也可选定非限定小句。"}]},"chapter-058-main-clause-yes-no-questions":{"title":{"en":"6.7 Main clause Yes-No questions","zh":"6.7 主句是非问句"},"summary":{"en":"English forms main clause Yes-No questions by Subject-Auxiliary Inversion, moving the auxiliary of the main clause, not of an embedded clause, before the subject. When no auxiliary is present, Do-Support inserts do, as in Do ghosts exist?. Questions may also be marked by intonation alone, and the section contrasts main clause questions, which ask, with embedded questions, which report.","zh":"英语通过主语—助动词倒装构成主句是非问句，移动的是主句的助动词，而非嵌入小句中的助动词，它被移到主语之前。当句中没有助动词时，do 支撑插入 do，如 Do ghosts exist?。疑问也可以只靠语调表示；本节还对比了真正发问的主句问句与表示转述的嵌入问句。"},"points":[{"en":"Yes-No questions are formed by moving the first auxiliary of the main clause before the subject.","zh":"是非问句通过把主句中的第一个助动词移到主语之前构成。"},{"en":"If an auxiliary sits inside the subject, it cannot move; only the main clause auxiliary can.","zh":"若助动词位于主语内部，它不能移位；只有主句的助动词才能前移。"},{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion is a transformation, a rule that reorders constituents and relates statements to questions.","zh":"主语—助动词倒装是一种转换，即通过重新排列句法成分把陈述句与疑问句关联起来的规则。"},{"en":"When a sentence lacks an auxiliary, Do-Support inserts do, as in Do ghosts exist? and Ghosts don't exist.","zh":"句子没有助动词时，do 支撑插入 do，如 Do ghosts exist? 与 Ghosts don't exist。"},{"en":"Yes-No questions can also be marked by question intonation alone, without any change in word order.","zh":"是非问句也可以只靠疑问语调标记，完全不改变词序。"}],"terms":[{"en":"Yes-No question","zh":"是非问句","defEn":"A question that can be answered with yes or no in a language like English.","defZh":"在英语一类语言中，可以用 yes 或 no 来回答的问句。"},{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion","zh":"主语—助动词倒装","defEn":"The process that moves the main clause auxiliary to a position before the subject.","defZh":"把主句助动词移到主语之前位置的句法过程，又称 Subject-Aux Inversion。"},{"en":"transformation","zh":"转换","defEn":"A rule that changes sentence structure predictably by reordering constituents.","defZh":"通过重新排列句法成分，以可预测的方式改变句子结构的规则。"},{"en":"Do-Support","zh":"do 支撑","defEn":"The rule that inserts the auxiliary do when a sentence requires an auxiliary but has none.","defZh":"当句子因语法需要助动词而本身又没有助动词时，插入助动词 do 的规则。"},{"en":"question intonation","zh":"疑问语调","defEn":"The rising melody that marks a question without any change in word order.","defZh":"一种不改变词序、仅凭句末上升语调来标记疑问的方式。"},{"en":"embedded question","zh":"嵌入疑问句","defEn":"A question inside another clause, which reports rather than performs a question.","defZh":"位于另一小句内部的疑问小句，用于转述而非真正发问。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Will [the information [that was shared]] _ surprise them?","noteEn":"Only the main clause auxiliary will can invert; the auxiliary was inside the subject cannot.","noteZh":"只有主句助动词 will 可以倒装；位于主语内部的助动词 was 不能前移。"},{"text":"Do ghosts exist?","noteEn":"Do-Support supplies the auxiliary do because the corresponding statement Ghosts exist has none.","noteZh":"由于相应的陈述句 Ghosts exist 没有助动词，do 支撑提供了助动词 do。"},{"text":"Ghosts don't exist.","noteEn":"Negation also requires an auxiliary, so do appears here as well.","noteZh":"否定同样需要助动词，因此这里也出现了 do。"},{"text":"Ghosts exist?","noteEn":"A Yes-No question marked by intonation alone, good for asking for repetition or showing surprise.","noteZh":"仅靠语调标记的是非问句，适合请对方重复或表示惊讶。"}],"body":[{"en":"Yes-No questions can be answered with yes or no. English forms them by moving the first auxiliary of the main clause to the front of the sentence, before the subject: It will rain becomes Will it rain?, and They have left becomes Have they left yet?. This is Subject-Auxiliary Inversion. Only an auxiliary of the main clause moves: in [The information [that was shared]] will surprise them, was belongs to the subject, so only Will [the information [that was shared]] _ surprise them? is grammatical.","zh":"是非问句可以用 yes 或 no 回答。英语把主句的第一个助动词移到句首、即主语之前：It will rain 变成 Will it rain?，They have left 变成 Have they left yet?。此过程称主语—助动词倒装。只有主句的助动词才能移位：在 [The information [that was shared]] will surprise them 中，was 属于主语，故只有 Will [the information [that was shared]] _ surprise them? 合语法。"},{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion is a transformation: a rule that changes sentence structure in a predictable way by reordering constituents and relates one set of sentences to another. Current theory often describes transformations as movement. Theories differ over whether transformations are real operations in a speaker's mental grammar or only generalizations. Tellingly, no human language moves the first auxiliary encountered to form questions, which suggests that structure and constituency, not linear order, are fundamental.","zh":"主语—助动词倒装是一种转换：它通过重新排列句法成分、以可预测的方式改变句子结构，把一组句子与另一组句子关联起来。当代句法理论常把转换描写为移位。各家理论的分歧在于：转换究竟是说话人心理语法中真实运作的操作，还是仅仅是对陈述与疑问关系的概括。值得注意的是，没有任何人类语言通过移动碰到的第一个助动词来构成疑问句，这说明对语法而言，结构与成分关系而非线性词序才是根本的。"},{"en":"When a sentence has no auxiliary, English supplies one: Ghosts exist becomes Do ghosts exist?, and the same do is needed for negation, since Ghosts don't exist is grammatical while forms like Ghostsn't exist are not. This rule is Do-Support. If an auxiliary is already present, do cannot be added, so *They don't have left and *Don't they have left? are ungrammatical alongside They haven't left.","zh":"当句子没有助动词时，英语会补出一个：Ghosts exist 变成 Do ghosts exist?；否定句同样需要 do，因为 Ghosts don't exist 合语法，Ghostsn't exist 一类形式则不合。这条规则即 do 支撑。若句中已有助动词，就不能再添加 do，所以 *They don't have left 和 *Don't they have left? 都不合语法，而 They haven't left 合语法。"},{"en":"Yes-No questions may also be formed with no change in word order, using question intonation: Ghosts exist? alongside Do ghosts exist?. These are more restricted and suit contexts of asking someone to repeat themselves or expressing surprise. Main clause questions really ask for information and take a question mark, while embedded questions like They asked if I like chocolate report what someone said and take none. The two combine in Should they know whether ghosts exist?.","zh":"是非问句也可以完全不改变词序，仅靠疑问语调构成：Ghosts exist? 与 Do ghosts exist? 并存。这类问句限制较多，适合请对方重复或表达惊讶。主句问句真正提问、寻求信息，句末用问号；They asked if I like chocolate 这样的嵌入问句只是转述他人所说的话，句末不用问号。二者可合并，见于 Should they know whether ghosts exist?。"}]},"chapter-059-main-clause-content-questions":{"title":{"en":"6.8 Main clause content questions","zh":"6.8 主句内容疑问句"},"summary":{"en":"Content questions ask for specific information rather than yes or no. In English the content question word must appear at the beginning of the clause (Question Word Fronting) and Subject-Auxiliary Inversion applies as in Yes-No questions. Leaving the question word in-situ yields echo questions, and many other languages use question particles or leave question words in place.","zh":"内容疑问句问的是具体信息，而不是用 yes 或 no 作答。在英语中，疑问词必须出现在小句开头（疑问词前置），同时像是非问句一样发生主语—助动词倒装。疑问词留在原位则形成回声问句；许多其他语言则使用疑问助词，或让疑问词留在原位。"},"points":[{"en":"Content questions ask for specific information, such as time or location, rather than a yes or no answer.","zh":"内容疑问句问的是时间、地点一类具体信息，而不是要求 yes 或 no 的回答。"},{"en":"All languages can ask content questions, even if their question words do not share an initial sound.","zh":"所有语言都能提出内容疑问，即使其疑问词并不共享同一个起始音。"},{"en":"A content question word or the phrase it heads must appear at the beginning of the clause.","zh":"疑问词或以其为中心语的短语必须出现在小句的开头。"},{"en":"Grammatical main clause content questions also show Subject-Auxiliary Inversion, like Yes-No questions.","zh":"合乎语法的主句内容疑问句同是非问句一样，也发生主语—助动词倒装。"},{"en":"Many languages mark Yes-No questions with a question particle or leave content question words in-situ.","zh":"许多语言用疑问助词标记是非问句，或让疑问词留在原位。"}],"terms":[{"en":"content question","zh":"内容疑问句","defEn":"A question that asks for specific information rather than a yes or no answer.","defZh":"询问具体信息、而非要求以 yes 或 no 来作答的问句。"},{"en":"content question word","zh":"疑问词","defEn":"A word such as who, what, where, when, why, or how that forms content questions.","defZh":"who、what、where、when、why、how 等构成内容疑问句的词。"},{"en":"Question Word Fronting","zh":"疑问词前置","defEn":"The generalization that a content question word must appear at the beginning of the clause.","defZh":"疑问词或其引导的短语必须出现在小句开头这一普遍规律。"},{"en":"in-situ","zh":"原位","defEn":"Describes a question word that stays in the position of the corresponding non-question phrase.","defZh":"指疑问词停留在相应非疑问短语原有位置上的情况，字面意思为在原处。"},{"en":"echo question","zh":"回声问句","defEn":"An in-situ question used to ask someone to repeat what they said.","defZh":"疑问词留在原位的问句，用于请对方重复刚刚说过的话。"},{"en":"question particle","zh":"疑问助词","defEn":"A fixed word added to a sentence to mark it as a Yes-No question.","defZh":"加在句子上以标记是非问句的固定虚词，如法语 est-ce que。"}],"examples":[{"text":"What has the squirrel hidden?","noteEn":"The question word is about the object of hide but appears at the very beginning of the clause.","noteZh":"疑问词问的是 hide 的宾语，却出现在小句的最开头。"},{"text":"Where is it snowing?","noteEn":"A content question about location, showing both fronting and Subject-Auxiliary Inversion.","noteZh":"询问地点的内容疑问句，同时体现了疑问词前置和主语—助动词倒装。"},{"text":"It's snowing where?","noteEn":"An echo question, in which the question word stays in-situ and the intonation rises.","noteZh":"回声问句，疑问词留在原位，句末语调上升。"},{"text":"Usagi-wa nani-o tabe-ru ka","noteEn":"A Japanese content question in which nani-o stays in-situ and the particle ka is clause-final.","noteZh":"日语内容疑问句，nani-o 留在原位，助词 ka 位于小句末尾。"}],"body":[{"en":"Until now we have looked at Yes-No questions, which ask whether something is the case. Content questions ask for specific information about part of a sentence, for example time in When was it snowing? or location in Where is it snowing?. English often calls them WH-questions, but this book says content question words for who, what, where, when, why, and how. Their answer is a word or phrase corresponding to the question word, never yes or no.","zh":"此前讨论的是是非问句，它们询问某事是否成立；内容疑问句则就句子的某一部分询问具体信息，例如 When was it snowing? 问时间，Where is it snowing? 问地点。英语常称这类问句为 WH 疑问句，本书则把 who、what、where、when、why、how 统称为疑问词。内容疑问句的回答是与疑问词相对应的词或短语，绝不是 yes 或 no。"},{"en":"Content questions in English involve changes in word order. In What has the squirrel hidden?, the question word asks about the object of hide, yet it appears at the very beginning of the clause; this is Question Word Fronting. Ordinary information-seeking questions cannot leave the word in the statement position, so *It's snowing where?, *It was snowing when?, and *Squirrels hide nuts how? are not grammatical. All the grammatical content questions also show Subject-Auxiliary Inversion.","zh":"英语的内容疑问句涉及词序变化。在 What has the squirrel hidden? 中，疑问词问的是 hide 的宾语，却出现在小句的最开头，这就是疑问词前置。真正求取信息的问句不能把疑问词留在陈述句中的原位置，因此 *It's snowing where?、*It was snowing when? 和 *Squirrels hide nuts how? 都不合语法。所有合语法的主句内容疑问句也都发生主语—助动词倒装。"},{"en":"When a content question word does stay in the position where the corresponding phrase would appear in a statement, it is in-situ, meaning in place. In many languages this is the normal way to form content questions, but in English it is not the default and is used mainly for echo questions, as when you did not quite hear someone. Echo questions also take the rising intonation of Yes-No questions rather than the falling intonation of ordinary content questions.","zh":"如果疑问词确实停留在相应的非疑问短语在陈述句中本应出现的位置，就称其为原位，意思是在原处。在许多语言中，这是构成内容疑问句的常规方式；但在英语中它并非默认手段，主要用于回声问句，比如没听清对方的话时。回声问句还采用是非问句的上升语调，而不是一般内容疑问句的下降语调。"},{"en":"Languages vary in how they mark questions. Many use a question particle, such as French est-ce que at the start of a sentence, Japanese ka at the end, or Mandarin ma at the end. Because Japanese is head-final, ka is clause-final, and Japanese also leaves content question words in-situ: in Usagi-wa nani-o tabe-ru ka the word nani-o sits where the object would sit in a statement. Such particles resemble the English complementizer if or whether in main clauses more than the auxiliary do.","zh":"各语言标记疑问的方式彼此不同。许多语言使用疑问助词，如法语的 est-ce que 位于句首，日语的 ka 和汉语普通话的 ma 位于句末。由于日语是中心语后置语言，ka 出现在小句末尾，日语还让疑问词留在原位：在 Usagi-wa nani-o tabe-ru ka 中，nani-o 就位于相应宾语在陈述句中所处的位置。这类助词更像出现在主句中的英语标句词 if 或 whether，而不像助动词 do。"}]},"chapter-060-embedded-content-questions":{"title":{"en":"6.9 Embedded content questions and relative clauses","zh":"6.9 嵌入的内容疑问句与关系小句"},"summary":{"en":"Any verb that can embed a yes-no question can also embed a content question, but embedded content questions take no complementizer and no Subject-Auxiliary Inversion, unlike main clause ones. Clauses also appear as complements of nouns and as relative clauses that modify nouns. Relative clauses front a relative pronoun and leave a gap, just like content questions.","zh":"凡是能嵌入是非问句的动词也能嵌入内容疑问句，但嵌入式内容疑问句不能出现标句词，也不进行主语—助动词倒装，这与主句内容疑问句不同。小句还可充当名词的补足语，或充当修饰名词的关系小句。关系小句与内容疑问句一样需要前置并留下空位，只不过前置的是关系代词。"},"points":[{"en":"Any verb that can embed a yes-no question can also embed a content question, as know, ask, and wonder show.","zh":"凡是能嵌入是非问句的动词，也能嵌入内容疑问句，know、ask 和 wonder 都如此。"},{"en":"Embedded content questions contain no complementizer and do not undergo Subject-Auxiliary Inversion, unlike main clause content questions.","zh":"嵌入式内容疑问句不能出现标句词，也不进行主语—助动词倒装，这一点与主句内容疑问句不同。"},{"en":"Clauses may appear as complements of nouns, often nouns derived from clause-embedding verbs, and questions there require the preposition of.","zh":"小句可作名词补足语，这类名词多由能嵌入小句的动词派生而来；此时疑问小句须由介词 of 引导。"},{"en":"Relative clauses modify a noun rather than complement it, and are introduced by that or a relative pronoun like who or which.","zh":"关系小句修饰名词而非充当其补足语，可由 that 或 who、which 一类关系代词引导。"},{"en":"Like content questions, relative clauses leave a gap and front a relative pronoun; free relatives stand alone without a modified noun.","zh":"与内容疑问句一样，关系小句也留下空位并前置关系代词；自由关系小句单独使用，不修饰名词。"}],"terms":[{"en":"complementizer","zh":"标句词","defEn":"A word like that, if, or whether that introduces an embedded clause.","defZh":"引导嵌入小句的词，如 that、if、whether，出现在小句的最左边缘。"},{"en":"relative clause","zh":"关系小句","defEn":"A clause that modifies a noun instead of serving as its complement.","defZh":"修饰名词而非充当名词补足语的小句，通常由关系代词引导并含有一个空位。"},{"en":"relative pronoun","zh":"关系代词","defEn":"A word such as who, which, where, when, or why that introduces a relative clause.","defZh":"引导关系小句的词，如 who、which、where、when、why，传统语法称之为关系代词。"},{"en":"free relative clause","zh":"自由关系小句","defEn":"A relative clause that stands alone without modifying any noun.","defZh":"不修饰任何名词、单独充当名词短语使用的关系小句，英语中多由 whoever、whatever 等引导。"},{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion","zh":"主语—助动词倒装","defEn":"Movement of an auxiliary verb to a position before the subject.","defZh":"助动词移到主语之前的句法操作，出现在英语主句内容疑问句中。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I know what squirrels have hidden.","noteEn":"An embedded content question: the question word is fronted but there is no inversion.","noteZh":"嵌入式内容疑问句：疑问词前置，但主语与助动词不发生倒装。"},{"text":"*I know what have squirrels hidden.","noteEn":"Ungrammatical for most speakers of Canadian English because embedded content questions do not invert.","noteZh":"对多数加拿大英语使用者不合语法，因为嵌入式内容疑问句不发生倒装。"},{"text":"The cookies (that) my brother baked turned out well.","noteEn":"A relative clause modifying the noun cookies and introduced by the optional complementizer that.","noteZh":"关系小句修饰名词 cookies，由可选的标句词 that 引导。"},{"text":"The irate guest complained about whoever was at the front desk.","noteEn":"A free relative clause introduced by whoever, occupying the position of a noun phrase.","noteZh":"由 whoever 引导的自由关系小句，占据名词短语所处的位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"Having surveyed main and embedded statements and yes-no questions, the chapter turns to content questions inside embedded clauses. Any verb that can embed a yes-no question, such as know, ask, or wonder, can also embed a content question: alongside I know if squirrels have hidden nuts we find I know what squirrels have hidden. The question word moves to the front of the embedded clause, exactly as in a main clause content question.","zh":"在考察了主句与嵌入小句的陈述句及是非问句之后，本节转向嵌入小句中的内容疑问句。凡是能嵌入是非问句的动词，如 know、ask、wonder，也都能嵌入内容疑问句：既有 I know if squirrels have hidden nuts，也有 I know what squirrels have hidden。疑问词移到嵌入小句的最前端，与主句内容疑问句一致。"},{"en":"Two things distinguish these from main clause content questions. First, no complementizer may appear: adding if, whether, or that to an embedded content question yields ungrammatical results. Second, there is no Subject-Auxiliary Inversion, so I know what squirrels have hidden is fine while I know what have squirrels hidden is not. Some varieties of English spoken in Belfast do allow inversion here.","zh":"它们与主句内容疑问句有两点不同。第一，不能出现标句词：在嵌入式内容疑问句中加 if、whether 或 that 都会造成不合语法。第二，不发生主语—助动词倒装，因此 I know what squirrels have hidden 成立，而 I know what have squirrels hidden 不成立。不过据 Henry（1995）描述，爱尔兰贝尔法斯特的某些英语变体允许这种倒装。"},{"en":"Clauses can also appear inside noun phrases. A clause may be the complement of a noun, especially a noun derived from a clause-embedding verb, as in the knowledge that squirrels hide nuts. When the complement is a question rather than a statement, it must be introduced by the preposition of; removing of makes the sentence ungrammatical. Nouns can likewise take ordinary noun phrase complements introduced by of or about.","zh":"小句也可以出现在名词短语内部。小句可以充当名词的补足语，尤其是由能嵌入小句的动词派生的名词，例如 the knowledge that squirrels hide nuts。当补足语是疑问小句而非陈述小句时，必须由介词 of 引导；去掉 of 句子便不合语法。名词同样可以带由 of 或 about 引导的普通名词短语补足语。"},{"en":"Relative clauses are a different kind of clause inside a noun phrase: they modify a noun instead of complementing it. They may be introduced by the optional complementizer that or by a relative pronoun such as who, where, or which. Like content questions, they contain a gap and front an element, a process the chapter calls Relative Fronting. Relative pronouns are optional, and English also has a silent relative pronoun. Free relative clauses, such as whoever was at the front desk, stand alone without any modified noun.","zh":"关系小句是名词短语中另一类小句：它们修饰名词，而不充当名词的补足语。关系小句可以由可选的标句词 that 引导，也可以由 who、where、which 等关系代词引导。与内容疑问句一样，关系小句内部含有一个空位并需要前置某个成分，本节把这一操作称为关系词前置。关系代词是可选的，英语还存在一个零形式的关系代词。自由关系小句（如 whoever was at the front desk）则单独使用，不修饰任何名词。"}]},"chapter-061-arguments-and-thematic-roles":{"title":{"en":"6.10 Arguments and thematic roles","zh":"6.10 论元与题元角色"},"summary":{"en":"Subject and object are structural notions, but the participants in an eventuality play distinct semantic roles called thematic roles. Verbs select both the number of arguments they take and the roles those arguments bear. Roles discussed here include agent, causer, experiencer, theme, instrument, location, and goal. Weather verbs like rain describe eventualities with no participants.","zh":"主语和宾语是结构概念，而事件或状态中的参与者扮演不同的语义角色，即题元角色。动词不仅选择论元的数量，也选择论元所承担的题元角色。本节讨论的题元角色包括施事、致事、经历者、主题、工具、处所和目标。rain 一类天气动词所描述的事件则没有任何参与者。"},"points":[{"en":"Subject and object are structural terms: subjects precede the verb and control agreement, while objects follow the verb.","zh":"主语和宾语是结构术语：主语位于限定动词之前并控制一致，宾语位于动词之后。"},{"en":"Thematic roles describe the part a participant plays in an eventuality, and different subjects can bear different roles.","zh":"题元角色描述参与者在事件或状态中所起的作用，不同的主语可以承担不同的题元角色。"},{"en":"An agent acts on purpose, a causer causes without purpose, and an experiencer undergoes a mental state.","zh":"施事有意地发出动作，致事并非有意地使某事发生，经历者则经历某种心理状态。"},{"en":"The theme is the participant something happens to; instruments, locations, and goals typically appear in prepositional phrases.","zh":"主题是某事所发生的对象；工具、处所和目标通常出现在介词短语中。"},{"en":"Verbs select both the number and the thematic roles of their arguments; a single argument is always the subject.","zh":"动词既选择论元的数量，也选择题元角色；只有一个论元时，该论元必定是主语。"},{"en":"Weather verbs like rain and snow have a syntactic subject but describe eventualities with no participants at all.","zh":"rain、snow 等天气动词带有句法主语，但所描述的事件没有任何参与者。"}],"terms":[{"en":"thematic role","zh":"题元角色","defEn":"The role a participant plays in an eventuality, such as agent, theme, or goal.","defZh":"参与者在事件或状态中所扮演的角色，如施事、主题、目标等。"},{"en":"agent","zh":"施事","defEn":"An animate actor who does something on purpose.","defZh":"有意发出动作的有生命参与者，例如 The pirate sank the ship 中的 the pirate。"},{"en":"causer","zh":"致事","defEn":"An often inanimate participant that makes something happen without acting on purpose.","defZh":"通常无生命、并非有意地使某事发生的参与者，如 The bilge pump malfunction 作主语。"},{"en":"experiencer","zh":"经历者","defEn":"An animate participant that experiences a mental state, including perception.","defZh":"经历心理状态（包括感知）的有生命参与者，如 I fear pirates 中的 I。"},{"en":"theme","zh":"主题","defEn":"The participant to which something happens, which may or may not be changed.","defZh":"某事所发生的对象，可能随事件而改变，也可能不受影响。"},{"en":"goal","zh":"目标","defEn":"The location or person that receives the theme, often the indirect object.","defZh":"接受主题的处所或人，在多数双及物结构中充当间接宾语。"}],"examples":[{"text":"The pirate sank the ship.","noteEn":"Here the subject is an agent, since the pirate acts on purpose.","noteZh":"此处主语是施事，因为 the pirate 有意发出动作。"},{"text":"The ship sank.","noteEn":"The same verb used intransitively, with the ship as the theme subject.","noteZh":"同一个动词用作不及物，the ship 充任主题主语。"},{"text":"The pirates sent a message to the ship.","noteEn":"The ship is the goal, receiving the theme a message.","noteZh":"the ship 是目标，接受主题 a message。"},{"text":"It is raining.","noteEn":"A weather verb: the sentence has a subject, but the eventuality has no participants.","noteZh":"天气动词：句子有主语，但事件本身没有任何参与者。"}],"body":[{"en":"Predicates were earlier classified by transitivity: intransitive verbs take only a subject, transitive verbs take a subject and an object, and ditransitive verbs add an indirect object. But subject and object are structural notions. In English a subject appears at the beginning of a declarative clause, bears nominative case if it is a pronoun, and controls agreement on the tensed verb, while an object follows the verb and bears accusative case. These positions tell us nothing yet about meaning.","zh":"前面按及物性对谓语作了分类：不及物动词只带主语，及物动词带主语和宾语，双及物动词再加一个间接宾语。但主语和宾语都是结构概念。在英语中，主语出现在陈述小句的开头，若为代词则用主格，并控制限定动词的一致；宾语位于动词之后，若为代词则用宾格。这些结构位置本身并不说明意义。"},{"en":"To talk about meaning, verbs can be seen as describing events or states, and eventuality is used here as a cover term for both. An eventuality involves a number of participants, and the roles those participants play are called thematic roles. Subjects do not always have the same role: in The children yelled the subject acts on purpose, in The wind blew the tree down it does not, and in The tree burned something simply happens to the subject.","zh":"要讨论意义，可以把动词视为描述事件或状态，本节用「事件」一词统称二者。一个事件包含若干参与者，这些参与者所扮演的角色称为题元角色。主语并不总是承担同一角色：The children yelled 的主语有意发出动作，The wind blew the tree down 的主语并非有意，而 The tree burned 中只是某事发生在主语身上。"},{"en":"The chapter defines several roles. An agent is an animate actor who acts on purpose; a causer is typically inanimate and causes something to happen without purpose; an experiencer is an animate participant with a mental state, as with verbs like see, hear, fear, and like. A theme is the participant something happens to. Instruments, locations, and goals are usually expressed in prepositional phrases, and in most ditransitives the indirect object is the goal.","zh":"本节界定了几种角色。施事是有意发出动作的有生命参与者；致事通常无生命，并非有意地使某事发生；经历者是有心理状态的有生命参与者，见于 see、hear、fear、like 等动词。主题是某事所发生的对象。工具、处所和目标通常由介词短语表达，在多数双及物结构中，间接宾语就是目标。"},{"en":"Verbs select not only how many arguments they take but also which thematic roles those arguments bear, and they are not entirely free in mapping roles onto positions: an agent is always the subject, and a lone argument is always the subject. English has agent intransitives like The pirate laughed and theme intransitives like The tree fell. Weather verbs such as rain and snow have a subject but describe eventualities with no participants.","zh":"动词不仅选择论元的数量，也选择这些论元承担哪些题元角色；而且角色到句法位置的映射并非完全自由：施事总是主语，唯一的论元也总是主语。英语中既有 The pirate laughed 这样的施事不及物动词，也有 The tree fell 这样的主题不及物动词。rain、snow 等天气动词又有所不同：它们有主语，但所描述的事件没有任何参与者。"}]},"chapter-062-adding-or-removing-arguments-causatives-and-passives":{"title":{"en":"6.11 Changing argument structure: Causatives and passives","zh":"6.11 改变论元结构：使役式与被动式"},"summary":{"en":"All languages can adjust the thematic roles expressed in a clause. Causatives add a causer or agent as a new subject, either syntactically with a verb like make or morphologically, as in Japanese. Benefactive applicatives add a participant the event is done for. Passives remove the original subject, promote the object, and add be plus a past participle.","zh":"所有语言都能调整小句中所表达的题元角色。使役式增加一个致事或施事作为新的主语，既可以用 make 一类动词在句法上实现，也可以用词形变化实现，如日语。受益施用式增加事件为之而做的参与者。被动式删除原主语、提升宾语，并使用 be 加过去分词。"},"points":[{"en":"Causatives add an extra causer or agent that becomes the new subject, as in I made them read a book.","zh":"使役式增加一个致事或施事，并使其成为新的主语，如 I made them read a book。"},{"en":"In morphological causatives such as Japanese, verb morphology adds the causer, and the causee receives dative rather than accusative case.","zh":"在日语等语言的形态使役式中，由动词形态增加致事，被使者用与格而非宾格标记。"},{"en":"Benefactive applicatives add a participant that the event is done for, usually as an indirect object.","zh":"受益施用式增加事件为之而做的参与者，通常使其充当间接宾语。"},{"en":"Passives demote the original subject, promote the object to subject, and require be plus a past participle.","zh":"被动式降级原主语，把原宾语提升为主语，并要求使用 be 加过去分词。"},{"en":"Every passive has an active counterpart; verbs like sink can be either active transitive or active intransitive.","zh":"每个被动小句都有对应的主动小句；sink 一类动词既可作及物主动，也可作不及物主动。"},{"en":"Everyday criticism of the passive often confuses its technical grammatical meaning with complaints about hiding the agent.","zh":"日常话语对被动式的批评常常把它的语法学含义与「掩盖施事」的抱怨混为一谈。"}],"terms":[{"en":"causative","zh":"使役式","defEn":"A construction that adds an extra causer or agent, which becomes the new subject.","defZh":"增加一个致事或施事并使其成为新主语的构式，如英语的 make 使役式或日语的形态使役式。"},{"en":"passive","zh":"被动式","defEn":"A construction that removes the original subject and makes the object the subject.","defZh":"删除原主语、并使原宾语成为主语的构式，英语中由 be 加过去分词构成。"},{"en":"active","zh":"主动式","defEn":"A non-passive clause, the counterpart from which a passive is formed.","defZh":"非被动的小句，是与被动式相对应的基本形式，如 They wrote a book 相对于 A book was written。"},{"en":"grammatical voice","zh":"语法语态","defEn":"A grammatical category including active and passive, and in Greek also middle voice.","defZh":"包括主动与被动在内的语法范畴，希腊语中还有中动语态。"},{"en":"benefactive applicative","zh":"受益施用式","defEn":"An argument-adding construction that adds a participant the event is done for.","defZh":"增加一个表示事件为之而做的参与者、通常使其作间接宾语的论元增容构式。"},{"en":"causee","zh":"被使者","defEn":"The participant made to perform an action in a causative construction.","defZh":"使役构式中被要求执行动作的参与者，在日语中用与格标记。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I made them read a book.","noteEn":"English syntactic causative: make adds a causer subject and the original subject becomes accusative.","noteZh":"英语句法使役式：make 增加一个致事主语，原主语变为宾格。"},{"text":"Watasi-wa neko-ni tabe-sase-ta","noteEn":"Japanese morphological causative: the suffix -sase adds the causer, and the causee takes dative -ni.","noteZh":"日语形态使役式：后缀 -sase 增加致事，被使者用与格 -ni 标记。"},{"text":"The ship was sunk (by the pirates).","noteEn":"A passive: be plus past participle, an optional by-phrase, and the original object as subject.","noteZh":"被动式：be 加过去分词，by 短语可选，原宾语充当主语。"},{"text":"I baked my friend a cake.","noteEn":"A benefactive applicative, adding my friend as an indirect object benefited by the event.","noteZh":"受益施用式，增加 my friend 作间接宾语，表示事件为之而做。"}],"body":[{"en":"Up to this point the thematic roles discussed are those that verb roots come specified with. But every language has ways of adjusting the roles expressed in a clause, either syntactically or through morphology. Causatives are one such device: they add an extra causer or agent, which becomes the new subject. English has several syntactic causatives, including the construction with make. In I made them read a book the original subject they now appears after make in accusative case, although its thematic role is unchanged.","zh":"此前讨论的题元角色都是词根本身所规定的。但所有语言都能在句法或词法层面调整小句中所表达的角色。使役式就是这样一种手段：它增加一个致事或施事，并使其成为新的主语。英语有多种句法使役式，其中包括用 make 的构式。在 I made them read a book 中，原来的主语 they 现在出现在 make 之后并变为宾格，但它的题元角色并未改变。"},{"en":"Other languages use morphological causatives, in which verbal morphology rather than a separate causative verb adds the causer. In Japanese, Watasi-wa neko-ni tabe-sase-ta contains the causative suffix -sase, and the original subject takes dative -ni rather than the accusative case found in English; causees in such languages are generally marked dative or accusative. Languages also have other argument-adding constructions, such as benefactive applicatives, which add a participant the event is done for: I baked a cake becomes I baked my friend a cake.","zh":"其他语言使用形态使役式，由动词形态而非独立的使役动词增加致事。日语 Watasi-wa neko-ni tabe-sase-ta 含使役后缀 -sase，原来的主语用与格 -ni 标记，而不是英语中的宾格；在既有使役式又有形态格的语言中，被使者通常标为与格或宾格。语言还有其他增容构式，例如受益施用式，它增加事件为之而做的参与者：I baked a cake 变成 I baked my friend a cake。"},{"en":"Conversely, some constructions remove an argument. The best known is the passive, which removes the original subject and turns the original object into the passive subject; the corresponding non-passive sentence is called active. A grammatical passive must demote the original subject, which may appear in an optional by-phrase, promote the object to subject, and carry the be plus past participle morphology.","zh":"相反，也有一些构式删除论元。最著名的是被动式：它删除动词原来的主语，并使原来的宾语成为被动句的主语；与之相应的非被动句称为主动句。合格的被动式必须降级原主语（可用可选的 by 短语来表达），把宾语提升为主语，并带有 be 加过去分词的典型形态。"},{"en":"The first property links each passive to an active counterpart, so The pirates sank the ship has the passive The ship was sunk (by the pirates). A theme intransitive such as The ship sank looks similar but lacks the by-phrase and the auxiliary, so it is not a passive. Popular advice often tells writers to avoid the passive because it supposedly hides the agent, yet the passive is precisely what allows the agent to appear in a by-phrase, which plain intransitives do not.","zh":"第一个特征把被动式与对应的主动句联系起来，因此 The pirates sank the ship 的被动形式是 The ship was sunk (by the pirates)。The ship sank 这样的主题不及物句看似相近，却既无 by 短语也无助动词，因而不是被动式。流行的写作建议常说应避免被动式，理由是它掩盖施事；但恰恰是被动式允许施事出现在 by 短语中，而普通不及物动词做不到这一点。"}]},"chapter-063-interim-summary":{"title":{"en":"6.12 Interim summary","zh":"6.12 阶段性小结"},"summary":{"en":"So far the chapter has covered core concepts of syntactic theory: languages are best described through structural relations rather than linear order, a phrase takes its properties from its head, and grammaticality judgements reveal fine syntactic detail. Clause classes such as questions and passives are described by their systematic relation to statements and actives, and the head direction parameter captures word order differences between English and Japanese.","zh":"本章至此介绍了句法理论的一些核心概念：自然语言更适合用结构关系而非线性顺序来描写，短语的性质由中心语决定，合乎语法性判断可揭示句法的细微之处。疑问句、被动句等小句类别通过与陈述句、主动句的系统性联系得到描写，而中心语方向参数则刻画了英语与日语之间的语序差异。"},"points":[{"en":"Natural languages are better described in terms of structural relations than in terms of linear word order.","zh":"与词语的线性顺序相比，用结构关系来描写自然语言更为恰当。"},{"en":"The properties of a phrase are determined by its head, the element that gives the phrase its category.","zh":"短语的性质由其中心语决定，中心语决定整个短语所属的范畴。"},{"en":"Grammaticality judgements let us investigate fine details about the syntax of a language.","zh":"合乎语法性判断使我们能够考察一种语言句法的细微之处。"},{"en":"Questions and passives can be described through their systematic relation to statements and actives.","zh":"疑问句和被动句可以通过它们与陈述句、主动句的系统性联系来描写。"},{"en":"The head direction parameter accounts for word order differences between English and Japanese in all clause types.","zh":"中心语方向参数解释了英语与日语在各类小句中的语序差别。"}],"terms":[{"en":"structural relation","zh":"结构关系","defEn":"A relation between words or phrases in a sentence, such as head and complement.","defZh":"句子中词语或短语之间的关系，如中心语与补足语的关系，而非单纯的线性顺序。"},{"en":"head","zh":"中心语","defEn":"The element that determines the properties and category of the phrase containing it.","defZh":"决定所在短语的性质与范畴的成分，如名词短语中的名词和动词短语中的动词。"},{"en":"grammaticality judgement","zh":"合乎语法性判断","defEn":"A speaker's intuitive judgement about whether a sentence is grammatical in their language.","defZh":"说话者对本族语中某个句子是否合乎语法所作出的直觉判断。"},{"en":"head direction parameter","zh":"中心语方向参数","defEn":"A parameter setting whether heads precede or follow their complements, as in English and Japanese.","defZh":"决定中心语位于补足语之前还是之后的参数设置，如英语与日语的差异。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the head direction parameter accounts for differences in word order between English and Japanese in all types of clauses","noteEn":"The chapter's illustrative case of how one parameter handles cross-linguistic word order variation.","noteZh":"本章用以说明单一参数即可解释跨语言语序差异的例证。"}],"body":[{"en":"This chapter has introduced core concepts of syntactic theory and shown how they help us reason about grammatical structures and about relations between classes of sentences. Natural languages are better described in terms of structural relations than in terms of the mere linear order of words. The properties of a phrase are determined by its head, and grammaticality judgements let us investigate fine details about a language's syntax, including which structures its grammar permits and which it rules out.","zh":"本章介绍了句法理论的一些核心概念，并展示了如何借助它们来思考语法结构以及各类句子之间的关系。与仅仅描写词语的线性顺序相比，用结构关系来描写自然语言更为恰当。短语的性质由其中心语决定，而合乎语法性判断则使我们能够考察一种语言句法的细微之处，例如哪些结构为语法所允许、哪些则被语法所排除。"},{"en":"Certain classes of clauses can be described by their systematic relation to other clauses: questions to statements, and passives to actives. Such concepts also capture syntactic differences across languages; the head direction parameter, for instance, accounts for word order differences between English and Japanese in all types of clauses. The remaining sections introduce tree diagrams and a derivational implementation of X-bar theory, in which grammatical sentences are described by constraints on well-formed trees plus movement transformations.","zh":"某些类别的小句可以通过它们与其他小句的系统性联系来描写：疑问句与陈述句相联系，被动句与主动句相联系。这些概念同样能够刻画语言之间的句法差异；例如中心语方向参数就解释了英语与日语在各类小句中语序的差别。本章余下的各节将引入树形图这一形式化记法，特别是 X 杠理论的一种推导式实现：一种语言的合乎语法句由关于良构树结构的制约以及可施加于这些结构的移位转换来描写。"},{"en":"Although the focus has been English, we have only scratched the surface of its syntactic grammar. The tools developed here can nevertheless be applied to other phenomena in English, or to the grammar of entirely unrelated languages.","zh":"尽管我们主要关注英语这一种语言，但我们对英语句法的了解仍然只是冰山一角。不过，这里发展出的工具既可用于英语中的其他现象，也可用于与英语完全无关的语言的语法，帮助我们继续考察它们的句法规律。"},{"en":"The concepts covered include structural relations rather than linear order, the head as the source of a phrase's properties, grammaticality judgements as evidence, the systematic links among clause classes, and the head direction parameter as an account of cross-linguistic word order.","zh":"这些概念包括：以结构关系而非线性顺序作为描写的基础；中心语决定短语的性质；合乎语法性判断作为句法证据；小句类别之间的系统性联系；以及用中心语方向参数解释跨语言的语序差异。"}]},"chapter-064-from-constituency-to-tree-diagrams":{"title":{"en":"6.13 From constituency to tree diagrams","zh":"6.13 从成分到树形图"},"summary":{"en":"This section introduces tree diagrams as a formal notation for phrase and sentence structure. It builds phrase structure rules for NPs, PPs, VPs, and modifier phrases such as AdvPs, AdjPs, and NumPs, showing how recursion arises and how full sentences are analysed. It also notes the dative alternation, the rare adjectives that take NP complements, and the rule for sentences with auxiliaries and negation.","zh":"本节引入树形图这一表示短语与句子结构的形式化记法，并给出名词短语、介词短语、动词短语以及副词短语、形容词短语、数词短语等修饰语短语的短语结构规则，说明递归如何产生以及整句如何分析。文中还提到与格交替、极少数带名词短语补足语的形容词，以及含助动词与否定的句子规则。"},"points":[{"en":"Phrase structure rules such as S → NP VP express sentence composition and were central to Chomsky 1957.","zh":"S → NP VP 这样的短语结构规则表达句子的构成，在 Chomsky 1957 的理论中居于核心地位。"},{"en":"Tree diagrams express the same information as several phrase structure rules at once.","zh":"树形图能一次表达若干条短语结构规则所提供的信息，比逐条罗列更为简洁。"},{"en":"Because a PP can contain an NP that contains another PP, phrase structure rules allow recursion.","zh":"由于介词短语中可以包含名词短语，而后者又可包含介词短语，短语结构规则容许递归。"},{"en":"Replacement tests with pronouns and with do identify noun phrases and verb phrases in sentences.","zh":"用代词和 do 进行替代测试，可以判定句子中的名词短语和动词短语。"},{"en":"Ditransitive verbs alternate between [NP NP] and [NP PP], an alternation called the dative alternation.","zh":"双及物动词可以在 [NP NP] 与 [NP PP] 两种形式之间交替，这种交替称为与格交替。"},{"en":"Complements of adjectives are almost always PPs, with rare NP-complement exceptions such as worth and done.","zh":"形容词的补足语几乎总是介词短语，仅有 worth、done 等极少数带名词短语补足语的例外。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phrase structure rule","zh":"短语结构规则","defEn":"A rule stating what elements a phrase of a given category may be made up of.","defZh":"说明某一范畴的短语可以由哪些成分构成的规则，如 S → NP VP 即为一例。"},{"en":"tree diagram","zh":"树形图","defEn":"A formal notation representing the hierarchical structure of a phrase or sentence.","defZh":"表示短语或句子层级结构的形式化图示记法，用来呈现句法成分之间的关系。"},{"en":"recursion","zh":"递归","defEn":"The property that a rule can apply to its own output.","defZh":"规则可以作用于自身输出的性质，如名词短语含介词短语、介词短语又含名词短语。"},{"en":"dative alternation","zh":"与格交替","defEn":"The alternation between a ditransitive [NP NP] form and an [NP PP] form.","defZh":"双及物动词在 [NP NP] 形式与 [NP PP] 形式之间交替出现的现象，如 give 的两种句式。"},{"en":"ditransitive verb","zh":"双及物动词","defEn":"A verb that combines with two object noun phrases, such as give.","defZh":"可以带两个宾语名词短语的动词，如 give 和 put，常可与介词短语形式交替。"},{"en":"Do-support","zh":"do 支持","defEn":"The insertion of the auxiliary do when negation or a question requires one but none is present.","defZh":"当否定或疑问需要助动词而句中又没有助动词时，插入助动词 do 的操作。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the six small robots from Boston","noteEn":"A noun phrase built as determiner, numeral, adjective, noun, and prepositional phrase.","noteZh":"由限定词、数词、形容词、名词和介词短语构成的名词短语。"},{"text":"The spaceship [gave orders to the crew].","noteEn":"The [NP PP] form of the ditransitive verb give, illustrating the dative alternation.","noteZh":"双及物动词 give 的 [NP PP] 形式，体现与格交替，即宾语改由介词短语表达。"},{"text":"I am [finished my coffee].","noteEn":"A deverbal adjective with an NP complement, found in Canadian English.","noteZh":"由动词派生的形容词带名词短语补足语，见于加拿大英语。"},{"text":"We are happy.","noteEn":"A verb followed by an adjective phrase, which needs a second rule for VPs.","noteZh":"动词之后接形容词短语，这种情况需要另立一条动词短语规则。"}],"body":[{"en":"This section introduces tree diagrams as a formal notation for phrase and sentence structure, so that hypotheses become specific and testable. The phrase structure rule S → NP VP, central to Chomsky 1957 and to generative syntax, says that a sentence may consist of an NP subject and a VP predicate. Trees express several rules at once, and current theories constrain possible trees rather than rules.","zh":"本节引入树形图这一形式化记法来表示短语与句子的结构，以便提出具体而可检验的假设。句法理论的目标是解释语言使用者关于哪些句子合乎语法、哪些不合乎语法的知识。短语结构规则 S → NP VP 在 Chomsky 1957 的理论中居于核心地位，开启了现代生成句法学：该规则表示句子可以由名词短语主语和动词短语谓语组成。树形图能同时表达若干条规则的信息；当代理论通常以对可能树结构的制约来表述，而非以对短语结构规则的制约来表述。"},{"en":"Noun phrases range from robots to the six small robots from Boston. The rule NP → (Det) (Num) (Adj)n N (PP)n captures them: an optional determiner, an optional numeral, any number of optional adjectives, a required noun, and any number of optional prepositional phrases. Prepositional phrases are simpler, as in from Boston, outside, just outside, and way beyond my knowledge, giving PP → (Deg) P (NP). Since a PP can contain an NP, recursion reappears.","zh":"名词短语的形态多种多样，从 robots 到 the six small robots from Boston。规则 NP → (Det) (Num) (Adj)n N (PP)n 概括了这些可能：可选限定词、可选数词、任意数量的可选形容词、必需的名词，以及任意数量的可选介词短语。介词短语的形式较少，如 from Boston、outside、just outside、way beyond my knowledge，可概括为 PP → (Deg) P (NP)。由于介词短语中可以包含名词短语，递归现象再次出现。"},{"en":"Verb phrases may be an intransitive verb, a transitive verb with an NP or PP complement, or a ditransitive verb with two object NPs: VP → Vintrans; VP → Vtrans NP; VP → Vditrans NP NP; VP → Vditrans NP PP; VP → Vtrans PP. Many ditransitive verbs alternate between [NP NP] and [NP PP], the dative alternation, and some like put allow only the latter. The general rule is VP → (AdvP) V (NP) (NP/PP) (AdvP)n, plus VP → V AdjP for We are happy and They seem nice.","zh":"动词短语可以只含一个不及物动词，可以是及物动词带名词短语或介词短语补足语，也可以是双及物动词带两个宾语名词短语，对应规则 VP → Vintrans、VP → Vtrans NP、VP → Vditrans NP NP、VP → Vditrans NP PP 和 VP → Vtrans PP。许多双及物动词可以在 [NP NP] 与 [NP PP] 两种形式之间交替，这称为与格交替；而像 put 这样的动词只允许后者。一般规则为 VP → (AdvP) V (NP) (NP/PP) (AdvP)n；另有少数动词带形容词短语，如 We are happy 和 They seem nice，故需补充一条 VP → V AdjP。"},{"en":"Modifier phrases follow patterns: AdvP → (DegP) Adv (PP) for quickly, very quickly, and quite quickly; AdjP → (DegP) Adj (PP); and NumP → (DegP) Num for exactly six, approximately 30, and very many. Adjective complements are nearly always PPs, with NP-complement exceptions: worth for all speakers, and the deverbal finished and done for many Canadian and some upstate New York and Pennsylvania speakers. Full sentences give S → (AdvP) NP (Aux) (Neg) VP (AdvP); negation needs an auxiliary and triggers Do-support. These rules merely list possible sequences.","zh":"各类修饰语短语也有相应规则：AdvP → (DegP) Adv (PP)，如 quickly、very quickly、quite quickly；AdjP → (DegP) Adj (PP)；NumP → (DegP) Num，如 exactly six、approximately 30、very many。形容词的补足语几乎总是介词短语，只有极少数例外允许名词短语：对所有说话者而言是 worth，而对多数加拿大英语使用者以及纽约州北部和宾夕法尼亚州的部分使用者而言，还包括由动词派生的 finished 和 done。综合起来得到 S → (AdvP) NP (Aux) (Neg) VP (AdvP)；否定必须借助助动词，因而触发 do 支持。这些规则只是列出可能出现的序列。"}]},"chapter-065-x-bar-theory-introduction":{"title":{"en":"6.14 Trees: Introducing X-bar theory","zh":"6.14 树形图：X 杠理论简介"},"summary":{"en":"X-bar theory restricts the shape of possible trees in order to make stronger predictions about grammar. Every phrase has a head of the same category, every head projects a phrase, and every phrase contains a mid-sized intermediate bar level. The section names the specifier and the complement, presents one-replacement and do so evidence for N-bar and V-bar, and shows that bar levels appear even without complements.","zh":"X 杠理论通过限制可能树结构的形状，对语法作出更强的预测。每个短语都有同范畴的中心语，每个中心语都投射出短语，而每个短语内部都含有一个中等大小的中间杠层级。本节界定了指示语与补足语，用 one 替代和 do so 替代分别论证名词杠与动词杠，并说明即使没有补足语也仍然存在杠层级。"},"points":[{"en":"X-bar theory restricts possible tree shapes and adds an intermediate bar level inside every phrase.","zh":"X 杠理论限制可能的树形，并在每个短语内部增加一个中间的杠层级。"},{"en":"Every phrase XP has a head of the same category X, and every head X projects a phrase XP.","zh":"每个短语 XP 都有同范畴的中心语 X，而每个中心语 X 都投射出短语 XP。"},{"en":"Phrases are not flat: the head forms a closer unit with its complement than with anything else.","zh":"短语并非扁平结构：中心语与其补足语构成的关系比其他成分更紧密。"},{"en":"The specifier is the child of XP and sister of X-bar; the complement is the sibling of the head.","zh":"指示语是 XP 的子女、X 杠的姐妹节点；补足语则是中心语的姐妹节点。"},{"en":"One-replacement replaces a noun with a following PP, leaving material before the noun behind.","zh":"one 替代替换名词及其后的介词短语，而把名词之前的成分留在原位。"},{"en":"Ellipsis and do so replacement show that a verb and its object form a single V-bar constituent.","zh":"省略和 do so 替代表明，动词与其宾语共同构成单一的动词杠成分。"}],"terms":[{"en":"X-bar theory","zh":"X 杠理论","defEn":"A theory restricting possible tree structures, named for the intermediate bar level inside phrases.","defZh":"一种限制可能树结构的理论，因短语内部的中间杠层级而得名。"},{"en":"bar level","zh":"杠层级","defEn":"A mid-sized constituent inside a phrase, lying between the head and the full phrase.","defZh":"短语内部中等大小的成分，位于中心语与完整短语之间，即所谓的部分短语。"},{"en":"specifier","zh":"指示语","defEn":"The child of XP and sister of X-bar, such as a determiner or possessor in an NP.","defZh":"XP 的子女、X 杠的姐妹节点，如名词短语中的限定词或领属成分等成分。"},{"en":"complement","zh":"补足语","defEn":"The sibling of the head, selected by it, such as the object of a verb.","defZh":"中心语的姐妹节点，由中心语选择，如动词的宾语或介词的宾语。"},{"en":"one-replacement","zh":"one 替代","defEn":"A constituency test in which one replaces a noun together with a following PP.","defZh":"一种成分测试，用 one 替换名词及其后的介词短语，用以检验名词杠成分。"},{"en":"do so replacement","zh":"do so 替代","defEn":"A constituency test in which do so replaces a verb together with its object.","defZh":"一种成分测试，用 do so 替换动词及其宾语，用以检验动词杠成分是否成立。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Cats sleep.","noteEn":"Even a two-word sentence consists of an NP followed by a VP.","noteZh":"即使是两个词的句子，也由名词短语加动词短语构成。"},{"text":"The many very fast spaceships carried a lot of valuable cargo.","noteEn":"Despite its length, this sentence also consists of an NP and a VP.","noteZh":"尽管句子很长，它也由名词短语和动词短语构成。"},{"text":"launch of a spaceship","noteEn":"The noun with its PP complement forms an N-bar constituent that one can replace.","noteZh":"名词及其介词短语补足语构成名词杠成分，可由 one 替代。"},{"text":"The spaceships landed.","noteEn":"Every phrase contains a bar level even though no complement is present.","noteZh":"即使没有补足语，每个短语也含有一个杠层级，句子同样如此。"}],"body":[{"en":"Constituency tests and phrase structure rules are a useful starting point, but they do not explain why certain structures are grammatical. X-bar theory makes stronger predictions by restricting the shape of trees and adding an intermediate bar level. A rule like NP → V (Adj) PP is impossible, since a noun phrase must contain a noun. X-bar theory therefore assumes that every phrase XP has a head of the same category X, and every head X projects a phrase of the same category XP.","zh":"成分测试和短语结构规则为思考可能的句子结构提供了有用的起点，但它们并未真正解释某些结构为何合乎语法。X 杠理论通过限制可能树结构的形状来作出更强的预测，并因此在短语内部引入一个额外的结构层次，称为杠层级。像 NP → V (Adj) PP 这样的规则之所以怪异，就在于名词短语中缺少名词。因此 X 杠理论假定：每个短语 XP 都有一个同范畴的中心语 X，而每个中心语 X 都投射出同范畴的短语 XP。"},{"en":"The same constraints are assumed for all categories in all languages, so determiners occur inside DPs and degree words inside DegPs. Phrases are not flat: the head stands in a closer relation to its complement than to anything else, and in English the complement follows the head. Hence every phrase contains a mid-sized intermediate phrase, X-bar, written X′ or X’. The rules are XP → (YP) X’ and X’ → X (ZP), where YP is the specifier and ZP the complement; the head selects its complement.","zh":"人们假定同样的制约适用于所有范畴和所有语言，因此限定词出现在限定词短语（DP）内，程度词出现在程度短语（DegP）内。短语并非扁平结构：中心语与某一成分的关系比与其他任何成分都更紧密，这个成分就是补足语；在英语中补足语位于中心语之后。因此每个短语内部都存在一个中等大小的部分短语，称为 X 杠，原写作 X̄，如今更常写作 X′ 或 X’。其规则为 XP → (YP) X’ 和 X’ → X (ZP)，其中 YP 是指示语，ZP 是补足语，中心语选择自己的补足语。"},{"en":"Evidence for N-bar comes from showing that a noun is closer to a following PP than to a preceding determiner. One-replacement replaces a noun and a following PP while leaving material before the noun behind, as in the contrast between today's one and today's launch of a spaceship. Replacing a determiner and noun instead is impossible. Determiners and possessors are in complementary distribution as the single specifier of NP, which accounts for this pattern.","zh":"名词杠的证据在于表明名词与其后介词短语的关系比与前置限定词的关系更紧密。one 替代可以替换名词及其后的介词短语，而把名词之前的成分留在原位，如 today's one 与 today's launch of a spaceship 的对比。反之，替换限定词加名词则不合语法。限定词与领属成分呈互补分布，因为名词短语只有一个指示语位置，只能容纳其中之一，这正解释了上述格局。"},{"en":"Verb phrases show the same pattern: a verb and its object can be elided together, leaving an adverb behind, but not with the object stranded. Do so replacement makes the same point. Verb and object therefore form a V’ constituent. The bar level is simply a mid-sized constituent, which could equally be called an intermediate phrase. Even without a complement every phrase contains a bar level, as in The spaceships landed, where sentences remain headless.","zh":"动词短语表现出同样的格局：动词与其宾语可以一起被省略，只留下副词，而把宾语孤立留下则不合语法。对许多说话者而言，do so 替代也证明了同一点。可见动词与宾语共同构成 V’ 成分。杠层级只是短语内部中等大小的成分，同样可以称为中间短语。即使没有补足语，每个短语也至少含有一个杠层级，如 The spaceships landed；而句子目前仍没有中心语。"}]},"chapter-066-x-bar-theory-sentences-as-tps":{"title":{"en":"6.15 Trees: Sentences as TPs","zh":"6.15 树形图：句子作为时短语（TP）"},"summary":{"en":"Earlier chapters labelled sentences simply S, but if every phrase must project a head, the sentence also needs one. Auxiliaries cannot be that head, since many sentences have none, so sentences are analysed as tense phrases (TPs) headed by tense. The same X-bar template then captures head-initial English and head-final Japanese.","zh":"此前的章节只把句子标为 S，但若每个短语都必须投射出中心语，句子同样需要一个中心语。助动词不能充当这一中心语，因为许多句子根本没有助动词，因此句子被分析为以时为中心语的时短语（TP）。本节随后用同一套 X 杠模板描写中心语前置的英语与中心语后置的日语。"},"points":[{"en":"Sentences are constituents, hence phrases, so X-bar theory requires them to have a head instead of S.","zh":"句子是句法成分，因而也是短语，所以 X 杠理论要求它有中心语，而不能只标为 S。"},{"en":"The rule S going to NP (Aux) VP left the sentence headless and the auxiliary without a phrase.","zh":"规则 S → NP (Aux) VP 使句子没有中心语，也使助动词没有属于自己的短语。"},{"en":"Auxiliaries are always inflected for tense, and the nonfinite marker to takes their place in nonfinite clauses.","zh":"助动词总是带时的屈折，在非限定小句中则由非限定标记 to 取代其位置。"},{"en":"TP suits X-bar theory because it always has a specifier, the subject, and a complement, the predicate.","zh":"TP 契合 X 杠理论，因为它总带有指示语（主语）和补足语（谓语）。"},{"en":"Category T in English holds modals, be, have, do, the marker to and abstract tense features.","zh":"英语的 T 范畴包含情态助动词、be、have、do、标记 to 以及抽象的时特征。"},{"en":"Head direction varies across languages, but specifiers always precede complements in all known languages.","zh":"中心语方向因语言而异，但在一切已知语言中指示语都先于补足语。"}],"terms":[{"en":"tense phrase (TP)","zh":"时短语（TP）","defEn":"The phrase category assumed for sentences in X-bar theory, headed by tense.","defZh":"X 杠理论中用来表示句子的一类短语，以时（T）为中心语，取代传统的 S。"},{"en":"finiteness","zh":"限定性","defEn":"The property of carrying tense, which independent sentences are said to have.","defZh":"携带时的属性；独立成句的句子总是限定的，即具有时。"},{"en":"head-initial","zh":"中心语前置","defEn":"A word order type in which heads precede their complements, as in English.","defZh":"中心语位于补足语之前的语序类型，如英语中动词先于其宾语。"},{"en":"head-final","zh":"中心语后置","defEn":"A word order type in which heads follow their complements, as in Japanese.","defZh":"中心语位于补足语之后的语序类型，如日语中动词后于其宾语。"},{"en":"Inflection Phrase (InflP/IP)","zh":"屈折短语（Inflection Phrase，InflP/IP）","defEn":"An alternative label for the functional phrase that makes a clause finite.","defZh":"功能短语的另一标签，指使小句获得限定性、并把主语与谓语连起来的投射层。"}],"examples":[{"text":"The robot repaired a spaceship.","noteEn":"A sentence without an auxiliary, whose final tree is a TP carrying abstract past tense.","noteZh":"不含助动词的句子，其最终树形图是带抽象过去时的 TP。"},{"text":"The robot will repair a spaceship.","noteEn":"Here the modal will occupies the head T position of the tense phrase.","noteZh":"此处情态助动词 will 占据时短语的中心语 T 位置。"},{"text":"Tokyo e","noteEn":"A Japanese PP meaning \"to Tokyo\", with the head postposition after its complement.","noteZh":"意为“到东京”的日语介词短语，中心语后置词位于补足语之后。"},{"text":"ringo-o tabe-ta","noteEn":"The Japanese verb follows the object; the sentence also begins with the topic Watasi-wa.","noteZh":"日语动词位于宾语之后，该句还以话题成分 Watasi-wa 开头。"}],"body":[{"en":"Earlier sections applied X-bar theory to many phrase types while sentences were still labelled simply S. But if a phrase is a string of words forming a constituent, sentences are phrases too, and X-bar theory requires every phrase to have a head. The old rule S going to NP (Aux) VP left the sentence without a head and any auxiliary without a phrase of its own.","zh":"此前的各节把 X 杠理论应用于各类短语，而句子仍只被标为 S。然而，如果短语就是构成句法成分的词串，句子也属于短语，而 X 杠理论要求每个短语都有中心语。旧规则 S → NP (Aux) VP 使句子没有中心语，也使助动词没有属于自己的短语。"},{"en":"Tense is chosen as the head because English auxiliaries are always inflected for tense, tense also appears on the main verb when no auxiliary is present, and the marker to takes the auxiliary position in nonfinite clauses. Sentences are therefore tense phrases, since tense represents finiteness and independent sentences are always finite. TP also fits X-bar theory because it always has a specifier, the subject, and a complement, the predicate. Category T covers the modals, be, have, do, to, and abstract features like [+PAST] and [–PAST].","zh":"之所以以时为中心语，是因为英语助动词总是带时的屈折；没有助动词时，时仍体现在主要动词上；在非限定小句中则由标记 to 占据助动词的位置。因此句子是时短语，因为时代表限定性，而独立成句的句子总是限定的。TP 也契合 X 杠理论，因为它总带有指示语（主语）和补足语（谓语）。T 范畴包括情态助动词、be、have、do、to，以及 [+PAST]、[–PAST] 这类抽象特征。"},{"en":"For languages that do not require tense, one option is to deny that sentences such as those of Mandarin or Cantonese are TPs and posit another category; the other, widely assumed in descendants of X-bar theory, is that something abstract still marks finiteness and glues subject and predicate together, sometimes called an Inflection Phrase (InflP or IP). Word order varies too: English is head initial, Japanese strictly SOV and head final, yet specifiers precede complements in every known language.","zh":"对于不需要时的语言，一种选择是否认汉语普通话或粤语的句子是 TP，而设定别的范畴；另一种选择在 X 杠理论的后续理论中被广泛采用：仍有某种抽象成分标示限定性，并把主语与谓语连接起来，它有时称为屈折短语（InflP 或 IP）。语序也存在差异：英语中心语前置，日语为严格 SOV、中心语后置；但在一切已知语言中，指示语都先于补足语。"}]},"chapter-067-x-bar-theory-modifiers-as-adjuncts":{"title":{"en":"6.16 Trees: Modifiers as adjuncts","zh":"6.16 树形图：修饰语作为附加语"},"summary":{"en":"X-bar theory can represent heads with their complements and specifiers, but it initially gave no place to modifiers. Adjuncts supply that place: extra bar levels create structural room for modifying elements. The section shows Adjs and NumPs inside NPs, AdvPs inside VPs and TPs, and modifier PPs elsewhere, and uses the one-replacement test to count bar levels.","zh":"X 杠理论能够表示中心语及其补足语和指示语，最初却没有为修饰语留出位置。附加语补上了这一空缺：增设杠层即可为修饰性成分创造结构空间。本节说明名词短语内的形容词短语与数词短语、动词短语和时短语内的副词短语，以及其他短语中的修饰性介词短语，并用 one 替换测试确定短语所需的杠层数。"},"points":[{"en":"Basic X-bar structure lost the phrase structure rules' ability to show where modifiers fit inside phrases.","zh":"基本的 X 杠结构失去了短语结构规则原有的能力，无法表示修饰语在短语中的位置。"},{"en":"A phrase has one head and one final projection, yet it may in principle contain many partial phrases.","zh":"一个短语只有一个中心语和一个最终投射，但原则上可以包含许多部分短语。"},{"en":"An adjunct is a constituent that is both the child and the sibling of a bar-level node.","zh":"附加语是既作某个杠层节点的女儿、又作其姊妹的句法成分。"},{"en":"Unlike specifiers and complements, adjuncts may appear on either side of the phrase structure.","zh":"与指示语和补足语不同，附加语可以出现在短语结构的任意一侧。"},{"en":"All adverbs and all adjective phrases inside NP are adjuncts, whereas PPs may be complements or adjuncts.","zh":"一切副词以及名词短语内的形容词短语都是附加语，而介词短语可为补足语也可为附加语。"}],"terms":[{"en":"adjunct","zh":"附加语","defEn":"A constituent that is both the child and the sibling of a bar-level node.","defZh":"既作杠层节点的女儿、又作其姊妹的句法成分，用来容纳修饰语。"},{"en":"bar level","zh":"杠层","defEn":"A mid-sized or partial phrase, intermediate between the head and the full phrase.","defZh":"介于中心语与完整短语之间的中间投射，即中等大小的部分短语。"},{"en":"modifier","zh":"修饰语","defEn":"An element such as an adjective or adverb that narrows or describes another element.","defZh":"如形容词、副词等用来限定或描写另一成分的词语，通常出现在附加语位置。"},{"en":"one-replacement","zh":"one 替换（one 替代测试）","defEn":"A constituency test in which one replaces an N-bar constituent.","defZh":"一种成分测试，用 one 替换名词短语中的某个杠层成分，以检验其结构。"},{"en":"do so replacement","zh":"do so 替换","defEn":"A constituency test in which do so replaces a V-bar constituent.","defZh":"一种成分测试，用 do so 替换动词短语中的某个杠层成分。"}],"examples":[{"text":"the early arrival of spring","noteEn":"Its N-bar supplies space for early to attach as an adjunct, since specifier and complement are filled.","noteZh":"指示语与补足语均已占满，其 N 杠为 early 提供了作附加语附着的空间。"},{"text":"a letter from home in the mailbox","noteEn":"Two PPs follow the head noun, each attaching as an adjunct to an N-bar level.","noteZh":"两个介词短语跟在名词中心语之后，各自附加在不同层次的 N 杠上。"},{"text":"I saw a letter from home in the mailbox, and one from the bank on the table.","noteEn":"The one-replacement test shows an N-bar containing letter but neither of the PPs.","noteZh":"one 替换测试表明存在一个包含 letter 但不含任一介词短语的 N 杠。"},{"text":"left the room","noteEn":"In one and the same verb phrase, one adverb precedes it and another follows it.","noteZh":"在同一个动词短语中，一个副词位于其前，另一个副词位于其后。"}],"body":[{"en":"X-bar theory captured the asymmetric relations between heads and their complements, and between heads and their specifiers. In doing so, however, it lost some coverage that phrase structure rules had provided, namely the ability to show how modifiers fit into the phrases they modify, such as adjectives and number phrases in NPs and adverbs in VPs. Adjuncts restore that coverage by expanding the X-bar template.","zh":"X 杠理论能够表示中心语与其补足语以及中心语与其指示语之间的不对称关系。但这样做也丢掉了短语结构规则原有的一部分描写力，无法表示修饰语如何进入它所修饰的短语：名词短语内的形容词短语和数词短语、动词短语与时短语内的副词短语，以及其他短语中的修饰性介词短语。附加语通过扩展 X 杠模板恢复了这种描写力。"},{"en":"The idea behind adjuncts is that a phrase contains only one head and one final projection, whereas a bar level is a mid-sized or partial phrase, and a larger phrase may contain many partial phrases. In the NP the early arrival of spring, the and of spring already occupy the specifier and complement slots, so the adjective phrase early needs a further N-bar level for its structural space. That modifier is an adjunct, a constituent that is both the child and the sibling of a bar-level node, and its position is flexible.","zh":"附加语的基本思想是：一个短语只有一个中心语和一个最终投射，而杠层是中等大小的部分短语，一个更大的短语可以包含许多部分短语。在名词短语 the early arrival of spring 中，the 与 of spring 已分别占据指示语和补足语位置，形容词短语 early 必须依靠增设的 N 杠层级获得结构空间。该修饰语就是附加语，即既作某杠层节点的女儿、又作其姊妹的句法成分，其位置较为灵活。"},{"en":"The same expansion lets two PPs follow a head noun, as in a letter from home in the mailbox. The one-replacement test reveals the structure: letter can be replaced by one with both PPs left behind, or with only the second one left behind, so an N-bar must contain letter but neither PP. Adverbs inside verb phrases act the same way, appearing at the beginning or the end of the VP, and more than one may occur, as in We deliberately left the room slowly.","zh":"同样的扩展使两个介词短语可以跟在名词中心语之后，如 a letter from home in the mailbox。one 替换测试揭示了其结构：letter 可被 one 替换，既可以留下两个介词短语，也可以只留下第二个，因此必然存在一个包含 letter 而不含任何介词短语的 N 杠。动词短语中的副词也是如此：它们可以出现在动词短语的开头或末尾，也可以同时出现多个，如 We deliberately left the room slowly。"},{"en":"All adverbs occur in adjunct positions, as do all adjective phrases inside NP; predicate adjectives, as in The book is long, are instead complements of the copular verb be. Prepositional phrases are less uniform, since they sometimes serve as complements and sometimes as adjuncts, as this section has illustrated. Constituency tests such as replacement with one for N-bar and do so replacement for V-bar are very useful for determining which role a particular PP plays.","zh":"所有副词都出现在附加语位置，名词短语内的所有形容词短语也是如此；而像 The book is long 中作谓语的形容词则是系动词 be 的补足语。介词短语不那么统一，它有时作补足语，有时作附加语，本节对两种情形都有示例。用 one 替换 N 杠、用 do so 替换 V 杠这类成分测试，对于判断某个介词短语究竟充当哪种角色非常有用。"}]},"chapter-068-structural-ambiguity":{"title":{"en":"6.17 Trees: Structural ambiguity in syntax","zh":"6.17 树形图：句法中的结构歧义"},"summary":{"en":"Section 5.9 showed structural ambiguity in morphology, where one string of morphemes may have several structures. Syntax behaves the same way: the sentence I saw someone with a telescope has two interpretations, because the PP may attach as an adjunct either to the verb phrase or to the object noun phrase. Each meaning corresponds to a different tree.","zh":"5.9 节展示了形态学中的结构歧义：同一串语素可以具有多种结构。句法同样如此：句子 I saw someone with a telescope 有两种解释，因为该介词短语既可以作动词短语的附加语，也可以作宾语名词短语的附加语。每个意义都对应一棵不同的树形图。"},"points":[{"en":"A single string of words may have more than one structure, each structure giving a different interpretation.","zh":"同一串词可以拥有不止一种结构，而每种结构产生不同的解释。"},{"en":"In I saw someone with a telescope the PP may modify either the VP or the object NP.","zh":"在 I saw someone with a telescope 中，该短语可修饰动词短语或宾语。"},{"en":"When the PP modifies the VP, the reading is that a telescope was used to see someone.","zh":"当该介词短语修饰动词短语时，意思是用望远镜看到了某人。"},{"en":"When it modifies the object NP, the reading is that the person seen had a telescope.","zh":"当它修饰宾语名词短语时，意思是被看到的那个人持有望远镜。"},{"en":"Each distinct meaning of an ambiguous sentence corresponds to its own potential tree structure.","zh":"歧义句的每一个不同意义都对应一种自己的可能树形结构。"}],"terms":[{"en":"structural ambiguity","zh":"结构歧义","defEn":"The situation in which one string of words has more than one possible structure.","defZh":"同一串词可以对应不止一种结构，并因此产生多种解释的现象。"},{"en":"adjunct of the verb","zh":"动词的附加语","defEn":"A modifier attached within the verb phrase, as with a telescope in the first reading.","defZh":"附着于动词短语内部的修饰语，如第一种解释中的 with a telescope。"},{"en":"object NP","zh":"宾语名词短语","defEn":"The noun phrase functioning as the object, which the PP may modify instead.","defZh":"充当动词宾语的名词短语，介词短语也可以转而修饰它，如 someone。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I saw someone with a telescope.","noteEn":"The ambiguous sentence, whose two readings depend on where the PP attaches.","noteZh":"有歧义的句子，其两种理解取决于介词短语附着的位置。"},{"text":"I was using a telescope, and I saw someone.","noteEn":"The first reading, in which the PP modifies the verb phrase headed by saw.","noteZh":"第一种理解，该介词短语修饰以 saw 为中心语的动词短语。"},{"text":"I saw someone, and that person had a telescope.","noteEn":"The second reading, in which the same PP modifies the object NP someone.","noteZh":"第二种理解，同一介词短语修饰宾语名词短语 someone。"}],"body":[{"en":"Morphology provided cases of structural ambiguity in which one string of morphemes can be assigned more than one structure, each structure matching a different interpretation. Syntax shows the same phenomenon. The familiar example I saw someone with a telescope has two possible readings. One reading is that the speaker was using a telescope and saw someone; the other is that the speaker saw someone and that person had a telescope.","zh":"形态学中就有结构歧义：同一串语素可以获得不止一种结构，而每种结构对应不同的解释。这种歧义并非词汇本身的模糊，而是结构造成的。句法中存在同样的现象。熟知的例子 I saw someone with a telescope 有两种可能的理解：一种是我用望远镜看到了某人，另一种是我看到某人，而那人带着望远镜。"},{"en":"The difference lies in where the prepositional phrase attaches. Under the first interpretation, the PP with a telescope modifies the verb phrase headed by saw, so it is an adjunct of the verb. Under the second, that very PP modifies the noun phrase someone, so it is an adjunct of the object noun phrase. The two trees for the sentence therefore differ in the attachment site of a single modifier.","zh":"差别在于该介词短语所附着的位置。在第一种解释下，介词短语 with a telescope 修饰以 saw 为中心语的动词短语，因而是动词的附加语。在第二种解释下，同一介词短语修饰名词短语 someone，因而是宾语名词短语的附加语。因此该句的两棵树形图只在同一个修饰语的附着位置上不同。"},{"en":"Other instances of structural ambiguity work the same way: each distinct meaning of one string of words will correspond to a different potential tree structure. Many such cases in syntax involve modifiers occupying adjunct positions on one or both interpretations, which is why the adjunct structures introduced earlier are central to analysing ambiguous sentences. Some practical implications of ambiguity, including legal interpretation, are discussed in section 8.3 on semantics and pragmatics in the legal domain.","zh":"其他结构歧义的情形也是如此：同一串词的每一个不同意义，都对应一种不同的可能树形结构，关键在于树形结构本身，而不在于词语的表面顺序。句法中的这类歧义大多涉及在一种或两种解释中处于附加语位置的修饰语，这也是前文介绍的附加语结构对歧义句分析至关重要的原因。歧义在实践中的一些影响，尤其是它所导致的法律解释难题，将在 8.3 节“法律领域中的语义学与语用学”中讨论。"}]},"chapter-069-x-bar-structure-embedded-clauses-as-cps":{"title":{"en":"6.18 Trees: Embedded clauses","zh":"6.18 树形图：嵌入小句"},"summary":{"en":"Complementizers are what allow a clause to be embedded as the complement of a verb, and X-bar principles require the C head to project a CP above the embedded TP. English may leave the declarative C head null, and uses if or whether for embedded Yes-No questions. The features [–Q] and [+Q] sort declarative from interrogative C heads, while nonfinite embedding takes a null C or for with to in T.","zh":"标句词使小句能够嵌入，充当动词的补足语；按 X 杠理论，标句词中心语必须投射出 CP，并以内嵌 TP 为补足语。英语陈述标句词的 C 位置可以没有语音形式，内嵌是非问句则由 if 或 whether 占据 C。特征 [–Q] 与 [+Q] 把 C 中心语分为陈述式与疑问式，非限定内嵌小句的 C 是零形式或 for，T 的中心语是 to。"},"points":[{"en":"Because every head projects a phrase, the complementizer C heads a CP that takes TP as its complement.","zh":"每个中心语都要投射出短语，标句词 C 投射为 CP，以内嵌 TP 为补足语。"},{"en":"In English the declarative C head may be null, so that can be absent while the CP remains.","zh":"英语陈述句的 C 中心语可以为空，that 可以不出现，但 CP 依然存在。"},{"en":"Embedded Yes-No questions place if or whether in C, giving them the same structure as declaratives.","zh":"内嵌是非问句把 if 或 whether 放在 C，结构与内嵌陈述小句相同。"},{"en":"Declarative C heads are [–Q] and interrogative ones are [+Q], and verbs select which types they take.","zh":"陈述标句词带 [–Q] 特征，疑问标句词带 [+Q] 特征，动词选择与哪类 CP 组合。"},{"en":"Nonfinite embedded clauses take a null C or for, with to heading the embedded T.","zh":"非限定内嵌小句以零形式 ∅ 或 for 作标句词，由 to 充当内嵌 T 的中心语。"}],"terms":[{"en":"complementizer","zh":"标句词","defEn":"A functional head that introduces an embedded clause and heads a CP.","defZh":"引导内嵌小句、并投射出 CP 的功能性中心语，英语中如 that、if、whether 以及零形式。"},{"en":"embedded clause","zh":"嵌入小句","defEn":"A clause that appears inside a larger sentence and serves as a verb's complement.","defZh":"位于更大句子内部、充当动词补足语的小句，可以是否定形式，也可以是非限定形式。"},{"en":"complementizer phrase (CP)","zh":"标句词短语（CP）","defEn":"The phrase projected by a complementizer head, which takes TP as its complement.","defZh":"由标句词中心语投射而成的短语，以内嵌的 TP 为补足语，是内嵌小句在树形图中的整体。"},{"en":"Q feature","zh":"Q 特征","defEn":"A feature marking a C head as declarative [–Q] or interrogative [+Q].","defZh":"用来标记 C 中心语性质的特征：陈述式为 [–Q]，疑问式为 [+Q]。"},{"en":"nonfinite clause","zh":"非限定小句","defEn":"An embedded clause whose T is headed by the nonfinite marker to.","defZh":"内嵌小句中 T 以非限定标记 to 为中心语的那一类，其 C 是零形式或 for。"},{"en":"null complementizer","zh":"零标句词","defEn":"A C head with no pronounced form, as in English declarative embedding.","defZh":"没有语音形式的 C 中心语，例如英语陈述内嵌小句中可以省略的 that。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Deniz said that Samnang might leave.","noteEn":"An embedded declarative in which that fills the C head position.","noteZh":"内嵌陈述小句，that 充当 C 中心语，整个 CP 做 said 的补足语。"},{"text":"Deniz said ∅ Samnang might leave.","noteEn":"The same structure with a null C head in English.","noteZh":"结构完全相同，只是英语的 C 中心语没有语音形式，通常记作 ∅。"},{"text":"Eryl wonders whether ghosts exist","noteEn":"An embedded Yes-No question with whether in the C head.","noteZh":"内嵌是非问句，由 whether 充当 C 中心语，属于带 [+Q] 特征的疑问标句词。"},{"text":"I want for ghosts to exist","noteEn":"A nonfinite embedded clause with for as C and to in T.","noteZh":"非限定内嵌小句，for 作 C 中心语，非限定标记 to 作内嵌 T 的中心语。"}],"body":[{"en":"Earlier sections showed that complementizers are what allow a clause to be embedded, that is, to serve as the complement of a verb. Because every head must project a phrase of the same category, the complementizer C projects a CP. Since verbs select whether they take an embedded clause, that CP is the complement of the verb, and the CP in turn takes TP as its own complement. When a clause such as Samnang might leave is embedded under said, the lower TP is placed inside the CP rather than inside the main clause VP, because the C head and its CP would not fit there.","zh":"此前的章节已经说明，标句词使小句得以嵌入，充当动词的补足语。按照 X 杠结构的原则，每个中心语都必须投射出同类短语，因此标句词 C 投射出 CP。动词可以选择是否带内嵌小句，所以这个 CP 是动词的补足语，CP 本身又以 TP 为补足语。Deniz said something 与 Samnang might leave 各对应一棵 TP 树形图；当 Samnang might leave 嵌入 said 之下时，较低的 TP 要放进 CP 内部，不能放进主句 VP，因为 C 中心语及其 CP 在那里没有位置。主句 VP 只包含动词本身，内嵌小句整体作为 CP 与动词处于姐妹关系。"},{"en":"English does not always pronounce the complementizer. In Deniz said ∅ Samnang might leave the CP is still assumed to exist, but its C head is null; this differs from claiming that no CP is present. Embedded Yes-No questions look structurally much like embedded declaratives, except that if or whether occupies the C head, as in Eryl wonders whether ghosts exist. Declarative heads, whether that or null, carry a negative Q feature, while interrogative heads such as if and whether carry a positive Q feature, so verbs select which CP types they combine with.","zh":"英语并不总是把标句词说出来。在 Deniz said ∅ Samnang might leave 中，我们仍假定存在 CP，只是它的 C 中心语为空，这与认为根本没有 CP 不同。内嵌是非问句在结构上与内嵌陈述小句大体一致，区别只在于 if 或 whether 占据 C 中心语，如 Eryl wonders whether ghosts exist。陈述标句词无论 that 还是零形式都带否定 Q 特征，if 与 whether 等疑问标句词带肯定 Q 特征。不同动词因此可以只与陈述 CP 组合、只与疑问 CP 组合、两者皆可或都不行，这正是用特征刻画 C 中心语的原因。"},{"en":"Embedded nonfinite clauses take a null C or for as their complementizer, which can be called a nonfinite complementizer, and their TP is headed by the nonfinite marker to, as in I want for ghosts to exist. The basic structure of clauses is now formalized within X-bar theory. The next step is to express transformations over tree structures, beginning with the concept of syntactic movement.","zh":"非限定内嵌小句的标句词是零形式或 for，可称为非限定标句词，其 TP 以非限定标记 to 为中心语，如 I want for ghosts to exist。这类小句与限定内嵌小句的另一处差别，就在于 T 的中心语不是时标记，而是非限定标记 to。内嵌小句既可取限定形式，也可取非限定形式，但二者都需要 CP 一层。至此小句的基本结构已在 X 杠理论中形式化，下一步是在树形结构上表达转换，首先引入句法移位的概念。"}]},"chapter-070-x-bar-theory-subject-aux-inversion-as-head-movement":{"title":{"en":"6.19 Trees: Movement","zh":"6.19 树形图：移位"},"summary":{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion in English main clause questions is analyzed as Head Movement, in which the auxiliary moves from T up to C, a derivation called T-to-C movement. Content questions additionally require Phrasal Movement, fronting an entire WH-phrase into Spec,CP, a process known as WH-movement. Embedded content questions undergo the same WH-movement without inversion, and languages such as Tlingit allow an overt question complementizer alongside a filled Spec,CP.","zh":"英语主句是非问句中的主谓倒装被分析为中心语移位，也就是助动词由 T 向上移入 C，这种推导称为 T 到 C 移位。内容疑问句还需要短语移位，把整个 WH 短语前置到 CP 的指示语位置，即 WH 移位。内嵌内容疑问句同样进行 WH 移位，但不发生主谓倒装；特林吉特语等语言还允许在 CP 指示语已被占据的同时出现显性疑问标句词，说明英语的限制并非普遍规律。"},"points":[{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion in English main clause questions is the auxiliary moving from T to C.","zh":"英语主句是非问句中的主谓倒装，就是助动词从 T 位置移入 C 位置的移位。"},{"en":"Head Movement moves a head into the next higher head position and is drawn with an arrow.","zh":"中心语移位把中心语移入树形图中上一个更高的中心语位置，书中用箭头标示移动的终点。"},{"en":"A fronted question phrase is not a head but a whole phrase, so it cannot land in C.","zh":"前置的疑问语段不是单个中心语，而是整个短语，因此不能落在 C 这个中心语位置。"},{"en":"Phrasal Movement moves a phrase into a higher specifier, and WH-movement targets Spec,CP.","zh":"短语移位把短语移入更高的指示语位置，WH 移位的着陆点就是 CP 的指示语。"},{"en":"Embedded content questions front the WH-phrase but do not carry out T-to-C movement.","zh":"内嵌内容疑问句把 WH 短语前置，但不进行 T 到 C 移位，因此不出现主谓倒装。"},{"en":"English forbids an overt complementizer with a filled Spec,CP, but Tlingit permits it.","zh":"英语不允许 CP 指示语被占据时再出现显性标句词，特林吉特语却允许二者共存。"}],"terms":[{"en":"Head Movement","zh":"中心语移位","defEn":"Movement of a head into the next higher head position in the tree.","defZh":"把中心语移入树形图中相邻的更高中心语位置的移位，通常用箭头表示。"},{"en":"T-to-C movement","zh":"T 到 C 移位","defEn":"Head movement of the auxiliary from T into C in main clause questions.","defZh":"英语主句疑问句中助动词由 T 移到 C 的中心语移位，用以构成是非问句。"},{"en":"Phrasal Movement","zh":"短语移位","defEn":"Movement of a phrase into a higher specifier position.","defZh":"把整个短语移入更高指示语位置的移位，又称 XP 移位。"},{"en":"WH-movement","zh":"WH 移位","defEn":"Movement of a WH-phrase from its original position into Spec,CP.","defZh":"把 WH 短语从其基础位置移入 CP 指示语位置的短语移位。"},{"en":"trace","zh":"语迹","defEn":"The empty position left behind by a moved element, written as italic t.","defZh":"移位成分在原位留下的空位，通常写作斜体字母 t，本书并未采用。"},{"en":"Spec,CP","zh":"CP 指示语","defEn":"The specifier position of CP, the landing site of WH-movement.","defZh":"CP 的指示语位置，是 WH 短语移位后的着陆点，通常容纳疑问短语。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Have they left?","noteEn":"A main clause Yes-No question derived by T-to-C movement of the auxiliary.","noteZh":"内嵌是非问句，助动词 have 从 T 移到 C，因而出现在主语之前。"},{"text":"What has the squirrel hidden?","noteEn":"A content question combining WH-movement with T-to-C movement of the auxiliary.","noteZh":"内容疑问句，WH 短语移入 CP 指示语，助动词同时移到 C。"},{"text":"I know what squirrels hide","noteEn":"An embedded content question showing WH-movement but no subject-auxiliary inversion.","noteZh":"内嵌内容疑问句有 WH 移位但没有主谓倒装，C 中心语为空。"},{"text":"Daa sá kéet axá?","noteEn":"Tlingit content question with the particle sá after the fronted word.","noteZh":"特林吉特语内容疑问句，疑问词前置后还必须跟上疑问助词 sá，意为“杀人鲸吃什么”。"}],"body":[{"en":"Subject-Auxiliary Inversion, seen earlier, reverses the linear order of subject and auxiliary. Stated over X-bar structure, it is the auxiliary moving up and to the left. Embedded questions place a +Q complementizer if or whether before the subject, the same position an auxiliary occupies in a main clause question, so the auxiliary can be seen as moving from T to C. That is an instance of Head Movement, and the English pattern is named T-to-C movement. This textbook draws a line through the moving head in its base position and an arrow to where it lands; other resources may keep a trace, written as italic t, which this textbook does not use.","zh":"此前见过的主谓倒装改变的是主语与助动词的线性顺序。若用 X 杠结构表述，这就是助动词向左上方移动。内嵌疑问句把 +Q 标句词 if 或 whether 放在紧邻主语之前，而这正是主句疑问句中助动词出现的位置，因此倒装可理解为助动词由 T 移入 C。这属于中心语移位，英语主句疑问句中的这一模式称为 T 到 C 移位。本书在被移走的中心语上划一条横线，再用箭头指向移位终点；其他资料可能在原位留下斜体 t 作语迹，本书不予采用。"},{"en":"Content questions also front a question phrase, as in What has the squirrel hidden, Where is it snowing, and How do squirrels hide nuts. All show inversion, since the auxiliary precedes the subject, but T-to-C movement alone cannot explain the fronted phrase. The auxiliary already occupies C, and no head position can hold two words, so the question phrase must go higher. What moves is not a head but a whole phrase, as the larger NPs in What kind of nuts has the squirrel hidden and Which city is it snowing in show. These land in the empty Spec,CP by Phrasal Movement, or XP Movement; this instance is WH-movement.","zh":"内容疑问句还把疑问语段前置，如 What has the squirrel hidden、Where is it snowing、How do squirrels hide nuts，其助动词都在主语之前，说明发生了倒装。但仅靠 T 到 C 移位无法解释前置的疑问语段：助动词已占据 C，而一个中心语位置容不下两个词。再者，WH 疑问句中移动的不是中心语，而是整个短语，从 What kind of nuts has the squirrel hidden 与 Which city is it snowing in 这类更大的名词短语可以看出。这些短语落在空着的 CP 指示语，属于短语移位，也叫 XP 移位，即 WH 移位。"},{"en":"Embedded content questions such as I know what squirrels hide put the WH-phrase at the front of the CP but do not invert, so their trees lack the T-to-C step and their C position is empty. In many varieties of English an overt complementizer is impossible alongside a fronted phrase, which makes I know what if squirrels hide ungrammatical. That restriction is not universal. Tlingit, a Na-Dené language of Southeast Alaska and adjacent Canada, requires the question word at the left edge followed by the question particle sá, so Spec,CP and an overt +Q head are both filled.","zh":"I know what squirrels hide 这样的内嵌内容疑问句把 WH 短语放在 CP 之前，却不发生倒装，所以树形图缺少 T 到 C 这一步，C 位置是空的。在许多英语变体中，前置短语与显性标句词不能同时出现，因此 I know what if squirrels hide 不合语法。这一限制并非普遍规律。特林吉特语是阿拉斯加东南部及加拿大邻近地区的纳-德内语，其内容疑问句要求疑问词位于最左端，后面跟疑问助词 sá，于是 CP 指示语和显性 +Q 中心语同时被填充。"}]},"chapter-071-x-bar-theory-question-word-fronting-as-phrasal-movement":{"title":{"en":"6.20 Trees: Movement beyond questions","zh":"6.20 树形图：疑问句之外的移位"},"summary":{"en":"Movement is not limited to questions. English auxiliaries like be and have begin lower than T and move there by Head Movement, while in French and earlier English all verbs undergo V-to-T movement. Passives use two types of movement: the passive auxiliary raises from a VP shell to T, and the object NP moves into the empty subject position, a process called NP movement. Languages thus differ both in head ordering and in which movements occur.","zh":"移位并不只出现在疑问句中。英语的 be 和 have 等助动词起点低于 T，通过中心语移位上升到 T；而在法语以及早期英语中，所有动词都进行 V 到 T 移位。被动句同时使用两类移位：被动助动词从 VP 壳层移到 T，宾语 NP 则移入空着的主语位置，即 NP 移位。可见语言不仅在中心语前后位置上存在差异，在出现哪些移位上也各不相同。"},"points":[{"en":"Auxiliaries such as be and have start out below T and move into T by Head Movement.","zh":"be 和 have 这类助动词的起点在 T 之下，通过中心语移位上升到 T 位置。"},{"en":"Only a modal or to truly starts in T; other auxiliaries move there when T is unfilled.","zh":"真正起始于 T 的只有情态动词和非限定 to，其他助动词只在 T 尚未被占据时移入 T。"},{"en":"When a modal fills T, the lower auxiliary stays in an extra VP shell.","zh":"情态动词占据 T 时，较低的助动词留在额外的 VP 壳层中。"},{"en":"In French all verbs show the same distribution, which supports V-to-T movement of main verbs.","zh":"法语中所有动词的分布都相同，这支持主句动词也进行 V 到 T 移位的分析。"},{"en":"Passives combine V-to-T movement of be with NP movement of the object into Spec,TP.","zh":"被动句把 be 的 V 到 T 移位与宾语 NP 移入 TP 指示语这两种移位组合在一起。"}],"terms":[{"en":"V-to-T movement","zh":"V 到 T 移位","defEn":"Head movement in which a verb raises from V into the T position.","defZh":"动词从 V 位置上升到 T 位置的中心语移位，法语中所有动词都进行这种移位。"},{"en":"VP shell","zh":"VP 壳层","defEn":"An extra VP layer hosting a lower auxiliary when T is already filled.","defZh":"当 T 已被情态动词占据时，用来容纳较低助动词的额外 VP 层次。"},{"en":"modal","zh":"情态动词","defEn":"An auxiliary that starts out in T, such as will or might.","defZh":"起始位置就在 T 的一类助动词，如 will、might，通常每句只能出现一个。"},{"en":"NP movement","zh":"NP 移位","defEn":"Movement of an NP into Spec,TP to fill an otherwise empty subject position.","defZh":"把名词短语移入 TP 指示语以填补空主语位置的短语移位。"},{"en":"passive","zh":"被动（句）","defEn":"A clause type in which passive be blocks the subject and the object raises.","defZh":"由被动助词 be 阻止主语在初始位置出现、并使宾语上移的一类句式。"}],"examples":[{"text":"The leaves will be falling.","noteEn":"Future plus progressive, with the modal in T and be in a VP shell.","noteZh":"将来时加进行体，情态动词 will 在 T，助动词 be 留在额外的 VP 壳层中。"},{"text":"Les feuilles tombaient toujours.","noteEn":"A French main verb appearing before toujours meaning always, which indicates V-to-T movement.","noteZh":"法语主句动词出现在 toujours（“总是”）之前，说明主动词也移到了 T。"},{"text":"The ship was sunk (by the pirates).","noteEn":"The passive counterpart of an active sentence with a theme object.","noteZh":"与主动句对应的被动句，受事 the ship 由宾语位置移入主语位置。"},{"text":"The leaves will not have fallen.","noteEn":"Only will precedes negation, showing that have is not in T.","noteZh":"只有 will 出现在否定词之前，说明 have 并没有处在 T 位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"Movement is not confined to questions. English auxiliaries share a distribution different from main verbs: they appear before negation, before adverbs like always, and they undergo Subject-Auxiliary Inversion. But modals and nonfinite to differ from be and have. Modals generally cannot stack, and only the highest auxiliary behaves like T, so in The leaves will have been falling only will precedes negation, always and inversion, while the lower auxiliaries pattern with main verbs in an extra VP layer, or VP shell. The proposal is that only tense features, modals and to start out in T, and other auxiliaries move there only if that position is unfilled. Only be, as auxiliary and copula, and auxiliary have move to T in contemporary English.","zh":"移位不局限于疑问句。英语各助动词的分布与主动词不同：它们出现在否定词之前、always 这类副词之前，并且可以参与主谓倒装。但情态动词和非限定 to 与 be、have 不同。情态动词通常不能叠加，只有最高的助动词才像 T 一样分布，因此在 The leaves will have been falling 中只有 will 位于否定词、always 与倒装之前，较低的助动词与主动词一样位于额外的 VP 壳层。由此提出的假设是：只有时的特征、情态动词和非限定 to 起始于 T，其他助动词仅在 T 未被占据时移入 T。当代英语中只有 be 与作助动词的 have 移入 T。"},{"en":"In French, and in earlier English, all verbs move to T. French auxiliaries resemble English ones, appearing before negation and before adverbs like toujours meaning always. What differs is that French main verbs show the same distribution, as Les feuilles tombaient toujours shows. English main verbs cannot: The leaves fell not, The leaves fell always and Fell the leaves are all ungrammatical, though such orders occurred in Early Modern English around the 1600s. The difference is analyzed by saying that only be and auxiliary have undergo V-to-T movement in English, whereas all verbs do in French.","zh":"在法语和早期英语中，所有动词都移入 T。法语助动词与英语助动词相似：出现在否定词之前，以及 toujours（“总是”）这类副词之前。不同之处在于法语的主句动词分布完全相同，Les feuilles tombaient toujours 就体现了这一点。英语主动词做不到，The leaves fell not、The leaves fell always 和 Fell the leaves 都不合语法，尽管这类语序在约 17 世纪的早期现代英语中允许。因此可这样分析：英语只有 be 和作助动词的 have 进行 V 到 T 移位，而法语所有动词都进行这一移位。"},{"en":"Passives also use both movement types. In a movement-based theory, passive syntax, in particular the presence of passive be, prevents the subject from being introduced at all, leaving an empty subject position, as in the representation of was sunk with the ship still the object. Because English requires a subject in Spec,TP, the object NP the ship must move there, a new instance of phrasal movement called NP movement. Deriving the ship was sunk therefore involves two steps: passive be moves from a VP shell to T, and the object NP moves into Spec,TP.","zh":"被动句同样使用两类移位。在采用移位的理论中，被动句的句法，尤其是被动助词 be 的出现，从一开始就阻止主语被引入，从而留下空的主语位置，如 was sunk 的初始表征中 the ship 仍处于宾语位置。由于英语要求 TP 指示语必须有主语，宾语 NP the ship 必须移入该位置，它是短语移位的新类型，即 NP 移位。因此推导 the ship was sunk 需两步：被动助词 be 从 VP 壳层移入 T，宾语 NP 移入 TP 指示语。"}]},"chapter-072-overview":{"title":{"en":"Trees: Summary","zh":"6.21 树形图：小结"},"summary":{"en":"This chapter's theory of syntax now has two parts: X-Bar Theory and two types of Movement. X-Bar Theory accounts for the overall shape of trees in individual languages, describing which tree shapes a given language allows and which it rules out. Movement is a theory of how an already built tree can be transformed, and together the two explain cross-linguistic word-order variation and relationships among sentence types.","zh":"本章的句法理论现在由两部分组成：X 杠理论与两类移位。X 杠理论解释个别语言中树形结构的整体格局，说明某一语言允许哪些树形结构、排除哪些。移位则是关于已经建成的树形结构如何被转换的理论。两者结合，可以解释跨语言的语序差异以及不同句式之间的关系。"},"points":[{"en":"X-Bar Theory specifies which tree shapes a given language permits and which it forbids.","zh":"X 杠理论规定某一语言允许哪些树形结构、禁止哪些树形结构。"},{"en":"Movement is a theory about transforming a syntactic tree after it has been built.","zh":"移位是关于在句法树建成之后对其进行转换的理论。"},{"en":"Movement offers a further way to describe differences in word order across languages.","zh":"移位提供了描述跨语言语序差异的另一条途径。"},{"en":"Movement links sentence types, relating statements to questions and basic order to topicalized order.","zh":"移位把不同句式联系起来，将陈述句与疑问句、基本语序与话题化语序相关联。"},{"en":"Displaced elements are pronounced in a position different from the one they belong in.","zh":"被移位的成分在发音时出现在与其本应所属位置不同的地方。"}],"terms":[{"en":"X-Bar Theory","zh":"X 杠理论","defEn":"A theory describing the possible and impossible shapes of syntactic trees in a language.","defZh":"描述某一特定语言中可能出现和不可能出现的句法树形状的理论。"},{"en":"movement","zh":"移位","defEn":"A transformation that changes an already built syntactic tree.","defZh":"对已经构建好的句法树进行改变的一种转换操作。"},{"en":"head-initial","zh":"中心语前置","defEn":"A word order in which the head precedes its complement within a phrase.","defZh":"在短语中中心语位于其补足语之前的语序。"},{"en":"head-final","zh":"中心语后置","defEn":"A word order in which the head follows its complement within a phrase.","defZh":"在短语中中心语位于其补足语之后的语序。"},{"en":"topicalization","zh":"话题化","defEn":"Fronting a phrase so that it functions as the topic of the sentence.","defZh":"把某一短语前移，使其充当句子话题的操作。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"The syntactic theory established in this chapter has two components: X-Bar Theory and Movement. X-Bar Theory is responsible for the overall shape of trees within a single language, specifying which tree shapes that language permits and which it rules out. Movement, by contrast, is a theory about transforming a tree after it has already been constructed, and adding it lets the theory explain more than before.","zh":"本章建立的句法理论由两个部分构成：X 杠理论和移位。X 杠理论负责说明个别语言中树形结构的整体格局，即指明该语言允许哪些树形结构，又排除哪些树形结构。与它不同，移位是关于在树形结构已经构建完成之后如何对其加以转换的理论；把移位纳入理论之中，使我们的句法理论获得了更强的解释力。换句话说，X 杠理论管的是树形结构能长成什么样，而移位管的是已经长成的树形结构还能怎样变化。"},{"en":"This extra explanatory power shows up in two areas. First, Movement gives us another way to describe word-order differences across languages: X-Bar Theory already allows head-initial and head-final order, and Movement lets us say that languages transform their basic word order in different ways or in different contexts. Second, Movement provides a way to talk about relationships between sentence types, such as statements and questions, or between a basic order and one in which some phrase has been topicalized or fronted.","zh":"这种解释力的扩展体现在两个方面。第一，移位为描述语言之间的语序差异提供了又一条途径：X 杠理论已经提供了中心语前置与中心语后置这两种语序上的变化，而移位使我们能够说，不同语言是以不同方式、或者在不同语境中转换其基本语序的。第二，移位使我们能够讨论不同句式之间的关系，例如陈述句与疑问句之间的关系，或者句子的基本语序与其中某个短语被话题化或前置之后的语序之间的关系。"},{"en":"By introducing Movement into the theory, we gain a way of talking about the fact that elements are sometimes displaced: they are pronounced in a position different from the one they belong in. With these tools we could investigate relationships between many more types of sentences, both in English and in any other language. Chapter 7 will also show that syntax is relevant to the computation of certain types of linguistic meaning, though not all types.","zh":"把移位引入理论之后，我们便有办法说明这样一个事实：成分有时会发生位移，也就是说，它们的发音位置在某种意义上并不是它们本应所属的位置。借助本章所建立的这些工具，我们可以考察英语以及任何其他语言中更多类型句子之间的关系。第 7 章还将表明，句法与某些类型语言意义的计算有关，但并非与所有类型的意义都有关。"}]},"chapter-073-practice-time-3":{"title":{"en":"Exercise your linguistics skills.","zh":"6.22 练习你的语言学技能。"},"summary":{"en":"This exercise set reviews the whole syntax chapter, from grammaticality judgements to tree drawing. Students invent acceptable, ungrammatical, and semantically odd sentences, classify sentences by structure and type, identify phrase categories and word classes, apply constituency tests, and analyse a constructed Language X. Later items cover complementizers and embedded clauses, Subject-Aux Inversion, content questions, thematic roles, passive versus active voice, structural ambiguity, Japanese word order, and trees for many sentences.","zh":"这套练习复习了整个句法章节，从合乎语法性判断一直到绘制树形图。学生要造出可接受、不合语法以及语义怪异的句子，按结构与类型给句子分类，识别短语类别与词类，运用成分测试，并分析一种人造语言 Language X。后面的题目涉及标句词与嵌入小句、主语—助动词倒装、内容疑问句、题元角色、被动与主动、结构歧义、日语语序，以及为大量句子绘制树形图。"},"points":[{"en":"Grammaticality judgements record what fluent speakers actually do, not what is supposed to be correct.","zh":"合乎语法性判断记录的是流利使用者的实际说法，而不是所谓应该正确的说法。"},{"en":"Classify sentences by structure and type, and identify predicates, subjects, and objects.","zh":"按结构和小句类型给句子分类，并识别谓语、主语与宾语。"},{"en":"Apply constituency tests to decide whether a string of words forms a constituent.","zh":"运用成分测试判断某个词串是否构成一个句法成分。"},{"en":"Identify word classes, auxiliaries, complementizers, and embedded clauses in the given sentences.","zh":"识别所给句子中的词类、助动词、标句词以及嵌入小句。"},{"en":"Apply transformations to build questions and compare passive clauses with their active counterparts.","zh":"运用转换生成疑问句，并比较被动小句与相应的主动小句。"},{"en":"Draw trees for many sentence types, including sentences that are structurally ambiguous.","zh":"为多种句式绘制树形图，包括存在结构歧义的句子。"}],"terms":[{"en":"grammaticality judgement","zh":"合乎语法性判断","defEn":"A speaker's assessment of whether a sentence is well formed in their language.","defZh":"说话人对某一句子在其语言中是否合乎语法的判断。"},{"en":"constituency test","zh":"成分测试","defEn":"A diagnostic used to show that a string of words forms a constituent.","defZh":"用来证明某个词串构成一个句法成分的诊断手段。"},{"en":"Subject-Aux Inversion","zh":"主语—助动词倒装","defEn":"A transformation that places an auxiliary before the subject in questions.","defZh":"在疑问句中把助动词移到主语之前的转换操作。"},{"en":"complementizer","zh":"标句词","defEn":"A word that introduces an embedded clause, such as that or if.","defZh":"引导嵌入小句的词，例如 that 或 if。"},{"en":"content question","zh":"内容疑问句","defEn":"A question that asks about a particular phrase, typically with a wh-word.","defZh":"针对某一特定短语提问的疑问句，通常使用疑问词。"},{"en":"thematic role","zh":"题元角色","defEn":"The semantic relation an NP bears to its predicate, such as agent or goal.","defZh":"名词短语与其谓语之间的语义关系，例如施事或目标。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Tsa akisesho ku ipapu.","noteEn":"A sentence of the constructed Language X, translated as I went to the school.","noteZh":"人造语言 Language X 的例句，英译为「我去了学校」。"},{"text":"Taroo-ga ringo-o tabeta.","noteEn":"Japanese example, translated as Taro ate an apple, used for word-order comparison.","noteZh":"日语例句，英译为「太郎吃了一个苹果」，用于比较语序。"},{"text":"The weather report said that it would be colder.","noteEn":"Used for clause type and predicate analysis, and for drawing a tree with an embedded clause.","noteZh":"用于分析小句类型与谓语，并绘制含嵌入小句的树形图。"},{"text":"One morning I shot an elephant in my pyjamas. How he got in my pyjamas I don’t know.","noteEn":"Groucho Marx's joke, cited to show that one sentence has two structural meanings.","noteZh":"格劳乔·马克斯的笑话，用来说明同一句子具有两种结构意义。"}],"body":[{"en":"The exercises close the chapter by putting its analytical tools to work. The first task asks students to invent sentences in a language they are fluent in: two that are fully acceptable, two that are ungrammatical, and two that are grammatical yet semantically odd. The point is that grammaticality judgements record what fluent speakers actually do, not what someone thinks ought to be correct.","zh":"这些练习让本章的分析工具得到实际运用。第一题要求用自己流利的语言造出句子：两句完全可接受，两句不合语法，两句合乎语法但语义怪异。其用意在于说明，合乎语法性判断记录的是流利使用者的实际说法，而不是某人认为应该正确的说法。"},{"en":"Several items train basic clause analysis. Students decide whether sentences are simple, compound, or complex, and declarative, interrogative, or imperative; they locate the main predicate and say whether it is intransitive, transitive, or ditransitive, and they identify subjects, direct objects, and indirect objects. They also label the category of bolded phrases and work out the basic order of subject, object, and verb in a constructed Language X, deciding whether that language is head-initial or head-final.","zh":"若干题目训练基本的小句分析。学生要判断句子是简单句、复合句还是复杂句，是陈述句、疑问句还是祈使句；找出主要谓语并说明它是不及物、及物还是双及物；还要识别主语、直接宾语和间接宾语。此外还需标出加粗短语的类别，并根据人造语言 Language X 的例句判断其主语、宾语和动词的基本顺序，以及它是中心语前置还是中心语后置。"},{"en":"Other exercises move to constituents, word classes, and embedding. Students apply two constituency tests to bolded strings, pick out nouns, verbs, adjectives, and all closed-class words from published prose, and separate modal auxiliaries, non-modal auxiliaries, and main-verb uses of have and be. For embedded clauses they identify every verb and subject, the main and embedded clauses, the type of the embedded clause, and the complementizer.","zh":"另一些练习转向成分、词类与嵌入结构。学生要对加粗的词串施加两种成分测试，从已公开版权的散文段落中挑出名词、动词、形容词以及所有封闭类词，并把情态助动词、非情态助动词以及 have 和 be 的主要动词用法区分开来。对于嵌入小句，需要指出每个动词和主语、主句与嵌入小句、嵌入小句的类型以及标句词。"},{"en":"The final tasks practise transformations and trees: undoing Subject-Aux Inversion to recover statements, forming content questions for underlined phrases, assigning thematic roles to every NP, judging clauses passive or active, drawing trees for many sentence types, comparing the order of NPs, VPs, and PPs in Japanese with English, and drawing the two trees behind the ambiguous elephant sentence.","zh":"最后一批任务练习转换与树形图：撤销主语—助动词倒装以还原陈述句，为加下划线的短语构造内容疑问句，为每个名词短语标注题元角色，判断小句是被动还是主动，为多种句式绘制树形图，比较日语与英语在名词短语、动词短语和介词短语上的语序，并画出大象那句歧义句两种含义各自对应的树形图。"}]}});
